		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-0069375b-1075-4120-8dd6-79925238b4f2">
		<rdfs:label>article-0069375b-1075-4120-8dd6-79925238b4f2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The new policy lays out some exceptions and had been expected since last month, when President Biden vowed not to let the department seize reporters’ phone and email records.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd522e1c-57a0-49bc-9835-fae39d9d58a6"/>
