		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-0069d746-310b-4178-afde-20ebe8f0348e">
		<rdfs:label>article-0069d746-310b-4178-afde-20ebe8f0348e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>U.S. officials reported more than 59,880 cases on Thursday. Bolivia’s leader became Latin America’s third to be infected. The Malaysian police questioned Al Jazeera journalists over a documentary about the country’s lockdown.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-006aacc6-1833-4c62-ae8a-611f31feed10">
		<rdfs:label>article-006aacc6-1833-4c62-ae8a-611f31feed10</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The endorsement was another example of the strong backing Joseph R. Biden Jr. enjoys from African-American leaders and voters.</rdfs:comment>
