	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-00718f2e-bd48-4338-82da-fe116fd2e7e9">
		<rdfs:label>article-00718f2e-bd48-4338-82da-fe116fd2e7e9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Biden administration has quietly approached congressional Democrats about a potential change to their high-profile but long-shot effort to transform most of the District of Columbia into the nation’s 51st state, according to executive and legislative branch officials.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-00729989-8230-42fc-9fe2-3bc902960f87">
		<rdfs:label>article-00729989-8230-42fc-9fe2-3bc902960f87</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Blame is a hallmark of American politics. Ronald Reagan couldn’t escape it in his first midterm elections 40 years ago. Can Biden?</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e9c4025-7dbe-4808-a3d4-b9d25fa14354"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-89135d87-ed63-4619-a5ce-c3f23d9e6fd4"/>
