	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-01ab0e8f-2c43-4edd-9eec-26d0da77b120">
		<rdfs:label>article-01ab0e8f-2c43-4edd-9eec-26d0da77b120</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Two primary lawyers will be arguing before the Supreme Court on Monday in the case on race-conscious admissions programs at the University of North Carolina, a challenge that will test the future of affirmative action in college admissions. They represent vastly divergent political backgrounds, but they have appeared before the court before.</rdfs:comment>
