	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-026f00b7-61c5-4006-8201-c96328702f78">
		<rdfs:label>article-026f00b7-61c5-4006-8201-c96328702f78</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Many younger voters are not old enough to remember a Democratic presidential primary that ended so quickly and congenially. Could it help Joe Biden in the fall?</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-027aa8c1-586d-440a-a525-f7aff0cf6296">
		<rdfs:label>article-027aa8c1-586d-440a-a525-f7aff0cf6296</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Food and Drug Administration would first need to decide that third doses are safe and effective for Pfizer-BioNTech and Moderna, the two vaccines that were rolled out first and have been most used.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3263b980-a580-440f-bdd2-6d7fa7bb3fab"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-17"/>
