	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-0477263c-93e2-49c3-8898-7e8dbf8ba5d6">
		<rdfs:label>article-0477263c-93e2-49c3-8898-7e8dbf8ba5d6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump came to the debate ready with his regular wrap on race when asked to explain his description of “Black Lives Matter” as a symbol of hate: He claimed he had done more than any president since Abraham Lincoln for African-Americans, and he called himself the “least racist person in this room.” (Never mind that the moderator of the debate, Kristen Welker, is a Black woman.)</rdfs:comment>
