	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-06891d07-0d8b-44a3-93da-c120f1cbbeba">
		<rdfs:label>article-06891d07-0d8b-44a3-93da-c120f1cbbeba</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Americans living outside the United States have been making plans to vote in the general election since the summer. But amid the coronavirus pandemic and global mail disruptions, their ballots still may not arrive in time to be counted on Nov. 3. And recent Supreme Court decisions mean that late arrivals in some states will not be counted at all.</rdfs:comment>
