		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-06bdd778-f244-4077-8b14-88ab7d98b93c">
		<rdfs:label>article-06bdd778-f244-4077-8b14-88ab7d98b93c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The prolonged uncertainty in spite of the clear preference of the public has intensified some Americans’ anger at a system in which a minority of people can claim a majority of power.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-06be1986-76a2-4e3e-b244-93f61fc6e7bc">
		<rdfs:label>article-06be1986-76a2-4e3e-b244-93f61fc6e7bc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As the pandemic wreaks havoc on public transit systems across the country, experts say it is low-income residents, people of color and essential workers bearing the brunt.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-83d40723-6a13-432d-8617-d546a58e6733"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-15"/>
