	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-07ddbe80-bf6a-4e70-be10-a2cea1d909a2">
		<rdfs:label>article-07ddbe80-bf6a-4e70-be10-a2cea1d909a2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The fourth and final night of the Democratic National Convention will air tonight from 9 p.m. to 11 p.m. Eastern time. Julia Louis-Dreyfus is the M.C. There are several ways to watch:</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-07dfc319-fd0d-4ffd-81a2-6e3a1d57c797">
		<rdfs:label>article-07dfc319-fd0d-4ffd-81a2-6e3a1d57c797</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Many protesters have volunteered to clean up after looting and vandalism, in the hope that the movement will not be defined by destruction.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-91caa243-6ff4-4c6d-affc-51bd8da8617d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-07e145f4-a1c3-4598-b5e1-9bbfb2c61dd7">
		<rdfs:label>article-07e145f4-a1c3-4598-b5e1-9bbfb2c61dd7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Around the country, local elections suggested that voters were rejecting the most sweeping calls to reinvent law enforcement.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9a5389b6-c0ea-4275-8951-1523cfe86f87"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-de093669-b27a-4345-ac65-683caba65a27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-07e186b9-b3aa-4c31-b9fa-e76fc56fbbf5">
		<rdfs:label>article-07e186b9-b3aa-4c31-b9fa-e76fc56fbbf5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>It was the second time in six weeks that Texas Democrats have staged a walkout to try to prevent passage of a sweeping election overhaul bill.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-011ddbd5-8a1e-4932-8bfc-bad05d0ca67f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-07e4e3ce-2895-4349-97f7-57a5a34678df">
		<rdfs:label>article-07e4e3ce-2895-4349-97f7-57a5a34678df</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After several near misses, Democrats can taste victory in Georgia — and Republicans fear President Trump’s lackluster numbers may drag down the party’s Senate candidates with him.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-887d1269-7020-4c8e-8dfc-eae7c464f3cb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-07eb5b27-e0bb-4166-b72e-6d81a2a1f48d">
		<rdfs:label>article-07eb5b27-e0bb-4166-b72e-6d81a2a1f48d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Voters in Nevada and South Carolina face an all-white top tier of 2020 candidates that was winnowed down by a largely white electorate.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-21d856ad-a6ae-406e-a9e4-9707218ad815"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9c6cc67a-b3c2-45c5-af7a-92a423ab1249"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-07ec1ed5-fabd-43e8-a450-233db8f781c1">
		<rdfs:label>article-07ec1ed5-fabd-43e8-a450-233db8f781c1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The U.S. State Department on Wednesday confirmed the death of a man believed to be the second American killed fighting in Ukraine.</rdfs:comment>
