		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-09ec40da-ed95-4547-a1f0-f05094d9a44d">
		<rdfs:label>article-09ec40da-ed95-4547-a1f0-f05094d9a44d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mr. Hall invoked his Fifth Amendment right against self-incrimination. He was with Mr. Floyd moments before police officers pulled him out of a car and later pinned him to the ground for more than nine minutes.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-edd059c5-3ec4-4bec-b45e-ca6834a9e51c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-09f26cfe-5629-458c-8dce-0f6dbdf9d9aa">
		<rdfs:label>article-09f26cfe-5629-458c-8dce-0f6dbdf9d9aa</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump is likely to win again in rural northern Michigan, a key to his surprise victory in the state in 2016. But can he pile up the same margin in 2020? Some have their doubts.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-44926325-5c4f-4e18-89e5-b1470d62842c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-09f949df-0849-4133-a4e2-790daeded4c2">
		<rdfs:label>article-09f949df-0849-4133-a4e2-790daeded4c2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats hope to portray Republican Senate candidates in some of the most competitive midterm races as too far outside the mainstream. For now, it seems to be working.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e9c4025-7dbe-4808-a3d4-b9d25fa14354"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-09fec397-85ab-4008-b385-768e62e01d0e">
		<rdfs:label>article-09fec397-85ab-4008-b385-768e62e01d0e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After a scare in November, New Jersey’s governor and other Democratic leaders held back-channel talks over lifting mandates and helping voters impatient with restrictions reclaim a sense of normalcy.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
