	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-0d8ee361-a814-4d7f-87a0-586369936c1f">
		<rdfs:label>article-0d8ee361-a814-4d7f-87a0-586369936c1f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In state after state, voters say they support liberal policies like single-payer health care, canceling student debt and the Green New Deal. But many are voting for Joe Biden, who has proposed largely moderate ideas.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4504805-5b5f-41c7-b157-41ff04a342ad"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-0d911d5f-f93c-4835-b2c8-03594ebce7a9">
		<rdfs:label>article-0d911d5f-f93c-4835-b2c8-03594ebce7a9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Senators Tammy Duckworth and Mazie Hirono had said they would support only “diversity candidates” until President Biden addressed the dearth of Asian-Americans and Pacific Islanders in his administration.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-0d929497-5641-41fb-927d-a4cfc4e15112">
		<rdfs:label>article-0d929497-5641-41fb-927d-a4cfc4e15112</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Even some anti-abortion adherents say Texas is failing families left impoverished by its war against abortion.</rdfs:comment>
