	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-0d9813ab-ce7d-43fd-9159-a77a943f0200">
		<rdfs:label>article-0d9813ab-ce7d-43fd-9159-a77a943f0200</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As the Senate majority leader on Sept. 11, 2001, Tom Daschle was among those hurriedly evacuated in the chaos of an expected attack on the Capitol, only to return later that evening for a bipartisan show of unity and resolve on the marble steps many had used to flee just hours earlier.</rdfs:comment>
