		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-0f12e103-631a-4553-a067-97cb35c4dc60">
		<rdfs:label>article-0f12e103-631a-4553-a067-97cb35c4dc60</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In his first newspaper interview since a public uprising forced him to step down in 2019, Ricardo A. Rosselló laments “the complete devastation of my reputation.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c27717ae-a4a7-43e2-a892-7d5659d97cf6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-0f12ebbe-2ecf-4fd8-8b0e-614da9e9c744">
		<rdfs:label>article-0f12ebbe-2ecf-4fd8-8b0e-614da9e9c744</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Ms. Trump herself has not followed the federal guidelines advising against discretionary travel, leaving Washington for another one of her family’s homes.</rdfs:comment>
