	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-0f1d866f-e334-4e43-ac09-c1306fe27693">
		<rdfs:label>article-0f1d866f-e334-4e43-ac09-c1306fe27693</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A Molotov cocktail was used against Wisconsin Family Action in Madison and did not ignite, but another fire was set, the police said.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a40b1cb-c11d-4122-ae5a-754463517860"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6289394d-f421-490d-8db3-a69be34cd200"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-0f1f584e-c1d0-48f3-b495-b040b40fe7c4">
		<rdfs:label>article-0f1f584e-c1d0-48f3-b495-b040b40fe7c4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Dick Cheney always saw doomsday threats from America’s enemies. His daughter is in a lonely battle against what both see as a danger to American democracy: Donald J. Trump.</rdfs:comment>
