	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-10dee63f-33cc-4212-8725-a25663c8b0aa">
		<rdfs:label>article-10dee63f-33cc-4212-8725-a25663c8b0aa</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Investigators focused on a sale of at least $1 million of stock in Cardlytics, a financial firm whose board the senator once sat on. They closed the case this summer without charges.</rdfs:comment>
