		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1199e33f-1359-4400-a7c0-669018cd7df1">
		<rdfs:label>article-1199e33f-1359-4400-a7c0-669018cd7df1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A group of President Trump’s most strident allies in the House is calling on Representative Liz Cheney of Wyoming, the No. 3 Republican, to resign from her leadership post after she voted to impeach Mr. Trump, dramatizing the bitter rifts within the party and setting up a messy internal feud that could define its future.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-119e8d60-0a7b-4f61-acd2-fbaf60a947c7">
		<rdfs:label>article-119e8d60-0a7b-4f61-acd2-fbaf60a947c7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A rumor floated by internet conservatives about the use of felt-tip markers by Arizona polling stations isn’t true, officials say.</rdfs:comment>
