	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-11ac67c5-25b8-47f0-9c3b-969b1be5dde0">
		<rdfs:label>article-11ac67c5-25b8-47f0-9c3b-969b1be5dde0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Four years ago, President Trump accepted the Republican presidential nomination in Cleveland over persistent opposition within his own party. There was a hopeless, last-minute effort to battle his nomination on the convention floor. There was Senator Ted Cruz’s admonition to voters to “vote your conscience,” in lieu of a call for party unity. There was Gov. John Kasich — the chief executive of the host state — declining to attend.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3488268a-8b17-411a-8185-6859abbab9a8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-11ae852a-de90-4a7b-9fd9-c639133cca0e">
		<rdfs:label>article-11ae852a-de90-4a7b-9fd9-c639133cca0e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The program, Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals, protects people brought to the United States as children by shielding them from deportation and letting them work.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-947ed571-ad87-49fb-b59a-9372d166d3c7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-11b09cde-6115-460f-9ed2-706c1ab8a23f">
		<rdfs:label>article-11b09cde-6115-460f-9ed2-706c1ab8a23f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Energy infrastructure has increasingly come under assault, and analysts said the attack that cut off fuel supplies this week should be a “wake-up call.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d8148593-227b-4889-ae70-592b440737ae"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-11bd7c85-4891-4085-9aee-306666b85469">
		<rdfs:label>article-11bd7c85-4891-4085-9aee-306666b85469</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>California ranks as the second-most diverse state in the nation as its white population shrinks. Plus, San Francisco is the country’s most childless big city.</rdfs:comment>
