	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1b44de18-81d1-4828-91a4-5845cf48a0e2">
		<rdfs:label>article-1b44de18-81d1-4828-91a4-5845cf48a0e2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Gina McCarthy worked six or seven days a week, 12 to 14 hours a day, to produce America’s first real effort to combat climate change, a suite of Obama-era regulations that would cut pollution from the nation’s tailpipes and smokestacks and wean the world’s largest economy from fossil fuels.</rdfs:comment>
