		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1ce364ff-66de-40fe-95f9-d58100ba859c">
		<rdfs:label>article-1ce364ff-66de-40fe-95f9-d58100ba859c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mr. Ryan, who mounted a long-shot campaign for president in 2019, plans to compete for the state’s open Senate seat. His campaign will test Democrats’ strength in a state tilting to the right.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1ce3d97d-7851-4e86-9fd0-872731a3dcea">
		<rdfs:label>article-1ce3d97d-7851-4e86-9fd0-872731a3dcea</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Native American tribes are competing for the first federal grants designed to help move communities away from high water and other dangers posed by climate change.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-1688cc77-a368-49e6-8ab4-200858492d4b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-74659e03-2c48-4140-91f4-08e5d544f77a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1ce53fa3-7ef5-4475-b12d-cd3b2ed89e17">
		<rdfs:label>article-1ce53fa3-7ef5-4475-b12d-cd3b2ed89e17</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With pressure mounting to get Covid-19 vaccine doses into arms as quickly as possible, many overburdened city health departments across the country have turned to partnerships with hospitals, nonprofit organizations and pharmacies. In Philadelphia this week, one such deal went awry after the city leaned on a start-up led by college students who were eager to get involved but had little experience.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-edd059c5-3ec4-4bec-b45e-ca6834a9e51c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f08506e1-4ec6-45c9-9d85-46fe67848dee"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1cea466d-2faa-43d9-9df2-27fc2a2992d0">
		<rdfs:label>article-1cea466d-2faa-43d9-9df2-27fc2a2992d0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Trump campaign has intensified its efforts to stop vote counting and to question the validity of ballots, with nearly a dozen lawsuits in Nevada, Pennsylvania, Michigan and Georgia.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-90788841-2a13-4598-abd3-3b677caff4d4"/>
