	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1cfd647f-ff50-4ce2-9033-873b4d8f254e">
		<rdfs:label>article-1cfd647f-ff50-4ce2-9033-873b4d8f254e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>MIAMI — Even before the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention recommended this week that vaccinated Americans in coronavirus hot spots around the country go back to wearing face coverings indoors, a resistance had been building against any new masking requirements, no matter the resurgence of infections.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1d061b86-c376-4401-b625-e6877f56c224">
		<rdfs:label>article-1d061b86-c376-4401-b625-e6877f56c224</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The former president, who is expected to announce a third presidential bid shortly after the midterms, opened a swing of four rallies in Iowa.</rdfs:comment>
