	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1d447146-4a16-4855-9b94-ab8193da681e">
		<rdfs:label>article-1d447146-4a16-4855-9b94-ab8193da681e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>If you follow @POTUS, @WhiteHouse or the other official presidential handles on Twitter, you’ll have to re-follow them on Jan. 20 when President-elect Joseph R. Biden Jr. takes office.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a729ee81-a348-4bc3-99ad-2b76a637c418"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1d4e8c96-35fd-4a1d-bc8c-905730d57f87">
		<rdfs:label>article-1d4e8c96-35fd-4a1d-bc8c-905730d57f87</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats prepared a spending bill to keep the government funded past a Thursday deadline, but moderates dug in harder against their ambitious social safety net bill.</rdfs:comment>
