		<rdfs:label>article-1d573c06-193e-4e95-bc3e-7113df99b684</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president’s picks for the department’s No. 2 and 3 spots pledged to restore independence to law enforcement.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd522e1c-57a0-49bc-9835-fae39d9d58a6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1d5760f7-17bb-4d51-824b-7b67b1fd9d06">
		<rdfs:label>article-1d5760f7-17bb-4d51-824b-7b67b1fd9d06</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Disregarding the advice of his own health experts, President Trump also attacked the C.D.C.’s reopening guidelines as onerous and expensive.</rdfs:comment>
