	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1e191dac-dc93-4107-abf4-25c4f1ff6902">
		<rdfs:label>article-1e191dac-dc93-4107-abf4-25c4f1ff6902</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Just over a week after President Trump tested positive for the coronavirus, he is about to start holding rallies again.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1e1c1958-ae97-46de-97b0-5915c3441f4b">
		<rdfs:label>article-1e1c1958-ae97-46de-97b0-5915c3441f4b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Donald Trump’s tax returns illustrate the profound inequities of the tax code and the shambolic state of federal enforcement.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1e1c30d0-5d26-4e68-b3d9-aae60cdc50c0">
		<rdfs:label>article-1e1c30d0-5d26-4e68-b3d9-aae60cdc50c0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Research by the Brookings Institution found evidence that a new payment card helped offset the loss of subsidized meals when schools closed because of the pandemic.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9e94ebbb-365e-41ef-9a76-b300ca95c3d1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1e27dc84-e208-4648-aa80-b41f38a4e04b">
		<rdfs:label>article-1e27dc84-e208-4648-aa80-b41f38a4e04b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Colorado once looked like it had gotten a grip on the coronavirus. Gov. Jared Polis, a Democrat, is a zealous mask wearer who imposed a statewide mandate. Hospitalization levels stayed low for much of the summer and fall. The state even began dismantling two emergency field hospitals it set up early in the pandemic.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b0d8acac-ba33-4091-b922-0eb5b9ab904d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1e285a88-6f98-4ed8-baed-c52f070f5f24">
		<rdfs:label>article-1e285a88-6f98-4ed8-baed-c52f070f5f24</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In a letter Friday night, Senator Mitch McConnell, the majority leader, urged his Republican colleagues “to be cautious and keep your powder dry until we return to Washington.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1e2a8fd3-c9ab-46a0-8bce-9c967049054f">
		<rdfs:label>article-1e2a8fd3-c9ab-46a0-8bce-9c967049054f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After saying he would phase out the group, the president now says he will keep it. But he has regularly ignored the information and guidance it has provided.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1e2cb6e2-c258-49f8-910a-e2fcbe5ecd9e">
		<rdfs:label>article-1e2cb6e2-c258-49f8-910a-e2fcbe5ecd9e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Surprise victories in the Midwest catapulted President Trump to victory four years ago, and the region again looms as the critical battleground. Both candidates are focusing on it in the final days.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7da4dfa6-58ba-4b1b-8d80-6c39df820022"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c67a9047-7b94-4e45-aaa9-c820c2b967de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
