	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f1acdba-fdb7-4130-807f-d9d6d2ee6238">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f1acdba-fdb7-4130-807f-d9d6d2ee6238</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>City officials said 164 residents at the privately run shelter, Dallas Life, were taken by bus to a hotel. They will be isolated in individual rooms for two weeks while the shelter is cleaned.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6bc8c5a9-d09c-4f66-9308-4f0bbc37ff83"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f1d2ab7-4297-4d9c-a9f5-5fa9e5d5a36c">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f1d2ab7-4297-4d9c-a9f5-5fa9e5d5a36c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mr. Biden, speaking to black supporters about the need to improve the country, accused President Trump of dividing the nation and pledged to unite it.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f1df02d-4942-40a9-a66c-b0e7d1dfa506">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f1df02d-4942-40a9-a66c-b0e7d1dfa506</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden attended the groundbreaking for an Intel computer chip factory in a heavily Republican part of Ohio, an effort to focus voter attention on parts of the economy that are improving.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f204e7c-0fbe-4779-8d3d-9d6b23dbe37a">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f204e7c-0fbe-4779-8d3d-9d6b23dbe37a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Here are the daily schedules of the presidential and vice-presidential candidates for Friday, Sept. 25. All times are Eastern time.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f213e04-2b6a-4d6c-8465-e2fb53f8d03c">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f213e04-2b6a-4d6c-8465-e2fb53f8d03c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>We spent a lot of time covering the candidates’ ups and downs in Iowa. Almost none of it mattered.</rdfs:comment>
