		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f342a57-5a21-458e-a730-34b0b6e2a4bd">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f342a57-5a21-458e-a730-34b0b6e2a4bd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The $180 million Senate contest, a political scientist said, “was like being a local in Woodstock in 1969: When it first started, it was exciting and fun, but by the end, it was muddy and dirty.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-91caa243-6ff4-4c6d-affc-51bd8da8617d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f37063c-5ad3-4183-bbae-3cd048cdada5">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f37063c-5ad3-4183-bbae-3cd048cdada5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democratic leaders are pressing the president-elect to cancel $50,000 in debt per student borrower by fast executive action, but he wants Congress to pass more modest relief.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-20357c46-ce72-4f6a-af65-5f9df4eb0032"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b782e9c4-4c0a-4c6c-aa6e-ee0fb7623560"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f37ef83-9828-4d4f-ab6d-38866bf92cc7">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f37ef83-9828-4d4f-ab6d-38866bf92cc7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>She is suddenly on Joe Biden’s shortlist. Can Michigan afford to lose her?</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-44926325-5c4f-4e18-89e5-b1470d62842c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f3976d9-5094-4264-ad41-53697112dfd5">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f3976d9-5094-4264-ad41-53697112dfd5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Virginia’s move to end the death penalty was a welcome step. The administration can do more.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f39ad85-00aa-426f-a3b7-721eb00a3167">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f39ad85-00aa-426f-a3b7-721eb00a3167</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Millions of Americans lost crucial unemployment coverage as President Trump continued to criticize the bill that would keep pandemic aid from lapsing.</rdfs:comment>
