		<rdfs:label>article-1f5fc574-b774-4627-b101-17326ed43053</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>For all its size and economic might, California has long had one of America’s lowest number of hospital beds relative to its population. Now state officials warn that this shortfall, combined with acute staffing shortages, may prove catastrophic.</rdfs:comment>
