	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f89c06c-fdcb-4869-bde3-c592ae5b6889">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f89c06c-fdcb-4869-bde3-c592ae5b6889</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With the central question of the case being exactly how Mr. Floyd died, and what role Mr. Chauvin’s actions played, the state indicated it would cast a much wider net than just relying on the autopsy report of the county medical examiner by bringing in a number of medical experts.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9a5389b6-c0ea-4275-8951-1523cfe86f87"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e2a444d6-76b3-4fc5-9655-0178ae16f402"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f8c47b1-881f-4d1c-bdcb-b17ec5e51242">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f8c47b1-881f-4d1c-bdcb-b17ec5e51242</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Separately, defense lawyers asked a judge to block the Trump-era special counsel from making the Steele dossier a focus of next month’s trial.</rdfs:comment>
