		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f90b6d3-a338-4989-b507-b4b679253c76">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f90b6d3-a338-4989-b507-b4b679253c76</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Keeping the top commander in the country longer is part of an effort to reassure Afghans as the Taliban step up their offensive.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5a3094b1-6bc7-47d7-8f53-c56fd8ed0c59"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1f91abea-3c92-49ca-85b8-917af4c3b0df">
		<rdfs:label>article-1f91abea-3c92-49ca-85b8-917af4c3b0df</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>But the justices allowed a vaccination requirement for health care workers at facilities that receive federal money.</rdfs:comment>
