	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-1fa76352-7714-47a6-a67e-e57adec23fae">
		<rdfs:label>article-1fa76352-7714-47a6-a67e-e57adec23fae</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president’s first rally since the coronavirus shuttered most of the country will take place on Juneteenth, which commemorates the end of slavery, in the city where one of the worst racist massacres in American history took place.</rdfs:comment>
