	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-211a2bd8-2a30-4cd1-8e26-e381bbff7825">
		<rdfs:label>article-211a2bd8-2a30-4cd1-8e26-e381bbff7825</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president fired the official who previously held the job and had played a key role in telling lawmakers about the whistle-blower complaint that prompted impeachment proceedings.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6f60db0f-4977-4567-b7bd-9abe5d4a35e8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-211d99ee-db28-4fc2-a688-497ed7267991">
		<rdfs:label>article-211d99ee-db28-4fc2-a688-497ed7267991</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>For all the oddities endemic to a mid-virus presidential campaign, the pair’s maiden gathering reflected a scene that seemed entirely plausible, even predictable, a year ago.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f33dc887-a9a6-4b4f-adce-fc81b6f27a0c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-211f526d-f1c2-4430-9fb4-cadf353d6924">
		<rdfs:label>article-211f526d-f1c2-4430-9fb4-cadf353d6924</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden’s address unfolded in a Capitol still grappling with a pandemic and the aftermath of a deadly riot, and now facing a war in Ukraine.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2124ad83-12d9-4ee1-a3ac-fdfcd86e91f8">
		<rdfs:label>article-2124ad83-12d9-4ee1-a3ac-fdfcd86e91f8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With impeachment behind them and an eye on November, Democrats appear to have decided that focusing on President Trump’s norm-shattering words and deeds only elevates him.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-212bd62e-9a37-408f-9413-0e2322849b64">
		<rdfs:label>article-212bd62e-9a37-408f-9413-0e2322849b64</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump’s public comments this week, perhaps fueled by anger over reports of his disrespect for those who died in America’s wars, take his attack on the military to a new level.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-46b2f3e2-fc43-4d1f-8134-a17365f8ec33"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5a3094b1-6bc7-47d7-8f53-c56fd8ed0c59"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-212dccce-247f-4acd-bdc8-5c62ce8b9bed">
		<rdfs:label>article-212dccce-247f-4acd-bdc8-5c62ce8b9bed</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As power began to flicker back on across much of Texas, millions across the state confronted another dire crisis: a shortage of drinkable water as pipes cracked, wells froze and water treatment plants were knocked offline.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3d036c4f-8ad0-458c-98fa-b15acd415658"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b0d8acac-ba33-4091-b922-0eb5b9ab904d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d7a0b17f-e0aa-44c5-a995-e81e028fa879"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-213ab9a0-6c5d-4c70-8f08-e318dee2a12b">
		<rdfs:label>article-213ab9a0-6c5d-4c70-8f08-e318dee2a12b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A missed deadline for flights to look for polar bears means the work to locate oil reserves in the Arctic National Wildlife Refuge is effectively killed.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e17310c8-39f3-4c91-8224-a91b0b94e409"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-213b0a5d-3e76-44a8-ba9a-0e51b10a1608">
		<rdfs:label>article-213b0a5d-3e76-44a8-ba9a-0e51b10a1608</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>More than three weeks after investigators obtained a warrant for the phone, the authorities in New Mexico and New York are working on coordinating the request.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-683ee0b4-5d4e-4695-b1d5-c0fdfd233bfa"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e826c370-9468-4832-be86-489a8da40f63"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2148f209-48b7-4db8-8460-f6f7bdc68cea">
		<rdfs:label>article-2148f209-48b7-4db8-8460-f6f7bdc68cea</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats still control the seven-seat court, which has been thrust into legal battles over coronavirus orders and gerrymandering.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4bd1aa5-c807-421e-b8ae-1b3824d70300"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-214b897b-9532-407b-b866-33c23cd47c4e">
		<rdfs:label>article-214b897b-9532-407b-b866-33c23cd47c4e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The White House has pushed for a $22.5 billion package at home and abroad, warning about the dire consequences of inaction. But a smaller package of $10 billion has been stalled in the Senate.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-214d436f-a2d6-4dff-8094-206f1657bebf">
		<rdfs:label>article-214d436f-a2d6-4dff-8094-206f1657bebf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>So far, the president has offered something for both hawks and isolationists. Will that last?</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-214e1fb6-bfdd-4059-a8f7-98531a6b1344">
		<rdfs:label>article-214e1fb6-bfdd-4059-a8f7-98531a6b1344</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Trump administration’s restrictive immigration policies have not deterred pregnant women from seeking to enter the United States.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0ac4eacb-81ae-4c9e-9ef7-b8474b71a672"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-214e35a2-a551-4d12-9c53-9834c48b78ac">
		<rdfs:label>article-214e35a2-a551-4d12-9c53-9834c48b78ac</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats announced that their Milwaukee convention would be almost entirely virtual, citing coronavirus concerns. Biden will skip the convention and accept the nomination in Delaware. In primary races, progressives triumphed and a polarizing Republican fell.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-215189f3-8e4f-4a12-89d8-c74050dd9c62">
		<rdfs:label>article-215189f3-8e4f-4a12-89d8-c74050dd9c62</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Friday: A family-owned restaurant went from being a popular buffet spot to only serving takeout food overnight. Ten months later, it is still here.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-14f82d09-3a15-43b0-8f6d-ebdb1405d989"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-21592d19-77d6-45f0-b721-feda44b89864">
		<rdfs:label>article-21592d19-77d6-45f0-b721-feda44b89864</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The former president faces serious legal jeopardy. A defeat for Herschel Walker would hardly help him with Republican voters.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e9c4025-7dbe-4808-a3d4-b9d25fa14354"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-215d394f-e9b0-4f9a-b8d0-a8c5e27da039">
		<rdfs:label>article-215d394f-e9b0-4f9a-b8d0-a8c5e27da039</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Steven Dillingham resigned on Monday as director of the Census Bureau, bringing an early end to a tumultuous tenure that culminated this month in charges that he had allowed politics to override policy at the nation’s premier statistical agency.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-be4a3e54-4b34-4f4b-b446-90f3692a587d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2166a811-a0fe-4ea8-8ed5-31d4f0651dc9">
		<rdfs:label>article-2166a811-a0fe-4ea8-8ed5-31d4f0651dc9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>While Justice Ruth Bader Ginsburg was alive, the prospect of an epic political and cultural battle was averted. But her death has brought a particular whiplash of sorrow and anger to Washington.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dcd0eb75-780a-43fe-aa5a-ac14ace05e96"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2167eaf6-afa5-4b06-88b1-254a2e680d98">
		<rdfs:label>article-2167eaf6-afa5-4b06-88b1-254a2e680d98</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With voters distracted by other issues and election denial flourishing, the country has what academics call a legitimacy problem.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e9c4025-7dbe-4808-a3d4-b9d25fa14354"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-21687760-8f51-47aa-88fd-096fc203ee32">
		<rdfs:label>article-21687760-8f51-47aa-88fd-096fc203ee32</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Renewed attacks on Afghan forces over the weekend underscored the difficulties of enforcing a peace agreement — and understanding what was happening on the ground.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3bea54bd-f3ee-4712-b704-2739e55e376e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2169303b-9c27-4374-9407-3d3f5a23189d">
		<rdfs:label>article-2169303b-9c27-4374-9407-3d3f5a23189d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Terry McAuliffe, the former governor of Virginia, will enter the contest for his old job on Wednesday, according to a person familiar with his plans, joining an already crowded Democratic primary that is likely to serve as a harbinger of the party’s future.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-216eb1ed-04ed-459f-a6ae-2f9ce240759c">
		<rdfs:label>article-216eb1ed-04ed-459f-a6ae-2f9ce240759c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The question of who should be chosen as California’s next senator is a battle between Black and Latino representation.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9c6cc67a-b3c2-45c5-af7a-92a423ab1249"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2172ec6a-f23a-4be3-83f9-4bbc28930b6b">
		<rdfs:label>article-2172ec6a-f23a-4be3-83f9-4bbc28930b6b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>“I’m calling on more business to step up. I’m calling on more parents to get their children vaccinated when they are eligible,” President Biden said.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2174490f-bf17-4006-b33e-5b98f4f3b03f">
		<rdfs:label>article-2174490f-bf17-4006-b33e-5b98f4f3b03f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mazars USA delivered an initial set of documents related to the former president’s finances to the House Oversight Committee as part of a settlement.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-17"/>
