	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2178543b-747a-44c7-987d-3b62e60d0994">
		<rdfs:label>article-2178543b-747a-44c7-987d-3b62e60d0994</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The balance of recent surveys suggests that the desire to return to normalcy has approached or even overtaken alarm about the coronavirus itself.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-17ddcb21-b8ba-45a7-8e71-073c17f7026b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2181fc05-36a5-4f8f-917d-0e97dae479d8">
		<rdfs:label>article-2181fc05-36a5-4f8f-917d-0e97dae479d8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In Canonsburg, known for its big Fourth of July parade, many people say they are proud of America and its military but weary of the two-decade war in Afghanistan.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c2e66850-f7bc-45ca-83ed-c0a1f8490a14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-17"/>
