	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-221e7480-213d-41ba-b987-3f67eee5346d">
		<rdfs:label>article-221e7480-213d-41ba-b987-3f67eee5346d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Biden administration has moved aggressively to undo former President Donald J. Trump’s policies and dislodge his loyalists from positions on boards and civil-service jobs, but it has hesitated on a related choice: whether to remove two inspectors general appointed by Mr. Trump under a storm of partisan controversy.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-02"/>
