	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-22b62e12-79cb-4334-8cce-98ee19a792a0">
		<rdfs:label>article-22b62e12-79cb-4334-8cce-98ee19a792a0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Members of Congress have begun a frenzy of lobbying to ensure that their pet projects and policy priorities are included in President Biden’s $2 trillion infrastructure and jobs plan, eager to shape what could be one of the most substantial public works investments in a generation.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-83d40723-6a13-432d-8617-d546a58e6733"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
