	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-256b0d01-6663-4dbe-af5a-9c5b229ac370">
		<rdfs:label>article-256b0d01-6663-4dbe-af5a-9c5b229ac370</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>John McCain once said, “May the words I utter today be tender and sweet, because tomorrow I may have to eat them.” The current White House has served up a buffet, with the president as head chef.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dcd0eb75-780a-43fe-aa5a-ac14ace05e96"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-256bbe26-d0d8-4888-8d60-87ad03a4ac57">
		<rdfs:label>article-256bbe26-d0d8-4888-8d60-87ad03a4ac57</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Beyond the R.N.C.’s walls, things haven’t slowed down.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-887d1269-7020-4c8e-8dfc-eae7c464f3cb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-256c071a-310d-420f-a7f6-3f5be4e60d6c">
		<rdfs:label>article-256c071a-310d-420f-a7f6-3f5be4e60d6c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>About 40 million people were at risk of severe thunderstorms or tornadoes, from Texas to Tennessee. To the north, rain, flooding and ice were all in the forecast.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d0804387-7ba1-4df8-b8ae-a8a9c6bfc424"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-256e4541-e416-449b-917c-7ebf93171547">
		<rdfs:label>article-256e4541-e416-449b-917c-7ebf93171547</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Medical providers must not engage in “ruthless utilitarianism” in deciding who gets lifesaving treatment for the coronavirus, a federal civil rights officer warned.</rdfs:comment>
