	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-259a7862-eea6-43a8-9f5e-7da26dc04f89">
		<rdfs:label>article-259a7862-eea6-43a8-9f5e-7da26dc04f89</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A deal would have a limited impact on the American economy, but the Trump administration sees it as an important geopolitical move.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-94d58c04-d925-44a3-9534-35b73b8dc25d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-259b38e1-030b-4254-a4a2-060c67f96b1d">
		<rdfs:label>article-259b38e1-030b-4254-a4a2-060c67f96b1d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>CHAPEL HILL, N.C. — By Sunday morning, less than two days after the death of Justice Ruth Bader Ginsburg, the signs were already stapled to telephone poles in this liberal college town. “VOTE!” they read, above an Uncle Sam-style image of the iconic feminist jurist.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-259c8ab8-4541-4f76-ac32-98629d960663">
		<rdfs:label>article-259c8ab8-4541-4f76-ac32-98629d960663</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A 2020 kidnapping plot against Gov. Gretchen Whitmer rattled Michigan. On Friday, her Republican opponent, Tudor Dixon, used it as a punchline in two campaign stops.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6fcc2118-4d59-415b-8f82-fd519f6b2d34"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-259e531c-d65e-4873-82f9-6553edeec13d">
		<rdfs:label>article-259e531c-d65e-4873-82f9-6553edeec13d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Dan Friesen and Jordan Holmes turned their Infowars-skewering podcast into a business. In the post-Trump era, they’re documenting Mr. Jones’s reckoning.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5f60b7f2-92f5-4980-9c8e-e8bf01cdb98f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-259e84af-7d7f-4b8c-8739-5b91e3e48fde">
		<rdfs:label>article-259e84af-7d7f-4b8c-8739-5b91e3e48fde</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>One president all but declared victory over the pandemic, hailing new vaccines as a “medical miracle” and congratulating himself for doing what “nobody has ever seen before.” The next president declared the pandemic deadlier than ever, calling it a “mass casualty” event that is leaving “a gaping hole” in America with more misery to come.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-922ad7b9-e6de-456a-9bc2-69207748d175"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-259ead10-be76-48ea-80c3-84b550f77a7f">
		<rdfs:label>article-259ead10-be76-48ea-80c3-84b550f77a7f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The first lady and the surgeon general visited an elementary school in Virginia as part of a strategy to enlist schools in promoting the vaccine.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25a07c39-6751-4c79-ba53-dbbdb5d3520a">
		<rdfs:label>article-25a07c39-6751-4c79-ba53-dbbdb5d3520a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The episode highlighted how murky new guidelines toward past use are, particularly for a White House that has pledged to embrace progressive positions.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd42dd7e-7a0d-4a74-908e-252de023edfb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25a15310-03dd-428f-a638-696af87ad7d6">
		<rdfs:label>article-25a15310-03dd-428f-a638-696af87ad7d6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The infrastructure bill could reshape priorities across the country, jump-starting critical projects that stalled over funding. These are some of the possibilities.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-011ddbd5-8a1e-4932-8bfc-bad05d0ca67f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25a9183e-633e-413a-8e74-284e4845baac">
		<rdfs:label>article-25a9183e-633e-413a-8e74-284e4845baac</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Among the plans under consideration is whether to give migrant families a chance to apply for protections, and to possibly lifting the public health rule for single adults this summer.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dad1523a-f983-4f0f-af53-0061c7165e91"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25ab223f-0937-4401-bd04-96f0f9548f5e">
		<rdfs:label>article-25ab223f-0937-4401-bd04-96f0f9548f5e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>“The Burmese military regime continues to ignore the will of the people of Burma to restore the country’s path to democracy,” Secretary of State Antony J. Blinken said.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7479f929-0522-4f1f-a391-dcdb5f4e726c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25adebe0-efae-470b-92ed-2a921c1345dd">
		<rdfs:label>article-25adebe0-efae-470b-92ed-2a921c1345dd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Nonessential federal employees should be working from home.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25af1779-a8c6-4a59-b0d7-e53e7ad2df0f">
		<rdfs:label>article-25af1779-a8c6-4a59-b0d7-e53e7ad2df0f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Six of the nine deadliest mass shootings in the United States since 2018 were by people who were 21 or younger, a shift from earlier decades.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-58bc2d57-e088-419e-b3d5-1e8b56d1de98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7479f929-0522-4f1f-a391-dcdb5f4e726c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25b0d199-6e19-4cf0-9335-861bd9fc8b42">
		<rdfs:label>article-25b0d199-6e19-4cf0-9335-861bd9fc8b42</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Doctors and nurses in a Florida hospital thought the onslaught of coronavirus admissions had ended. Now they need more intensive care beds.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25b14d56-355c-4ee8-b1af-c2294f12a412">
		<rdfs:label>article-25b14d56-355c-4ee8-b1af-c2294f12a412</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats are debating whether doing nothing will cost more than doing something to deal with climate change, education, child care, prescription drugs and more.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6c995819-c171-430e-a414-f6167b134557"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25b6dbd0-8faa-4247-8896-07bf971d7de0">
		<rdfs:label>article-25b6dbd0-8faa-4247-8896-07bf971d7de0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The legislation would invest in traditional research and development, clashing with a broad Senate measure that focuses on cutting-edge technology to compete with China.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25bbc658-654c-4153-b3f9-09b569f91383">
		<rdfs:label>article-25bbc658-654c-4153-b3f9-09b569f91383</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In Maine, Sara Gideon prevailed over limited competition in the Democratic primary for Senate and will face Susan Collins in a race that has become the priciest Senate campaign in the state’s history.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-1a919c05-175d-4b8d-9183-278fc0c9195c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25bf57f3-aca5-4ba0-a9d3-132584fac750">
		<rdfs:label>article-25bf57f3-aca5-4ba0-a9d3-132584fac750</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mr. Cawthorn’s victory in the G.O.P. primary for a House seat formerly held by Mark Meadows, the White House chief of staff, was an upset for his handpicked successor, who had the president’s backing.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25c26467-a15b-45d4-8b0d-55ac823b0ae4">
		<rdfs:label>article-25c26467-a15b-45d4-8b0d-55ac823b0ae4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As the congressional committee investigating the Capitol riot races to conclude its work, the political stakes are increasing along with the legal expectations.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e9c4025-7dbe-4808-a3d4-b9d25fa14354"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-89135d87-ed63-4619-a5ce-c3f23d9e6fd4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25c50845-95aa-4318-adfa-81289daba654">
		<rdfs:label>article-25c50845-95aa-4318-adfa-81289daba654</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Representative Steve Scalise, the second-ranking House Republican, replaced a video that Twitter flagged as having been manipulated because the words of a progressive activist who was questioning Joseph R. Biden Jr. on his stance on defunding the police were misleadingly grafted together.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7da4dfa6-58ba-4b1b-8d80-6c39df820022"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8a614115-3578-4c7f-b70a-6cdd9b0a4f3d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25c9213e-1fe5-4eb5-b3fc-75e9891f5228">
		<rdfs:label>article-25c9213e-1fe5-4eb5-b3fc-75e9891f5228</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mr. Kristof, a two-time Pulitzer Prize winner known for his coverage of human rights abuses and women’s rights, said friends were trying to recruit him into the race to replace Gov. Kate Brown, a Democrat.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25c98c3d-c4d6-4da8-9548-ee1f165346d7">
		<rdfs:label>article-25c98c3d-c4d6-4da8-9548-ee1f165346d7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With Republicans set to filibuster, Democrats are focusing on staying unified in the face of defeat. But the path ahead for the legislation is murky at best.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25cb64ec-b122-4114-905b-0b07bfeb7c45">
		<rdfs:label>article-25cb64ec-b122-4114-905b-0b07bfeb7c45</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>We made it to election night, together. I’ll be keeping an eye on a few key places to get an early sense of how the results are unfolding.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25d0b941-a93e-4747-9681-2f4639ddc9a2">
		<rdfs:label>article-25d0b941-a93e-4747-9681-2f4639ddc9a2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Puerto Rico’s troubled history with its electrical service took a dramatic turn when the head of a private company that took over the power grid was held in contempt.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25d270ed-9d46-4c9b-8af5-6f81859d4672">
		<rdfs:label>article-25d270ed-9d46-4c9b-8af5-6f81859d4672</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Most politicians are hypocrites. Voters tend not to care. </rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd146215-8c12-40b0-bfb7-0d9c07c5e63d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25ddd591-ddf1-40e2-aeb8-b41aab3be76c">
		<rdfs:label>article-25ddd591-ddf1-40e2-aeb8-b41aab3be76c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>California became the first state to reach 500,000 total coronavirus cases. Once the site of a major outbreak, Italy now offers lessons for keeping the virus in check.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25e1b565-febc-4a72-a0cf-d3a7678229fc">
		<rdfs:label>article-25e1b565-febc-4a72-a0cf-d3a7678229fc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A federal appeals court ruled that a school board in Washington State could require the coach to stop praying at the 50-yard line after high school football games.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-947ed571-ad87-49fb-b59a-9372d166d3c7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25e1f43d-874c-4eea-87a0-a0fcb62693fb">
		<rdfs:label>article-25e1f43d-874c-4eea-87a0-a0fcb62693fb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Little is known about how a gallows came to be built near the Capitol, but the motif has become a favorite among right-wing extremists and white supremacists.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25e86296-0104-4dd6-b6ab-98a25e053621">
		<rdfs:label>article-25e86296-0104-4dd6-b6ab-98a25e053621</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>When the history of the Trump presidency is written, the clash with protesters that preceded President Trump’s walk across Lafayette Square may be remembered as one of its defining moments.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8b00605f-8eb9-4c84-bc14-9844319ed884"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-922ad7b9-e6de-456a-9bc2-69207748d175"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-97c01eac-52d6-4a76-a255-0fa61aef87cd"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-cb1c6257-e55e-46d6-bc3c-fe31dd29d0a0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd42dd7e-7a0d-4a74-908e-252de023edfb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd522e1c-57a0-49bc-9835-fae39d9d58a6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-25e95f97-b889-41ae-b147-8ac301164fed">
		<rdfs:label>article-25e95f97-b889-41ae-b147-8ac301164fed</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Three weeks into her tenure as Boston’s acting mayor, Kim Janey has done something her predecessor did not: order the police to release documents about a leader accused of sexual abuse.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-91caa243-6ff4-4c6d-affc-51bd8da8617d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
