		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-29eae5b8-147e-4084-abc7-576e1f16bacc">
		<rdfs:label>article-29eae5b8-147e-4084-abc7-576e1f16bacc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Keep an eye on what President Trump’s lawyers say about supposed voter fraud while they’re in an actual courtroom.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-29f15a09-97e5-4c3d-aba1-b33c375e250c">
		<rdfs:label>article-29f15a09-97e5-4c3d-aba1-b33c375e250c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>“We don’t have enough resources to adequately treat the patients in our hospitals, whether you are there for Covid-19 or a heart attack or because of a car accident,” said a top state health official.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-078e57d0-5b20-48e9-b039-c2569b2acb05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-becd702f-c674-4653-9a6c-90ee51977e85"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-29f2cc13-daba-4cf1-8cd6-3dd321ffeb77">
		<rdfs:label>article-29f2cc13-daba-4cf1-8cd6-3dd321ffeb77</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president sidestepped Congress when it became clear that his nominee for a top Defense Department position would not win Senate approval.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-46b2f3e2-fc43-4d1f-8134-a17365f8ec33"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-29f6db82-f1bc-4c6a-ba3c-97df0d15208c">
		<rdfs:label>article-29f6db82-f1bc-4c6a-ba3c-97df0d15208c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Representative Liz Cheney, Republican of Wyoming, who lost her primary to a Trump-backed challenger, has been focused on trying to keep election deniers out of office.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c67a9047-7b94-4e45-aaa9-c820c2b967de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-29f8a2b8-1ff4-47df-8a54-b3e2df0add3d">
		<rdfs:label>article-29f8a2b8-1ff4-47df-8a54-b3e2df0add3d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>“My instincts were telling me that something’s wrong,” Jena Scurry testified in court on Monday.</rdfs:comment>
