	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a45aa5c-0476-479d-8ee4-30fd0c5b4c46">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a45aa5c-0476-479d-8ee4-30fd0c5b4c46</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As President Trump refused to concede defeat on Saturday, top Republican congressional leaders followed suit, refraining from releasing the customary statements congratulating the victor that have been standard among senior lawmakers in both parties when a presidential election has been declared.</rdfs:comment>
