	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a5e9a79-5ebb-4f12-9d4c-27e452208772">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a5e9a79-5ebb-4f12-9d4c-27e452208772</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>William J. Walker has testified about how his requests for approval to deploy the National Guard on Jan. 6 went unanswered. Now it falls to him to prevent another rampage.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a66e21a-ade2-4123-a995-66261dc0d5a8">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a66e21a-ade2-4123-a995-66261dc0d5a8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The senator from Maine has emerged from the toughest re-election battle of her career more influential than ever, and ready to play a crucial deal-making role in a divided Senate.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a6989f8-5a44-4ead-aad6-220b0575a046">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a6989f8-5a44-4ead-aad6-220b0575a046</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The leaders heading to the Glasgow climate talks have made progress in recent years. But Earth is still on track for dangerous warming unless those efforts accelerate.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a6cde8f-4a3f-4eb6-a251-e5d2917abc0a">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a6cde8f-4a3f-4eb6-a251-e5d2917abc0a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mark Kelly, the former astronaut trying to unseat the Republican senator Martha McSally in Arizona, is one of the best-funded Democratic challengers in the nation. His latest ad uses an unusual narrator — Ms. McSally’s colleague, the Democratic senator Kyrsten Sinema — to push back on Ms. McSally’s attacks.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a6dfa8f-eb81-4ab5-b9f4-823fbbc5ced5">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a6dfa8f-eb81-4ab5-b9f4-823fbbc5ced5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Provincetown, Mass., the quirky community at the tip of Cape Cod, thought it was safe to return to prepandemic partying. It wasn’t.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-73dbb09e-59d9-4874-86d0-c19361c42fdb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-91caa243-6ff4-4c6d-affc-51bd8da8617d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a6e568c-f98a-4835-93bf-52dfde549f62">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a6e568c-f98a-4835-93bf-52dfde549f62</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Trying to find another avenue to push his baseless election claims, Donald Trump considered installing a loyalist.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd522e1c-57a0-49bc-9835-fae39d9d58a6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a6ea3a0-b2f1-44fd-a630-def39046fb5c">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a6ea3a0-b2f1-44fd-a630-def39046fb5c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Technology advances forced the Census Bureau to use sweeping measures to ensure privacy for respondents. The ensuing debate goes to the heart of what a census is.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-be4a3e54-4b34-4f4b-b446-90f3692a587d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a701dca-435a-4f80-9f6a-9a3ccaed2fdb">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a701dca-435a-4f80-9f6a-9a3ccaed2fdb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Gov. Kevin Stitt said he was “pretty shocked” to become the first governor known to have contracted the virus. Oklahoma has averaged more than 640 new cases per day over the past week.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-781f7c76-864b-4901-8b16-90c83d96e113"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d0804387-7ba1-4df8-b8ae-a8a9c6bfc424"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a73805a-e144-419d-a3fe-6de7485e4467">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a73805a-e144-419d-a3fe-6de7485e4467</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The U.S. Office of Government Ethics published financial disclosure forms on Thursday morning for Katherine Tai, the Biden administration’s expected nominee for the position of United States Trade Representative. Ms. Tai currently serves as chief trade counsel for the House Ways and Means Committee.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-94d58c04-d925-44a3-9534-35b73b8dc25d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a759654-538f-4afd-8444-9ae6b5f9c68e">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a759654-538f-4afd-8444-9ae6b5f9c68e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>ATLANTA, Ga. — A man working at a vote-counting site in Atlanta earlier this week has gone into hiding after being wrongly accused of discarding a ballot, according to Richard Barron, elections director for Georgia’s largest county, Fulton.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9943b18b-b21a-4097-affa-8e1a1ddd74f7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a7af3bf-bdbe-4df9-b7c6-a43aa88251c2">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a7af3bf-bdbe-4df9-b7c6-a43aa88251c2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Kanye West, the hip-hop artist and fashion designer who launched an independent presidential bid earlier this year, cast a vote for himself on Tuesday in what he said on Twitter was his first time voting in a presidential election.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9c6bcf1d-e179-43a7-9f78-6139ef8f52e0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a8065a1-44e4-460a-9ba3-710c0f0291b1">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a8065a1-44e4-460a-9ba3-710c0f0291b1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden announced that his administration would double its order of Pfizer’s scarce Covid-19 antiviral drug, which has been shown to reduce hospitalizations.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e4ac7a5-be1a-4937-b91e-66276e5f8dd9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7cf59892-95ab-4467-bd6d-b2944623f5eb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a814627-f9e0-4f26-89ab-e8e7d5d4db5c">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a814627-f9e0-4f26-89ab-e8e7d5d4db5c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Nostalgia for a time when Democratic leaders could embrace Republican leaders in a moment of crisis — and when a bipartisan group would gather for an annual roasting in Washington.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dcd0eb75-780a-43fe-aa5a-ac14ace05e96"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a87135f-2dcd-457d-a14c-f8d255d60d3e">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a87135f-2dcd-457d-a14c-f8d255d60d3e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Even as it seeks to rejoin a global council focused on protecting human rights, the United States must first aggressively address its own abuses — particularly against people of color, women, religious minorities and its L.G.B.T.Q. community, Secretary of State Antony J. Blinken said on Wednesday.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-71a85d28-5b81-446d-8c87-47f2948de4fa"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f4f38f08-6492-4112-8b82-52bd8aa6b34f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc2c2b47-32c2-43a0-8e5f-dd4e72335932"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a886648-79e6-46a9-91f7-8e2824bb1dcf">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a886648-79e6-46a9-91f7-8e2824bb1dcf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Negotiators from around the world are meeting in Canada in an effort to halt, and reverse, staggering declines in wildlife.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2afe2750-7a7d-460f-b9fb-4feddaf4f58b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2a8920c8-d13a-4be6-bf04-cf007353cc44">
		<rdfs:label>article-2a8920c8-d13a-4be6-bf04-cf007353cc44</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Decisions to bus migrants to the vice president’s residence and to fly others to Martha’s Vineyard were the latest attempts to provoke outrage over record arrivals at the border.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4d4e3743-3cf6-49c9-beea-1b12b8881a42"/>
