	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2b855f51-cf92-44d8-a181-4d32310c5218">
		<rdfs:label>article-2b855f51-cf92-44d8-a181-4d32310c5218</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The celebrity physician, a candidate in Pennsylvania’s Republican primary for Senate, has a long history of dispensing dubious medical advice on his daytime show and on Fox News.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c2e66850-f7bc-45ca-83ed-c0a1f8490a14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-12-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2b87fe27-0bdc-4666-9bb8-d5838d59c6b0">
		<rdfs:label>article-2b87fe27-0bdc-4666-9bb8-d5838d59c6b0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Preliminary research data show that about a fifth of all Americans who bought guns last year were first-time gun owners. Sales usually spike around elections, but the sheer volume is notable.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-81f0af94-b9cf-4dcb-8ae5-91c423d251ff"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2b8aa9d0-7801-4d01-9744-36525edd1d23">
		<rdfs:label>article-2b8aa9d0-7801-4d01-9744-36525edd1d23</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Simla, Colo., an isolated ranching community on the high plains, is the last place locals expect to be first for anything, especially a new, more infectious variant of the coronavirus.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fd9f1ad4-cd49-4185-a0bb-a129097c5a29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2b8bc6bf-8968-4412-a2c7-dad9ae8c9a3f">
		<rdfs:label>article-2b8bc6bf-8968-4412-a2c7-dad9ae8c9a3f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Here are some of the key local and statewide races and measures to watch in California.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-738c55e5-1f96-4b93-8c70-fc8c1c8c9119"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2b8e780c-f537-41bd-8806-a26c44e8b7ab">
		<rdfs:label>article-2b8e780c-f537-41bd-8806-a26c44e8b7ab</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Knowing the intentions of any autocratic leader is difficult, but President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia, who began his career as a K.G.B. officer, poses a particular challenge.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5a3094b1-6bc7-47d7-8f53-c56fd8ed0c59"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6f60db0f-4977-4567-b7bd-9abe5d4a35e8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2b8f07e5-abcf-4782-bbe8-1b7541dc13c8">
		<rdfs:label>article-2b8f07e5-abcf-4782-bbe8-1b7541dc13c8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>While it is hard to predict when we might get returns on election night, there are factors that can give us clues.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4d1965e-83d5-427c-92cb-8140b08c5176"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2b92bf34-1e0e-4523-bf22-f4848878e1dd">
		<rdfs:label>article-2b92bf34-1e0e-4523-bf22-f4848878e1dd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The tax would require that American households worth more than $100 million pay a rate of at least 20 percent on their income as well as unrealized gains in the value of liquid assets like stocks.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2b948ce0-3844-439e-995c-3f5b1c8e1139">
		<rdfs:label>article-2b948ce0-3844-439e-995c-3f5b1c8e1139</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As a Republican review of 2020 votes in Arizona sputtered to a close, Donald Trump and his allies signaled that their attack on the election, and their drive to reshape future elections, were far from over.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-93d154d3-6d3d-4599-ac55-e63a146d8d6f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2b9a91a6-7f52-4209-90c8-160c884d4a55">
		<rdfs:label>article-2b9a91a6-7f52-4209-90c8-160c884d4a55</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Top officials at the department met with prosecutors and the local police in Philadelphia in an effort to help cities prepare for a hot-weather crime wave marked by the Fourth of July.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7479f929-0522-4f1f-a391-dcdb5f4e726c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2b9b0b70-d8d4-4940-9d3a-b480be6a7c34">
		<rdfs:label>article-2b9b0b70-d8d4-4940-9d3a-b480be6a7c34</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Biden administration told a British court that the WikiLeaks founder would not be isolated and could serve out any sentence in Australia.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2b9c36b8-07fb-4ba7-a24a-9fd142f3dd62">
		<rdfs:label>article-2b9c36b8-07fb-4ba7-a24a-9fd142f3dd62</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The winner of Tuesday’s runoff will have the distinction of succeeding John Lewis, a giant of the civil rights era, and closing out what would have been the final days of his 17th term in Congress.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc5a47b7-5e7e-4d58-8ee7-caaf2f703c6a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2b9e13d2-b8a5-4803-b5a0-970bf96812fe">
		<rdfs:label>article-2b9e13d2-b8a5-4803-b5a0-970bf96812fe</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services has asked Congress for a lifeline amid the coronavirus pandemic, which has caused applications to plummet and brought it to the brink of insolvency.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4b043cde-c9ac-41fc-91ae-7eae6c420e38"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2ba074ab-c176-4806-b692-4487905f56f9">
		<rdfs:label>article-2ba074ab-c176-4806-b692-4487905f56f9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Two appeals courts nominees drew scant Republican support. Their approval was part of a post-Trump push by Democrats to rebalance the courts.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0e84c75e-7bc1-4744-83f1-7496fcf4721d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2ba33c0f-126b-4382-93fa-da683ffa02bf">
		<rdfs:label>article-2ba33c0f-126b-4382-93fa-da683ffa02bf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>For more than three decades, Eso Won Books has championed Black writers. The store is closing by the end of the year, its co-founder says.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-10ac2d2b-df6f-4f6e-81ed-6043c29aa826"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2ba37da9-bf81-4ff6-9e59-05e835d9437b">
		<rdfs:label>article-2ba37da9-bf81-4ff6-9e59-05e835d9437b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Few expect Mr. Buttigieg, the former mayor and now former presidential candidate, to remain at home for long. Here’s some ideas for what he could consider next.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2ba400c3-d819-4e3a-b432-a5fff1b7835c">
		<rdfs:label>article-2ba400c3-d819-4e3a-b432-a5fff1b7835c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Both parties have now lodged complaints saying the opposing party’s leader ran afoul of election law in not officially declaring 2024 presidential runs.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e9c4025-7dbe-4808-a3d4-b9d25fa14354"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2ba47ead-a559-44ae-83f8-1dfa5ff68dc4">
		<rdfs:label>article-2ba47ead-a559-44ae-83f8-1dfa5ff68dc4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The shift away from high-volume centers is an acknowledgment of the harder road ahead: a highly targeted push, akin to get-out-the-vote efforts, to persuade the reluctant to get shots.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2ba4d3c5-246f-4372-b231-32d888b30ec9">
		<rdfs:label>article-2ba4d3c5-246f-4372-b231-32d888b30ec9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Rolling back regulations ignores the central lessons from the country’s largest oil spill.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2ba59e41-0b9c-444c-a876-bb221122d0df">
		<rdfs:label>article-2ba59e41-0b9c-444c-a876-bb221122d0df</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As the world watches demonstrations unfold on television and social media, both the best and the worst of American law enforcement has been on display.</rdfs:comment>
