	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2bd49fa4-89a9-4ce2-b7a9-aad023bcc300">
		<rdfs:label>article-2bd49fa4-89a9-4ce2-b7a9-aad023bcc300</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The tribe has survived for more than a thousand years in the arid mesas. The megadrought gripping the Southwest is testing that resilience.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f7d54296-4f6d-4656-bd4e-ce98de1cb5ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2bd6396c-603a-49ff-adae-4d3b5d663e8d">
		<rdfs:label>article-2bd6396c-603a-49ff-adae-4d3b5d663e8d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In Arizona, where elections are getting closer, a federal appeals court undid strict limits on ballot collection and votes cast at the wrong precinct.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-be4a3e54-4b34-4f4b-b446-90f3692a587d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2bdb709a-afb8-4d20-8e67-953c0fb7c179">
		<rdfs:label>article-2bdb709a-afb8-4d20-8e67-953c0fb7c179</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president pledged to use all of the powers of his office to thwart Republicans still under the thumb of Donald J. Trump.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2bdd8b4f-2230-4fcf-a598-536145ec5011">
		<rdfs:label>article-2bdd8b4f-2230-4fcf-a598-536145ec5011</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A 5.9-magnitude aftershock came on the 15th day since tremors large and small began terrorizing southern Puerto Rico.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2bddc11e-981e-4cc7-96b2-8bb86ed2c84f">
		<rdfs:label>article-2bddc11e-981e-4cc7-96b2-8bb86ed2c84f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Republicans agree that values they view as traditional are at risk, but they’re wrestling with whether isolationism is the answer to their misgivings about global interconnectedness.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6fcc2118-4d59-415b-8f82-fd519f6b2d34"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-803bdb8f-8c3c-4210-80c9-22b0af3fd2ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2bddee9b-845d-4283-8f21-b3ee460eefb0">
		<rdfs:label>article-2bddee9b-845d-4283-8f21-b3ee460eefb0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As the United States begins the most ambitious vaccination drive in its history, with images of relieved health care workers getting a shot in the arm flashing across TV screens and news sites, fresh data revealed that more than one-quarter of Americans say they probably or definitely would not take a coronavirus vaccine.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2bde779c-1e75-4ed5-bb04-8881dda28f6c">
		<rdfs:label>article-2bde779c-1e75-4ed5-bb04-8881dda28f6c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A potential mess in Arizona was an unwelcome surprise for Democrats while they were still savoring their victories in 2022.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e9c4025-7dbe-4808-a3d4-b9d25fa14354"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2be068ac-b1e5-4166-bbf0-7702e44c446c">
		<rdfs:label>article-2be068ac-b1e5-4166-bbf0-7702e44c446c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Representative Marjorie Taylor Greene said being booted from committees left more time for her to push her party to the right. She’s part of a new wave of lawmakers more interested in brand-building than lawmaking.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2be3df33-d175-4ec1-8e12-e1ed61c97b76">
		<rdfs:label>article-2be3df33-d175-4ec1-8e12-e1ed61c97b76</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>For a party that tends to put up a unified front, things are starting to look a little shaky.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2be4f622-4bc3-44db-8d0a-03959eb666f2">
		<rdfs:label>article-2be4f622-4bc3-44db-8d0a-03959eb666f2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The White House has pledged $60 billion to a cause Robert Bullard has championed since the late seventies. He wants guarantees that the money will end up in the right hands.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d49974cc-9ac4-452b-a7a7-40cae7614e64"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2be553e7-bded-42ef-b7b4-cb02b3887534">
		<rdfs:label>article-2be553e7-bded-42ef-b7b4-cb02b3887534</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Christopher Rufo helped make critical race theory a conservative rallying cry. Now he sees L.G.B.T.Q. issues as an even more potent line of attack.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c2e66850-f7bc-45ca-83ed-c0a1f8490a14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2be88467-88dc-4455-ad3e-b274f0001631">
		<rdfs:label>article-2be88467-88dc-4455-ad3e-b274f0001631</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In their quest for Republican backing, Democrats say they missed opportunities in 2009 for a stronger response to the Great Recession. They’re determined not to repeat the mistake.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0e84c75e-7bc1-4744-83f1-7496fcf4721d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2be9057c-3fd5-45f5-8c46-b71924fee8e4">
		<rdfs:label>article-2be9057c-3fd5-45f5-8c46-b71924fee8e4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The death toll has climbed to 16, with almost 150 people missing.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2bee0d36-1031-4d4c-9279-55e52e50c2e6">
		<rdfs:label>article-2bee0d36-1031-4d4c-9279-55e52e50c2e6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Legal fights over how a pot of $8 billion should be allocated have complicated distribution to some of the nation’s poorest and most vulnerable communities.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-bdbbb05b-6fa3-49c7-aa85-71057abb04d2"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2bf559fd-9e39-42c7-90db-439867e89edc">
		<rdfs:label>article-2bf559fd-9e39-42c7-90db-439867e89edc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president’s announcement that he would pitch at Yankee Stadium on Aug. 15 startled the team’s officials, who had not scheduled such an event.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e4ac7a5-be1a-4937-b91e-66276e5f8dd9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd42dd7e-7a0d-4a74-908e-252de023edfb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2bf64ff6-c0df-4bd5-89b9-41814fa6a962">
		<rdfs:label>article-2bf64ff6-c0df-4bd5-89b9-41814fa6a962</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>All 42 million Americans who receive food stamps will soon see their benefits rise, the largest permanent increase in the program’s history, the Biden administration plans to announce on Monday.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9e94ebbb-365e-41ef-9a76-b300ca95c3d1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2bf9307c-797a-414e-ace6-12e765435977">
		<rdfs:label>article-2bf9307c-797a-414e-ace6-12e765435977</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Shop owners hope they don’t experience destruction similar to that of last summer as a verdict draws closer in the Derek Chauvin trial and tensions flare over a police shooting.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b234823e-9687-443c-921d-17ad590417a4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2bfba2f6-f11e-4717-a3fb-93f881924fe9">
		<rdfs:label>article-2bfba2f6-f11e-4717-a3fb-93f881924fe9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The announcement came after the president acknowledged a wildfire season that so far has claimed at least 20 lives and destroyed millions of acres of land in California, Oregon and Washington.</rdfs:comment>
