		<rdfs:label>article-2d2ebb46-faaa-4b68-b991-72572432e579</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Senator James Lankford, an Oklahoma Republican who sits on a key Senate oversight committee, said on a podcast released Wednesday that he had no objections to President-elect Joseph R. Biden Jr. receiving presidential daily briefings, and that he would take action himself if that did not begin by the end of the week.</rdfs:comment>
