	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2dceda50-cc7e-47cc-8298-32dff1282a21">
		<rdfs:label>article-2dceda50-cc7e-47cc-8298-32dff1282a21</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>ST. PAUL, Minn. — Jurors have reached a verdict after about 13 hours of weighing whether three former Minneapolis police officers violated George Floyd’s constitutional rights by not intervening to help him as he pleaded for air while Derek Chauvin knelt on his neck.</rdfs:comment>
