	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2f8ed5fe-b09d-46a5-8797-ebfbc6deb23c">
		<rdfs:label>article-2f8ed5fe-b09d-46a5-8797-ebfbc6deb23c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Pete Buttigieg’s stint at McKinsey gets more attention, but the time he spent driving “real people” around in a van for Al Gore might speak more directly to his candidacy.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dcd0eb75-780a-43fe-aa5a-ac14ace05e96"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-2f96d8a8-8c9f-4219-837a-c2d1de717469">
		<rdfs:label>article-2f96d8a8-8c9f-4219-837a-c2d1de717469</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Days after what might be the most damaging wildfire in state history, residents are just beginning to make sense of the long road back and the extent of the damage.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-072f3594-df4a-4e90-93a4-4757a5d6ad91"/>
