	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-32827fbb-885a-498e-8ec0-a11eb13bd745">
		<rdfs:label>article-32827fbb-885a-498e-8ec0-a11eb13bd745</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Companies see the outbreak as a chance to cash in, do some good, or both. Among the early winners: the Washington influence industry.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9fcaaf17-51fe-4de9-aec7-f53a415e4396"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-3283a67e-4c2a-442e-943d-e32265ace799">
		<rdfs:label>article-3283a67e-4c2a-442e-943d-e32265ace799</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Supreme Court’s move was expected, as Mr. Trump is no longer president and Twitter has permanently suspended his account.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-947ed571-ad87-49fb-b59a-9372d166d3c7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-05"/>
