	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-337b4131-fdc8-421d-94f2-736362731def">
		<rdfs:label>article-337b4131-fdc8-421d-94f2-736362731def</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>If Mark Kelly, the Democratic nominee for Senate in Arizona, unseats Senator Martha McSally, a Republican who was appointed to her seat and began serving last year, he could be sworn in as early as Nov. 30 — possibly in time to vote on a new Supreme Court nominee, elections experts said.</rdfs:comment>
