		<rdfs:label>article-33ca1d82-a669-4b36-a90b-ab8b186c0384</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Both men had similar backgrounds, working for years as Secret Service agents but considered more skilled in navigating the agency’s political infighting than as experts in protection. Both went on to land plum assignments: the sergeants-at-arms of the Senate and House.</rdfs:comment>
