		<rdfs:comment>A president’s address to a joint session of Congress is typically a crowded affair, as lawmakers from both parties, and their guests, pack the House floor. But President Biden’s speech on Wednesday, his first before Congress since his inauguration, will look very different.</rdfs:comment>
