	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-385d4d0f-5ea3-4c11-a4ec-0988bb050d3c">
		<rdfs:label>article-385d4d0f-5ea3-4c11-a4ec-0988bb050d3c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Garrett Rolfe, who was fired after the shooting and now faces criminal charges including felony murder, turned himself in on Thursday.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-385d78a1-5753-4595-8dba-aeed52c70daa">
		<rdfs:label>article-385d78a1-5753-4595-8dba-aeed52c70daa</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Michael Bloomberg’s appearance on the final night of the Democratic convention reignited questions about his pledge to throw his fortune behind the effort to defeat President Trump.</rdfs:comment>
