		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-3d7b24b7-f156-4d44-b5c7-3f1fb8c65d5d">
		<rdfs:label>article-3d7b24b7-f156-4d44-b5c7-3f1fb8c65d5d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Seven minutes elapsed between the initial rumblings and the collapse of Champlain Towers South in Surfside. But a security guard didn’t know how to activate the building’s warning system.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-becd702f-c674-4653-9a6c-90ee51977e85"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-3d7cd496-25dc-4ba9-9194-09dd37669e8f">
		<rdfs:label>article-3d7cd496-25dc-4ba9-9194-09dd37669e8f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Not since Bob Woodward and Carl Bernstein refused for decades to disclose the identity of their Watergate source has Washington been as eager to unmask a leaker.</rdfs:comment>
