		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4169a2db-cc49-4cbe-82cf-551350d930e1">
		<rdfs:label>article-4169a2db-cc49-4cbe-82cf-551350d930e1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The country is full of bird-themed mascots. But only a proud few have embraced the turkey.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a41a9526-e263-45c7-b53f-34febff27f00"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-de093669-b27a-4345-ac65-683caba65a27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-416aecb3-757b-48cb-983e-5e843c95caaa">
		<rdfs:label>article-416aecb3-757b-48cb-983e-5e843c95caaa</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A huge majority of Americans, including nearly two-thirds of Republicans, support the $1,400 stimulus checks President Biden is calling for, and his full $1.9 trillion stimulus proposal also has strong public backing, according to a new poll from Quinnipiac University.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-416fdf56-2faa-4783-9fd9-2388d6927453">
		<rdfs:label>article-416fdf56-2faa-4783-9fd9-2388d6927453</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The tale of a wild fox on Capitol Hill had captivated those who live and work there. Then a congressman and several others were bitten, the fox was captured and she turned out to be rabid.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e0dfbf0e-c179-4f28-a968-4570f9209555"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-416ff593-6bfb-45ca-9760-3a31f7c3d59a">
		<rdfs:label>article-416ff593-6bfb-45ca-9760-3a31f7c3d59a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Federico Klein was an outspoken religious conservative with a “perfectly suburban” background before the F.B.I. arrested him for assaulting Capitol Police.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc2c2b47-32c2-43a0-8e5f-dd4e72335932"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-41736dad-3e42-463e-9fad-3e4decd5f249">
		<rdfs:label>article-41736dad-3e42-463e-9fad-3e4decd5f249</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Setting a meeting gives the two leaders an opportunity for face-to-face time, but President Biden said he would deliver no “fundamental concessions” over Taiwan.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd42dd7e-7a0d-4a74-908e-252de023edfb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-41767c02-049c-4e75-83ef-813942edc6ab">
		<rdfs:label>article-41767c02-049c-4e75-83ef-813942edc6ab</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In Uvalde, Texas, where many children were killed, one family grieves the death of a small boy and holds his sister close.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ba1def2a-fecf-4911-9182-36727aa8deac"/>
