	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-41bac6e0-f7fa-4b68-bb7b-2c89a8697df8">
		<rdfs:label>article-41bac6e0-f7fa-4b68-bb7b-2c89a8697df8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Most parents were accused of crimes to get one child, maybe two, into an elite college. Douglas Hodge, the former chief of Pimco, paid bribes for at least four children, prosecutors say.</rdfs:comment>
