		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-44e7e6cb-1856-43fd-b2f7-7af6bcd2a7d4">
		<rdfs:label>article-44e7e6cb-1856-43fd-b2f7-7af6bcd2a7d4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Monday: Marqueece Harris-Dawson, a Los Angeles councilman, talks about why protests haven’t died down.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-738c55e5-1f96-4b93-8c70-fc8c1c8c9119"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-44ebe56b-2b6b-433d-809c-3e44be5691e5">
		<rdfs:label>article-44ebe56b-2b6b-433d-809c-3e44be5691e5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Plenty of numbers can quantify the way the pandemic and the resulting recession have battered the United States: At least 7.8 million people have fallen into poverty, the biggest plunge in six decades; 85 million Americans say they have had trouble paying basic household expenses, including food and rent.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ae47edf3-29dc-462d-b74b-f886ebf56402"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-44ed2aad-79bf-49db-89e7-afbc3036f739">
		<rdfs:label>article-44ed2aad-79bf-49db-89e7-afbc3036f739</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Thursday: A recent U.S.C. study about the sport takes on new urgency.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-738c55e5-1f96-4b93-8c70-fc8c1c8c9119"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-44f1fa88-c836-4e65-89b3-c6c0d3d77c96">
		<rdfs:label>article-44f1fa88-c836-4e65-89b3-c6c0d3d77c96</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Taking aim at a key plank of the former president’s impeachment defense, the lawyers argued that the constitutional protections do not apply to an impeachment proceeding.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-44f4edce-6654-43e1-943f-37728cdd5353">
		<rdfs:label>article-44f4edce-6654-43e1-943f-37728cdd5353</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Before prosecutors called their first witness, lawyers for both sides made opening statements to jurors in the trial of Derek Chauvin, the former Minneapolis police officer charged with murder in George Floyd’s death.</rdfs:comment>
