	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-47e1199a-0b28-450f-be93-a5b451de9f2c">
		<rdfs:label>article-47e1199a-0b28-450f-be93-a5b451de9f2c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>California, the nation’s most populous state, will scrap most of its complex, frequently shifting pandemic rules on Tuesday — one of the last states to do so. But that doesn’t mean the state will immediately snap back all the way to prepandemic life.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-738c55e5-1f96-4b93-8c70-fc8c1c8c9119"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-47e2b694-cb0f-45cf-8f55-63888401945f">
		<rdfs:label>article-47e2b694-cb0f-45cf-8f55-63888401945f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>“I guess it’s something in society we know will happen again, over and over,” said a parent who lost a child in the massacre at Sandy Hook Elementary in 2012.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5f60b7f2-92f5-4980-9c8e-e8bf01cdb98f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-47e3fba9-23ee-4607-8249-e0a7ca1cf9c3">
		<rdfs:label>article-47e3fba9-23ee-4607-8249-e0a7ca1cf9c3</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Florida lawmakers, at the request of Gov. Ron DeSantis, passed new laws sharply curtailing mask and vaccine mandates. Fringe anti-vaccination views met with little pushback.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-47e45e1e-426b-44bc-a0cc-26d3fe7f93ce">
		<rdfs:label>article-47e45e1e-426b-44bc-a0cc-26d3fe7f93ce</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As claims about Herschel Walker pile up, Senator Raphael Warnock has stuck with his strategy of bipartisan outreach, relying on ads to slam his opponent.</rdfs:comment>
