	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-486ba456-f743-403a-b430-95a839b12432">
		<rdfs:label>article-486ba456-f743-403a-b430-95a839b12432</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The call that upended Cynthiana, Ky., came around 5 p.m. on March 6. Officials had been bracing for the inevitable, and it had just arrived. A resident was sick. Five others would soon be, too.</rdfs:comment>
