	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49c870ae-6e79-4fdf-adb2-9d4f8a22cca0">
		<rdfs:label>article-49c870ae-6e79-4fdf-adb2-9d4f8a22cca0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Senator Thom Tillis of North Carolina, one of the Republicans’ most vulnerable incumbents, tried to turn around his faltering re-election campaign on Monday night, clashing with Cal Cunningham, his Democratic challenger, in a televised debate that largely focused on the coronavirus pandemic.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49c8a620-98b4-4e69-93d4-7ead75dbaa7d">
		<rdfs:label>article-49c8a620-98b4-4e69-93d4-7ead75dbaa7d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Ms. McCarthy will serve as a senior adviser to President-elect Joseph R. Biden Jr., coordinating climate change policy throughout the government.</rdfs:comment>
