		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49c9356d-712f-49d0-861c-efb45361d886">
		<rdfs:label>article-49c9356d-712f-49d0-861c-efb45361d886</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden, in a prime-time address on Thursday night, exaggerated elements of the coronavirus pandemic along with his, and his predecessor’s, response to it.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-be4afe5b-5317-4441-a7de-57071d96016d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49c9965f-5843-491f-b8d2-ec19390bc4b1">
		<rdfs:label>article-49c9965f-5843-491f-b8d2-ec19390bc4b1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Daily deaths have dropped considerably since their January peak, with about 44 percent of the population now fully vaccinated.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0cc8020e-7db7-428c-8db7-36cf2f5c4168"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3d0d7757-313d-444e-a4df-32876c51aaa0"/>
