	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49d4bc1d-5226-48ab-9275-418aad8517b8">
		<rdfs:label>article-49d4bc1d-5226-48ab-9275-418aad8517b8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>At this point, I’m thinking less about polling averages and more about a few key variables that we can’t predict.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49d56dc2-2dfd-4eae-b8d5-c68b462efb56">
		<rdfs:label>article-49d56dc2-2dfd-4eae-b8d5-c68b462efb56</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump remains the most powerful man in the world, but powerless to achieve what he most wants: to avoid leaving office as a loser.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2c183a13-1898-4deb-ad56-cc02fd034eaf"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49dafb8b-46aa-48a4-8274-1f51894e2c80">
		<rdfs:label>article-49dafb8b-46aa-48a4-8274-1f51894e2c80</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The initial response by President Biden and other Democratic leaders to the overturning of Roe struck many Democrats as painfully inadequate.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49de530c-36d3-4423-9577-13831503d637">
		<rdfs:label>article-49de530c-36d3-4423-9577-13831503d637</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A terse announcement signaled a possible end to a long-running constitutional lawsuit. But former President Donald J. Trump is not a party to the arrangement.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49df3ed4-5a89-4156-bd5f-e36ffb10f94c">
		<rdfs:label>article-49df3ed4-5a89-4156-bd5f-e36ffb10f94c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After more than a week of counting, the Republican Party gained the 218 House seats needed to claim the majority, ushering in an era of divided government.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49e62413-94a6-4132-acdd-d6744ab9c2f5">
		<rdfs:label>article-49e62413-94a6-4132-acdd-d6744ab9c2f5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Jackson Women’s Health Organization was at the center of the case that overturned Roe v. Wade. Already, supporters are planning new ways to help women in one of the poorest spots in the nation get access to abortions.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d7a0b17f-e0aa-44c5-a995-e81e028fa879"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49e896c5-1df0-4fba-8b61-7a1aef5d3475">
		<rdfs:label>article-49e896c5-1df0-4fba-8b61-7a1aef5d3475</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The move by Jesuit priests is the largest such effort by the Roman Catholic Church and comes amid growing calls for reparations across the United States.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3b512360-cf90-44f3-a879-2fee3f0b6dfb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49e9df78-e628-4a7b-b07e-8e9b5807075b">
		<rdfs:label>article-49e9df78-e628-4a7b-b07e-8e9b5807075b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The university, which had climbed to No. 2 in the influential rankings, said it needed more time to address questions about its data, which were raised by a Columbia math professor.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4f1bc425-040c-4850-aa28-f277207d36bf"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49ec8162-936a-40e2-90d2-f3fb01b6099e">
		<rdfs:label>article-49ec8162-936a-40e2-90d2-f3fb01b6099e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The deployment will bring to 14,000 the number of American troops that President Biden has ordered to Europe since the Ukraine crisis began.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-46b2f3e2-fc43-4d1f-8134-a17365f8ec33"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49edf46f-3c20-4cba-9d23-275990787fab">
		<rdfs:label>article-49edf46f-3c20-4cba-9d23-275990787fab</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In the run-up to the midterm elections next month, President Biden is hoping his gearhead reputation will appeal to some parts of the Trump base.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4b06f805-a6f6-4cda-9908-3f8ddd3a0432"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49ee92b2-204d-49d6-979c-79595eca0384">
		<rdfs:label>article-49ee92b2-204d-49d6-979c-79595eca0384</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Ahead of the inauguration, President Joseph Biden and Vice President Kamala Harris attended Mass at the Cathedral of St. Matthew the Apostle in downtown Washington on Wednesday morning, joined by congressional leaders from both parties in a display of unity after weeks of tumult.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-81f0af94-b9cf-4dcb-8ae5-91c423d251ff"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-db01c77c-3043-4daf-9961-68109308c6bc"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49f185fc-47fe-46ef-ae3d-a40bc39b06cf">
		<rdfs:label>article-49f185fc-47fe-46ef-ae3d-a40bc39b06cf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Senator Susan Collins, a centrist from Maine, said a second meeting with Judge Ketanji Brown Jackson alleviated her concerns. It is unclear if other Republicans will join her.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0e84c75e-7bc1-4744-83f1-7496fcf4721d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-49f2cfe5-6492-4e50-a281-bfec837d9b48">
		<rdfs:label>article-49f2cfe5-6492-4e50-a281-bfec837d9b48</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president’s actions just before his supporters’ deadly rampage at the Capitol has created new risks for him.</rdfs:comment>
