	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4aca417e-3906-4359-9a14-8dfeba6ba1c5">
		<rdfs:label>article-4aca417e-3906-4359-9a14-8dfeba6ba1c5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>An unusual collection of founders is planning a $1 million pilot program for Ukrainian college students who are studying in the United States. They will underwrite their educations for a year as long as the students are willing to become “ambassadors” for democracy — with the target for that message being American students.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4aca49fb-f9c1-4634-8b95-bffb02737090">
		<rdfs:label>article-4aca49fb-f9c1-4634-8b95-bffb02737090</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Anchors navigated another day of anxiety and suspense at Fox News, which has reported that Joseph R. Biden has accrued 264 electoral votes, and at CNN, NBC, CBS and ABC, which have him at 253.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-06"/>
