	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4ad93ee8-2d3d-414d-8b66-d78fa75bc3ad">
		<rdfs:label>article-4ad93ee8-2d3d-414d-8b66-d78fa75bc3ad</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After the second day of a Republican National Convention whose proceedings trampled over long-established lines between governing and campaigning, Mark Meadows, the White House chief of staff, scoffed at concerns that President Trump and other top officials were abusing federal offices and property for political gain.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc2c2b47-32c2-43a0-8e5f-dd4e72335932"/>
