		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4ad99ed4-7dd2-4ab4-bd5a-f15978a6f9a7">
		<rdfs:label>article-4ad99ed4-7dd2-4ab4-bd5a-f15978a6f9a7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The former first lady Michelle Obama, one of the Democratic Party’s most respected figures, delivered what the Biden campaign called her “closing argument” for Joseph R. Biden Jr.’s candidacy on Tuesday, speaking in deeply personal terms to Americans disillusioned by politics about the need to vote.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8eb0923f-854c-4241-9d79-040d1aeeb0c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
