	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4b1c9a7d-f60c-4460-bc38-bdeba8cc8fe8">
		<rdfs:label>article-4b1c9a7d-f60c-4460-bc38-bdeba8cc8fe8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The “public charge” rule was supposed to ensure that green cards go only to self-sufficient immigrants, but in the pandemic, it is driving up hunger and leaving Joe Biden with a quandary.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4b1dee98-ba18-409b-9a80-b22fdfb31881">
		<rdfs:label>article-4b1dee98-ba18-409b-9a80-b22fdfb31881</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Nevada’s rules around mail-in voting, and the voters’ embrace of the method contribute to a delay in race calls.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-256e095e-335c-4403-9a00-3366dd2b451f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-11"/>
