	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4b351197-dd12-4088-a496-5792005e5118">
		<rdfs:label>article-4b351197-dd12-4088-a496-5792005e5118</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>On social media, on cable networks and even in the halls of Congress, supporters of Donald J. Trump tried to rewrite history in real time, pushing the fiction that left-wing agitators were to blame for the violence on Jan. 6.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4b39025f-6af5-4729-a0b7-97da74ccdacf">
		<rdfs:label>article-4b39025f-6af5-4729-a0b7-97da74ccdacf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>East and West Coast governors unite, and so do Biden and Sanders: This is your morning tip sheet.</rdfs:comment>
