		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4b472598-508f-4a82-8378-09ce5c8edef3">
		<rdfs:label>article-4b472598-508f-4a82-8378-09ce5c8edef3</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump and Joseph R. Biden Jr. remain locked in a tight race in Georgia, and the state’s two Senate seats, which are both up for grabs, are competitive, according to a poll of state voters released Friday.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8a614115-3578-4c7f-b70a-6cdd9b0a4f3d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4b4747c2-7abd-4112-92ed-8f5bf6a1c364">
		<rdfs:label>article-4b4747c2-7abd-4112-92ed-8f5bf6a1c364</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Justice Brett M. Kavanaugh on Wednesday corrected an error in an opinion he issued as part of a Supreme Court ruling that barred Wisconsin from counting mail-in ballots that arrive after Election Day.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9493ea93-a147-4e19-9296-f5df4abc72c2"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4b4c7f13-5971-4f23-ac86-1260650498b4">
		<rdfs:label>article-4b4c7f13-5971-4f23-ac86-1260650498b4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Fox News, which counts President Trump as one of its most voracious viewers, brushed aside the revelations in a report by The New York Times that the billionaire real estate mogul paid little or no federal income taxes for most of the past 20 years.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-44926325-5c4f-4e18-89e5-b1470d62842c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4bd1aa5-c807-421e-b8ae-1b3824d70300"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4b4f4bc8-6cd7-4a4b-a3dd-e7ac96712685">
		<rdfs:label>article-4b4f4bc8-6cd7-4a4b-a3dd-e7ac96712685</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A return to the nuclear deal is the first step out of the morass.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4b4fc617-c3b8-4f23-8fe1-63f08ba8d3b5">
		<rdfs:label>article-4b4fc617-c3b8-4f23-8fe1-63f08ba8d3b5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A Michigan lawmaker is pushing for a bipartisan effort to secure the release of Paul N. Whelan, who has not contacted his family or the U.S. Embassy since July 4.</rdfs:comment>
