	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4bcb5feb-6615-4f6d-b1b3-244656895556">
		<rdfs:label>article-4bcb5feb-6615-4f6d-b1b3-244656895556</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Conspiracy theorists won a major victory on Tuesday as Marjorie Taylor Greene, a Republican supporter of the convoluted pro-Trump movement QAnon, triumphed in her House primary runoff election in Georgia, all but ensuring that she will represent a deep-red district in Congress.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-93d154d3-6d3d-4599-ac55-e63a146d8d6f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4504805-5b5f-41c7-b157-41ff04a342ad"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-bd6dc076-a1a0-4152-9f20-ce7eece97d34"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4bce3216-c055-48c7-ab16-f5abe92dad1a">
		<rdfs:label>article-4bce3216-c055-48c7-ab16-f5abe92dad1a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>From border controls to anti-union efforts, the Trump administration is using the coronavirus to seek policies that the president wanted before the pandemic.</rdfs:comment>
