	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4beaa318-5ffe-4231-b46f-b0113e439eff">
		<rdfs:label>article-4beaa318-5ffe-4231-b46f-b0113e439eff</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Two weeks after taking office, President Biden has demanded that Myanmar reverse a coup d’état and that Russia release its most famous dissident politician, Aleksei A. Navalny, whose arrest and sentencing incited protests of a size and intensity that surprised officials here, and most likely inside the Kremlin.</rdfs:comment>
