		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4ca18efe-99d6-4011-83ca-1a274970299e">
		<rdfs:label>article-4ca18efe-99d6-4011-83ca-1a274970299e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Campaigning for black votes ahead of Super Tuesday, the former New York mayor was a long way from home.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8bd6a423-6819-4b09-a62a-0da24a70fd29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4ca24eff-7895-4673-85da-f49a2694513f">
		<rdfs:label>article-4ca24eff-7895-4673-85da-f49a2694513f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The divisive “public charge” policy allowed officials to deny permanent residency to immigrants deemed likely to need public benefits, leading some immigrants to even avoid hospitals.</rdfs:comment>
