		<rdfs:label>article-4e017681-fae6-47ed-bc1e-6a1c3da8cb46</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Republican State Senate’s autopsy of the 2020 vote, broadly seen as a shambolic, partisan effort to nurse grievances about Donald J. Trump’s loss here in November, risks driving away some of the very people the party needs to win statewide elections in 2022.</rdfs:comment>
