	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e471668-c5ad-41dd-b233-e1b371a6370c">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e471668-c5ad-41dd-b233-e1b371a6370c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The lengthy legal brief provided the first extended defense of former President Donald J. Trump’s conduct since the Jan. 6 assault on the Capitol. It arrived as senators locked in rules for an exceedingly fast trial.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e489fdb-dce3-42a3-b2c6-dd257ea3f813">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e489fdb-dce3-42a3-b2c6-dd257ea3f813</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump claimed that it was the impeachment charge, not the violence and ransacking of the Capitol, that was “causing tremendous anger.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3d036c4f-8ad0-458c-98fa-b15acd415658"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c67a9047-7b94-4e45-aaa9-c820c2b967de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e49893a-9107-4bce-b63c-864c1a00cc06">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e49893a-9107-4bce-b63c-864c1a00cc06</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The court will hear highly anticipated arguments over whether the president’s accountants and bankers must disclose information about his financial affairs.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-947ed571-ad87-49fb-b59a-9372d166d3c7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e4c9a8e-6432-4a1f-85c5-9233b69eaa7e">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e4c9a8e-6432-4a1f-85c5-9233b69eaa7e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Trump administration officials passed when Pfizer offered months ago to sell the U.S. government additional doses of its Covid-19 vaccine, according to people familiar with the matter.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3263b980-a580-440f-bdd2-6d7fa7bb3fab"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4030cfe1-123b-49ce-ab64-a8c3b8a9ff83"/>
