		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e54af97-2070-47e5-b6e2-f87aff2bcfeb">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e54af97-2070-47e5-b6e2-f87aff2bcfeb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump’s son-in-law has become a central player in the administration’s effort to curb the pandemic. But critics say he is part of the problem.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e4ac7a5-be1a-4937-b91e-66276e5f8dd9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-922ad7b9-e6de-456a-9bc2-69207748d175"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e5548af-9856-4fea-8141-b8963aa3fcfc">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e5548af-9856-4fea-8141-b8963aa3fcfc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president said he also planned to invite South Korea, Australia and India to the meeting of world leaders in order to discuss China’s future.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e559a59-9dd4-4139-8fc7-03b3492f1ecb">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e559a59-9dd4-4139-8fc7-03b3492f1ecb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Trump administration’s decision to eventually withdraw several thousand troops from America’s longest war has triggered a debate within the 29-country alliance.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3bea54bd-f3ee-4712-b704-2739e55e376e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6f60db0f-4977-4567-b7bd-9abe5d4a35e8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e591cca-e6c2-448c-b901-2c6a69b64ab9">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e591cca-e6c2-448c-b901-2c6a69b64ab9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>On the first day of the election-season confirmation hearings, Democrats portrayed Judge Amy Coney Barrett as a threat to Americans’ health care coverage as Republicans charged anti-Catholic bias.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e5a2292-361c-4263-a14c-9f14f83ad6d6">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e5a2292-361c-4263-a14c-9f14f83ad6d6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A federal grand jury has issued at least one subpoena, and investigators are seeking interviews in the case of sensitive documents that ended up at the former president’s Florida home.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2c183a13-1898-4deb-ad56-cc02fd034eaf"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e6226c2-5181-4941-b4eb-630aec27683d">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e6226c2-5181-4941-b4eb-630aec27683d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The voluminous coronavirus relief and spending bill that blasted through Congress on Monday includes provisions — good, bad and just plain strange — that few lawmakers got to read.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-15798bd0-9ac6-4a8f-b8e5-198cebcc4448"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-864756c8-4d62-42e5-a6e4-482550bf62a9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e646ba0-1d25-4ced-bebc-c65664687fdf">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e646ba0-1d25-4ced-bebc-c65664687fdf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>This was no phone call transcript, no dry words on a page open to interpretation. This was a horde of extremists pushing over barricades and beating police officers. This was a mob smashing windows and pounding on doors. This was a mass of marauders setting up a gallows and shouting, “Take the building!” and “Fight for Trump!”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-922ad7b9-e6de-456a-9bc2-69207748d175"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e649830-24f8-4a62-b8e3-ac6d2cc97863">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e649830-24f8-4a62-b8e3-ac6d2cc97863</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As the coronavirus rages, Americans’ views of President Trump have risen slightly to reach record highs, polls show. But he remains polarizing.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-887d1269-7020-4c8e-8dfc-eae7c464f3cb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e70a485-f72c-4d56-9b7f-a2968fe9d14e">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e70a485-f72c-4d56-9b7f-a2968fe9d14e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Seattle area once had more coronavirus deaths than anywhere else in the United States. A year later, the region’s deaths per capita are lower than any other large metropolitan area.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-becd702f-c674-4653-9a6c-90ee51977e85"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e71516c-8209-4f01-be64-48dd359f8d48">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e71516c-8209-4f01-be64-48dd359f8d48</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president is increasingly fixated on seeing criminal action against his political opponents.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc2c2b47-32c2-43a0-8e5f-dd4e72335932"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e764d8b-1c41-4718-a7e0-a524b4ccaf92">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e764d8b-1c41-4718-a7e0-a524b4ccaf92</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Federal authorities and academics have long described private paramilitary organizations as “militias.” Some critics say the term gives the groups more legitimacy than they deserve.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-17d88f11-8c44-408d-8ac2-945b979b26ce"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e77259a-9d08-4cdf-aaaa-b94e984ccfb2">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e77259a-9d08-4cdf-aaaa-b94e984ccfb2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Hundreds of little-noticed but consequential revisions to the U.S. immigration system will remain in place unless President Biden’s team specifically looks for — and roots out — the changes.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e791a8f-8153-49cc-b3d0-39e6c0a735e5">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e791a8f-8153-49cc-b3d0-39e6c0a735e5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The American Family Plan, which the president wants to pay for by increasing the capital gains tax and the top marginal income tax rate, currently doesn’t include an effort to expand health coverage.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6c995819-c171-430e-a414-f6167b134557"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e7b1d6f-85f5-47d0-9644-bcf02b04bccc">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e7b1d6f-85f5-47d0-9644-bcf02b04bccc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Rising case counts and stagnant vaccination rates could prove equally frustrating for President Biden and the G.O.P., making it impossible to shift the public’s attention to other priorities.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3488268a-8b17-411a-8185-6859abbab9a8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e836071-bb54-45a7-93e3-ad74c047a36f">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e836071-bb54-45a7-93e3-ad74c047a36f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The New York Times asked poets laureate from across the country what the people in their states had to be thankful for in this difficult year.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e8d1de1-145d-475b-9500-4fb80f3a4130">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e8d1de1-145d-475b-9500-4fb80f3a4130</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>For Republicans, anemic fund-raising, missteps by Donald J. Trump and weak candidates could stand in the way of bigger statehouse gains in November.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e8ece99-5714-4e88-bb1e-d41b68fe2b77">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e8ece99-5714-4e88-bb1e-d41b68fe2b77</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Stocks on Wall Street slid on Wednesday, erasing any remaining gains for October. Traders on Wall Street had already been on edge as the presidential election approaches and lawmakers failed to reach an agreement on what economists say is an essential plan to support businesses and out-of-work Americans.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a73d44b5-9249-4d0f-a6d7-7ea3bca69c46"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b07e74a2-0fd9-4722-879f-acf7f5304101"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e9089eb-9fd3-46c4-af95-cee4ac933d72">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e9089eb-9fd3-46c4-af95-cee4ac933d72</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After a court ruling put the state’s six-week abortion ban back into effect, Ms. Abrams said that while economic struggles would come and go, “this law is permanent.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a0f415ea-f8d1-4b12-b0c0-6cb1a91c315d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e9207e2-86f5-4027-82df-5f6ab39d2d79">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e9207e2-86f5-4027-82df-5f6ab39d2d79</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The tight governor’s race in Virginia is a proving ground for strategies that could help determine control of Congress next year.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c2e66850-f7bc-45ca-83ed-c0a1f8490a14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e933a23-d306-4dc0-9e80-53e768fc691e">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e933a23-d306-4dc0-9e80-53e768fc691e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president suggested that the Wisconsin city, which has been roiled by protests and violence this week, had succumbed to “mob rule.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4e96009d-a5ab-4094-a9e3-24c49ed602dc">
		<rdfs:label>article-4e96009d-a5ab-4094-a9e3-24c49ed602dc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A declassified report said a clearer answer would require more information from Beijing or new discoveries and reiterated divisions over natural causes vs. a lab leak.</rdfs:comment>
