	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4fc2b0bb-42b1-4be8-84ad-593a366556ce">
		<rdfs:label>article-4fc2b0bb-42b1-4be8-84ad-593a366556ce</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The latest judge assigned to the long-running death penalty case is based in Virginia and has had a military career focused on defense work, but he has been on the bench for less than two years.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4bd6cfaa-ebec-415a-8c53-2870f770bfa7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4fc3f365-d134-4099-acdc-bdb7fe98f40e">
		<rdfs:label>article-4fc3f365-d134-4099-acdc-bdb7fe98f40e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Americans who are still making up their minds in the presidential contest are weighing a complex set of issues and applying a range of viewpoints to the two candidates. They don’t fit neatly into partisan stereotypes.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-4fc7a7e8-3082-4af5-b4b2-1b3d7b6f331c">
		<rdfs:label>article-4fc7a7e8-3082-4af5-b4b2-1b3d7b6f331c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Executives of the nation’s largest Protestant denomination ignored victims, resisted reforms and were concerned with avoiding ‘potential liability,’ the third-party investigation says.</rdfs:comment>
