		<rdfs:label>article-51475e8a-066a-427c-99f4-061f33ebd57d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>There was a framed copy of the Lilly Ledbetter Fair Pay Act of 2009 on the wall of the chambers of Justice Ruth Bader Ginsburg, who died on Friday. She counted the law among her proudest achievements, even as it illustrated her limited power. As part of the Supreme Court’s four-member liberal wing, she did her most memorable work in dissent.</rdfs:comment>
