	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-571b8f57-33e8-4200-9bae-1a62e4cd6785">
		<rdfs:label>article-571b8f57-33e8-4200-9bae-1a62e4cd6785</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>An internal Trump administration report expects about 200,000 daily cases by June. The White House bars coronavirus task force officials from testifying to Congress without approval.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-571fb8a9-c8b3-4242-a18a-a25b540b97b5">
		<rdfs:label>article-571fb8a9-c8b3-4242-a18a-a25b540b97b5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Republican senator is leaning into her centrist credentials and bipartisan ties in her re-election race, hoping that voters will reward moderation as the G.O.P. has lurched to the right.</rdfs:comment>
