		<rdfs:label>article-584cb3b3-2014-483f-8385-a7058bfb3ce6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Large, simultaneous heat waves are growing more common. China, America, Europe and India have all been stricken recently, and scientists are starting to understand why certain far-flung places get hit at once.</rdfs:comment>
