	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5b9777ec-1c72-4a3a-abe7-3cbdfc93611c">
		<rdfs:label>article-5b9777ec-1c72-4a3a-abe7-3cbdfc93611c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With the pandemic entering a new phase in the United States marked by fewer precautions and the rise of the even more transmissible Omicron subvariant BA.2, the Biden administration has begun stressing the importance of mitigating the risk of indoor aerosol transmission, the primary driver of the pandemic.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e2ba983e-eb48-483d-afa1-e67b02e88f99"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5b9795e9-bf3d-42b1-8771-b9c83e8f4580">
		<rdfs:label>article-5b9795e9-bf3d-42b1-8771-b9c83e8f4580</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>There’s a huge fire debt in the West that must be paid off, experts say, either through controlled burns or out-of-control blazes. Either way, that means smoke.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-34b65400-07ab-404a-9fe3-c1a27b1be114"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5b9b239e-5cbb-49bc-b144-f1b635910e84">
		<rdfs:label>article-5b9b239e-5cbb-49bc-b144-f1b635910e84</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>While Dr. Anthony Fauci has urged caution in using hydroxychloroquine, some doctors are prescribing it to patients who have the virus despite the fact it has never been tested for it.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-922ad7b9-e6de-456a-9bc2-69207748d175"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-db3e2dbf-1da2-4b43-a84d-0db7fa77084d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd42dd7e-7a0d-4a74-908e-252de023edfb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5b9d1c13-6cd7-47d1-abea-c79057bb4987">
		<rdfs:label>article-5b9d1c13-6cd7-47d1-abea-c79057bb4987</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>An investigation found credible evidence of sexual misconduct spanning many years. Several massage therapists made accusations against Mr. Zacharias, who died last spring.</rdfs:comment>
