	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5c46c4c9-0fb1-4572-a62b-14d5c8de83a3">
		<rdfs:label>article-5c46c4c9-0fb1-4572-a62b-14d5c8de83a3</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump’s conduct on Monday evening — leaving Walter Reed hospital despite being infectious and in the relatively early stages of the coronavirus, making a show of taking off his mask before re-entering the White House, and exhorting Americans, “Don’t be afraid of Covid” — struck many health experts as dangerous and irresponsible.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8a614115-3578-4c7f-b70a-6cdd9b0a4f3d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5c46ecac-2ba8-475c-a751-aafd12fcfb4a">
		<rdfs:label>article-5c46ecac-2ba8-475c-a751-aafd12fcfb4a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Federal health officials called for a halt in the use of the company’s coronavirus vaccine while they study serious illnesses that developed in six American women.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3263b980-a580-440f-bdd2-6d7fa7bb3fab"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e4ac7a5-be1a-4937-b91e-66276e5f8dd9"/>
