		<rdfs:comment>The Fort Lauderdale police said that Mr. Parscale’s wife called the authorities to their home because he was armed and threatening to hurt himself.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d0c193d-27cf-4a80-9f85-68363431d053">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d0c193d-27cf-4a80-9f85-68363431d053</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A journal that sits in a staff room just off the intensive care unit at a Milwaukee hospital tells the story of the devastating surge of the coronavirus that much of the country is experiencing. In longhand, the nurses and doctors who are tending to desperately ill Covid-19 patients share their thoughts in the journal, as a way to help one another through this.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f08506e1-4ec6-45c9-9d85-46fe67848dee"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d0fae80-be47-4a24-a730-acda4fca9a62">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d0fae80-be47-4a24-a730-acda4fca9a62</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With two weeks remaining in his re-election campaign, President Trump made the coronavirus his message and Dr. Anthony S. Fauci his foil, dismissing scientific advisers as “these idiots.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e4ac7a5-be1a-4937-b91e-66276e5f8dd9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d14a348-5219-4ca8-9161-3ccc3de29de2">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d14a348-5219-4ca8-9161-3ccc3de29de2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Pete Souza, the former White House photographer-turned-Trump troll, now uses his popular Twitter feed almost exclusively to ridicule Representative Ronny Jackson, the former White House doctor-turned-Trump acolyte.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c67a9047-7b94-4e45-aaa9-c820c2b967de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d176cf4-ce25-4b2b-ad0a-711f0d13bb22">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d176cf4-ce25-4b2b-ad0a-711f0d13bb22</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Complaints have emerged about his oversight of safety measures on previous productions.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-683ee0b4-5d4e-4695-b1d5-c0fdfd233bfa"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e826c370-9468-4832-be86-489a8da40f63"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f7d54296-4f6d-4656-bd4e-ce98de1cb5ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d17c960-fd4c-4b12-9412-ae452b4826e7">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d17c960-fd4c-4b12-9412-ae452b4826e7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Online donors were guided into weekly recurring contributions. Demands for refunds spiked. Complaints to banks and credit card companies soared. But the money helped keep Donald Trump’s struggling campaign afloat.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d192718-3fbd-447b-92f6-fa682dbc4da1">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d192718-3fbd-447b-92f6-fa682dbc4da1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A Supreme Court environmental case being decided this month is the product of a coordinated, multiyear strategy by Republican attorneys general and conservative allies.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c55cfad1-37a4-40de-ab47-b363a537db6a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d197f68-4e21-4bc1-9611-d8b1cb6ba88e">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d197f68-4e21-4bc1-9611-d8b1cb6ba88e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>But the Biden administration is close to finishing a new playbook for counterterrorism strikes outside conventional war zones.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d1b9758-b302-49c9-a9d3-f90a2f2d0e75">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d1b9758-b302-49c9-a9d3-f90a2f2d0e75</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The race comes down to a few critical battlegrounds: This is your morning tip sheet.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-887d1269-7020-4c8e-8dfc-eae7c464f3cb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d22ad3f-da3c-4374-9f3d-abf22650c140">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d22ad3f-da3c-4374-9f3d-abf22650c140</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In new guidance, the Labor Department effectively exempted many small businesses from a new requirement to provide paid leave to employees affected by the crisis.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-31b0603c-dea7-4c16-8a8c-92b47ac393ac"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6c995819-c171-430e-a414-f6167b134557"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d263a3c-c1d5-4736-a3f8-8ff3e2acb13e">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d263a3c-c1d5-4736-a3f8-8ff3e2acb13e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Prices climbed 9.1 percent from a year earlier, ramping up pressure on the Federal Reserve to continue raising interest rates.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-19a7fb6b-a5ad-4f65-8d9c-b053a6ce8ab9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d273d75-eb4e-4873-a2fd-72644efd0ae1">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d273d75-eb4e-4873-a2fd-72644efd0ae1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mr. Jeffries, a Democrat, would be the first Black politician to head a House or Senate caucus for either major party.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d28dff5-a3b2-4d7b-be9e-8457666a403b">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d28dff5-a3b2-4d7b-be9e-8457666a403b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Republicans want to filter out “nuisance” impeachments while Democrats want to demand more evidence.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0e84c75e-7bc1-4744-83f1-7496fcf4721d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d29c3a2-6f64-45f2-8570-211fad01be2b">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d29c3a2-6f64-45f2-8570-211fad01be2b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>If they are confirmed, Ed Gonzalez and Chris Magnus would be responsible for delivering on President Biden’s promise to return compassion to the immigration system.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dad1523a-f983-4f0f-af53-0061c7165e91"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d2cec81-cc25-4d29-8e0b-b1ed3269ab3c">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d2cec81-cc25-4d29-8e0b-b1ed3269ab3c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Trump administration is considering postponing tariff payments on some imported goods for 90 days as part of its response to a faltering economy</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-94d58c04-d925-44a3-9534-35b73b8dc25d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d2dcf02-075d-44ca-aeb5-968993dce040">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d2dcf02-075d-44ca-aeb5-968993dce040</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The biggest worry about Bitcoin is that politicians will start taking it seriously.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45dcdf16-b5a1-43ae-b828-c69e316ccb32"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d33465c-db48-481b-9798-0f96c720c04d">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d33465c-db48-481b-9798-0f96c720c04d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Patience is a virtue that municipal leaders, meditation experts and anyone who has glanced in passing at various Election Day scenarios keep urging voters to embrace. Fine. But easier said than done.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-19a85a44-1ec9-486d-a179-a97a1e8231de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d336aed-5dac-4c34-8eaf-05032184e2bc">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d336aed-5dac-4c34-8eaf-05032184e2bc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The first medical expert called by Derek Chauvin’s defense team said George Floyd died after a combination of factors — including pre-existing heart conditions, drug use and exposure to vehicle exhaust from the police cruiser — caused his death. He faced difficult cross-examination.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-38612bef-d331-4b4e-8a11-2278ecc52a9a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d347eb2-9fb2-4548-be69-b2d2204c9883">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d347eb2-9fb2-4548-be69-b2d2204c9883</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The move is intended to help avoid upending the election as the F.B.I. inadvertently did in 2016 when its campaign inquiries shaped the outcome of the race.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd522e1c-57a0-49bc-9835-fae39d9d58a6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d37def0-893a-4209-809f-ab5cb26bd4ac">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d37def0-893a-4209-809f-ab5cb26bd4ac</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Democratic presidential nominee hit back at attacks delivered at the Republican National Convention.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-577cfa39-5806-4396-ae24-cdf4ba406715"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8eb0923f-854c-4241-9d79-040d1aeeb0c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d3dd66f-8afb-4b03-9190-8ca3bb05dc4d">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d3dd66f-8afb-4b03-9190-8ca3bb05dc4d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With states like California and Texas voting on Tuesday, about one-third of all pledged delegates are up for grabs.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-887d1269-7020-4c8e-8dfc-eae7c464f3cb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d41d888-3109-43b2-a537-0c902959bbc2">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d41d888-3109-43b2-a537-0c902959bbc2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>During breaks, the camera delivering the live feed of the Derek Chauvin trial will often pan away to a copy of the seal that is affixed to the wall behind the judge.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-aa072c75-47e7-4e18-a3b7-fa0a805a8159"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d42bdf4-bfea-40b3-adb5-1fadf5da4bcc">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d42bdf4-bfea-40b3-adb5-1fadf5da4bcc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mark Esper’s comments reflected the turmoil within the military over President Trump, who has said he could put active-duty troops on the streets to perform law enforcement functions.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3bea54bd-f3ee-4712-b704-2739e55e376e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-46b2f3e2-fc43-4d1f-8134-a17365f8ec33"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5a3094b1-6bc7-47d7-8f53-c56fd8ed0c59"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d433485-08de-43c6-8ed0-12872346187b">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d433485-08de-43c6-8ed0-12872346187b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The terror of that day felt palpably real again as senators sitting in judgment of Donald J. Trump were forced to relive the first mass siege of the Capitol since British invaders ransacked the building in 1814.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-922ad7b9-e6de-456a-9bc2-69207748d175"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d45d121-8171-43a6-954d-321d43c6f6bc">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d45d121-8171-43a6-954d-321d43c6f6bc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In a series of public hearings, the House select committee investigating the Jan. 6 attack laid out a powerful account of Mr. Trump’s efforts to overturn the 2020 election. This evidence could allow federal prosecutors, who are conducting a parallel criminal investigation, to indict Mr. Trump.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c67a9047-7b94-4e45-aaa9-c820c2b967de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d470ade-3bb8-413a-9110-c7ef625aefec">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d470ade-3bb8-413a-9110-c7ef625aefec</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>High inflation, food insecurity and a possible global recession loom large as the Group of 20 summit discussions begin.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4b06f805-a6f6-4cda-9908-3f8ddd3a0432"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6c995819-c171-430e-a414-f6167b134557"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d561dcd-c5f4-41a4-b841-4d1c74b80b46">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d561dcd-c5f4-41a4-b841-4d1c74b80b46</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The panel investigating the Capitol attack faced stonewalling from allies of former President Donald J. Trump on two new fronts.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-12-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d56e3a9-3041-48b7-aecd-50292c664141">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d56e3a9-3041-48b7-aecd-50292c664141</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A dire virus warning, and new wrangling over Trump’s tax returns: This is your morning tip sheet.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-887d1269-7020-4c8e-8dfc-eae7c464f3cb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d57685f-c16d-4666-b82d-b10a4ed11340">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d57685f-c16d-4666-b82d-b10a4ed11340</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Similar mandates have gained momentum among both public and private employers as cases have jumped across the country with the spread of the Delta variant.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-738c55e5-1f96-4b93-8c70-fc8c1c8c9119"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d5c792b-21c4-446e-9d16-5cb948f978ef">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d5c792b-21c4-446e-9d16-5cb948f978ef</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Traumatic brain injury is a signature wound of the wars in Iraq and Afghanistan. But the military still has no objective way of diagnosing it in the field.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3bea54bd-f3ee-4712-b704-2739e55e376e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fd9f1ad4-cd49-4185-a0bb-a129097c5a29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5d5c9e13-8bc7-4126-9ae8-d267069f92f4">
		<rdfs:label>article-5d5c9e13-8bc7-4126-9ae8-d267069f92f4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>If the U.S. military withdrawal does not lead to a further descent into chaos in Afghanistan, next-door Pakistan could be the real winner.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-92d6a2c3-4676-4b0a-b692-bac80f669045"/>
