		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5e6539df-a835-4d21-b9d5-eb856a7b2a7f">
		<rdfs:label>article-5e6539df-a835-4d21-b9d5-eb856a7b2a7f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>“What’s the expression — ‘Where’s the beef?’ I need some beef,” Judge Raymond Dearie, the independent arbiter, said during a conference call.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-90788841-2a13-4598-abd3-3b677caff4d4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5e67981b-bcc6-4062-a283-935242273e3f">
		<rdfs:label>article-5e67981b-bcc6-4062-a283-935242273e3f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>More than 1.5 million people are without power across the United States and Canada, and more could lose electricity over the coming days. It’s complicating holiday menus.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a479c8fb-1ce3-4e94-99b3-195a6e3f3e57"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5e6a6290-659e-4215-988b-6fa7ab285428">
		<rdfs:label>article-5e6a6290-659e-4215-988b-6fa7ab285428</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The lawsuit accuses President Biden of overstepping his authority in directing the government to cancel as much as $20,000 in student loan debt for millions of people.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-5e6a8dab-878b-4d2e-b9d4-caf507b3e8d2">
		<rdfs:label>article-5e6a8dab-878b-4d2e-b9d4-caf507b3e8d2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The town along Florida’s east coast suffered severe erosion from Hurricane Ian in September. Now it’s bracing for more.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2be727fb-cf41-4818-994b-9c1be76cc392"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-cba23544-9dbd-4cb6-bff2-605d99ef916d"/>
