	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-602ffd08-7a85-4f6b-a627-08fc88de21cb">
		<rdfs:label>article-602ffd08-7a85-4f6b-a627-08fc88de21cb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Most Confederates were ultimately pardoned for the crime of treason against the United States. Decades later, the Army began honoring them in southern states.</rdfs:comment>
