	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-61516685-5f83-440e-9027-c1542f42edd4">
		<rdfs:label>article-61516685-5f83-440e-9027-c1542f42edd4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>China’s quiet ambivalence about aspects of Russia’s war in Ukraine has long been understood by Moscow, but ties between the two countries remain strong — even if it was notable that President Vladimir V. Putin acknowledged Beijing’s concerns publicly, American officials said Thursday.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6f60db0f-4977-4567-b7bd-9abe5d4a35e8"/>
