	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-62154c15-79a6-4fe1-98d1-03e83e3a9558">
		<rdfs:label>article-62154c15-79a6-4fe1-98d1-03e83e3a9558</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats’ fund-raising blasts filled email boxes and social media feeds as they aimed to capitalize on the fear and alarm that many left-leaning voters felt.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c2e66850-f7bc-45ca-83ed-c0a1f8490a14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-621a2ecd-ebb7-4ed4-b961-abf812ed8b7d">
		<rdfs:label>article-621a2ecd-ebb7-4ed4-b961-abf812ed8b7d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The former attorney general is seeking to win back the Senate seat he held for two decades in a primary contest that has turned into a contest of loyalty to President Trump, who fired him.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ef6cc7eb-b6e8-4dba-84e0-6b42579e91d0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-621a5ee3-ff8b-40ad-8da5-5c33a172c18a">
		<rdfs:label>article-621a5ee3-ff8b-40ad-8da5-5c33a172c18a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Any proposed changes to a century-old recall law are likely to be met with stiff opposition from Republicans, who see it as one of the last avenues of influence in a Democratic-led state.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2bfc1d86-f654-490c-ae5c-efaa41acbbe5"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-67a3c4a4-f876-44f2-8bb0-0eebbb88c77a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-621afcc3-4f41-4dcb-bda5-c2b702cc4c36">
		<rdfs:label>article-621afcc3-4f41-4dcb-bda5-c2b702cc4c36</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Tuesday: Gov. Gavin Newsom said he doesn’t mean “nation-state” literally. But he’s proud of it. Also: Remembering Rosary Celaya Castro-Olega.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-738c55e5-1f96-4b93-8c70-fc8c1c8c9119"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-621ed5b8-ba23-4b30-9e47-cbf457bd4821">
		<rdfs:label>article-621ed5b8-ba23-4b30-9e47-cbf457bd4821</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>“We deplore the desecration of the United States Capitol building, the shedding of innocent blood, the loss of life, and the quagmire of dysfunction that threaten our democracy.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-db01c77c-3043-4daf-9961-68109308c6bc"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-621fa898-682c-4277-9d28-b0a1d21ba539">
		<rdfs:label>article-621fa898-682c-4277-9d28-b0a1d21ba539</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Along with falling short of expectations in the Senate, Democrats also saw their House majority shrink as Republicans made crucial pickups.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-6222d71d-d518-4eea-929e-e0a3ca38aae7">
		<rdfs:label>article-6222d71d-d518-4eea-929e-e0a3ca38aae7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>If President Trump has subjected his predecessor to a thousand paper cuts on Twitter, former President Barack Obama responded on Wednesday night with one grand rhetorical saber stroke, offering one of the most comprehensive denunciations of one president by another in American history.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7479f929-0522-4f1f-a391-dcdb5f4e726c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-62268af5-68c5-4295-a4af-489cabc8ed4b">
		<rdfs:label>article-62268af5-68c5-4295-a4af-489cabc8ed4b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The warning was a notable departure for a Department of Homeland Security accused of being reluctant during the Trump administration to publish intelligence reports or public warnings about the dangers posed by extremists and white supremacist groups.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-62322b8a-aa1b-4b74-a69d-f57852c48fd8">
		<rdfs:label>article-62322b8a-aa1b-4b74-a69d-f57852c48fd8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Even some governors who have been critics of the president are openly grateful for federal supplies. But the administration’s response to the outbreak has still received mixed reviews.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3d0d7757-313d-444e-a4df-32876c51aaa0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d7a0b17f-e0aa-44c5-a995-e81e028fa879"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-6235776d-d322-42fb-b0f1-48ec05d9786f">
		<rdfs:label>article-6235776d-d322-42fb-b0f1-48ec05d9786f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>It’s really, finally, happening. This is your morning tip sheet.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-03"/>
