	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-62b48a04-b0d5-4f26-b5fd-dad4c83992ba">
		<rdfs:label>article-62b48a04-b0d5-4f26-b5fd-dad4c83992ba</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>WILMINGTON, Del. — Joseph R. Biden Jr. and Kamala Harris made their debut as running mates in a high school gymnasium on Wednesday, pledging to lead the country out of the coronavirus crisis.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7da4dfa6-58ba-4b1b-8d80-6c39df820022"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8eb0923f-854c-4241-9d79-040d1aeeb0c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-62b5a673-91d3-4c92-bff0-1d104d995c66">
		<rdfs:label>article-62b5a673-91d3-4c92-bff0-1d104d995c66</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In interviews, Democrats and Republicans had a range of reactions to the state’s Senate debate, including alarm, protectiveness, empathy and worry about the political implications.</rdfs:comment>
