	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-653ebd1d-4480-4321-a10b-b11a551c534b">
		<rdfs:label>article-653ebd1d-4480-4321-a10b-b11a551c534b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Senator James Lankford, an Oklahoma Republican who sits on a key Senate oversight committee, said on a podcast released on Wednesday that he had no objections to President-elect Joseph R. Biden Jr. receiving presidential daily briefings, and that he would take action himself if that did not begin by the end of the week.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8a614115-3578-4c7f-b70a-6cdd9b0a4f3d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-653f19ba-156f-4133-9878-586111775ecf">
		<rdfs:label>article-653f19ba-156f-4133-9878-586111775ecf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The extent of the damage was difficult to comprehend, even for residents who had survived and rebuilt after other powerful storms.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b0d8acac-ba33-4091-b922-0eb5b9ab904d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c27717ae-a4a7-43e2-a892-7d5659d97cf6"/>
