		<rdfs:label>article-68e299a9-d8e8-46f7-ace3-e66bb85e3a94</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>WASHINGTON — A new examination of how Russia used its cybercapabilities in the first months of the war in Ukraine contains a number of surprises: Moscow conducted more cyberattacks than was realized at the time to bolster its invasion, but more than two-thirds of them failed, echoing its poor performance on the physical battlefield.</rdfs:comment>
