	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-6d1d660a-3b7c-4591-8f6f-fb64ec560fa8">
		<rdfs:label>article-6d1d660a-3b7c-4591-8f6f-fb64ec560fa8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Asked by reporters about two issues of deep importance to Democrats, the party’s nominee was circumspect. The Biden campaign later released a fuller statement about Ms. Taylor.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-577cfa39-5806-4396-ae24-cdf4ba406715"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-6d23311e-28cc-49ff-a05a-5abbb4fba458">
		<rdfs:label>article-6d23311e-28cc-49ff-a05a-5abbb4fba458</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Twin emergencies on two coasts this week — Hurricane Isaias and the Apple Fire — offer a preview of life in a warming world and the steady danger of overlapping disasters.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-74659e03-2c48-4140-91f4-08e5d544f77a"/>
