	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-6fdccdc1-b831-43d4-9676-37d5f9dce3e9">
		<rdfs:label>article-6fdccdc1-b831-43d4-9676-37d5f9dce3e9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden is under pressure to redirect the American public’s focus after days of policy whiplash, shifting directives on mask usage, and roiling debates about requiring workers to receive the vaccine.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd42dd7e-7a0d-4a74-908e-252de023edfb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-6fe0ed2f-ec63-40cf-9c0b-cb159bf6d995">
		<rdfs:label>article-6fe0ed2f-ec63-40cf-9c0b-cb159bf6d995</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mr. Barr, then the attorney general, rejected a plea deal days after Mr. Floyd died, worried in part of protesters calling it lenient. Derek Chauvin was set to plead guilty to third-degree murder.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9a5389b6-c0ea-4275-8951-1523cfe86f87"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-10"/>
