		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-6fe3b31b-6849-4051-98d4-fc360d4fcdaa">
		<rdfs:label>article-6fe3b31b-6849-4051-98d4-fc360d4fcdaa</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Stimulus checks may be on their way, but those struggling to get by worry that the money will soon be gone. “Every morning I wake up thinking about where my help is going to come from,” one woman said.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9c6cc67a-b3c2-45c5-af7a-92a423ab1249"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-6fe612e0-e9a6-4e85-b2d1-5419a495ca62">
		<rdfs:label>article-6fe612e0-e9a6-4e85-b2d1-5419a495ca62</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The committee has sought for months to interview Ms. Thomas, the wife of Justice Clarence Thomas, about her involvement in efforts to overturn the 2020 election.</rdfs:comment>
