	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-6ff2b857-ef2a-4f39-86e5-ece846532beb">
		<rdfs:label>article-6ff2b857-ef2a-4f39-86e5-ece846532beb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Republicans hold a narrow majority in the Senate, meaning they can only afford to lose a few votes in their push to confirm a replacement for Justice Ruth Bader Ginsburg. Here are the potential swing votes.</rdfs:comment>
