	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-700bca16-2bbb-48eb-b15d-5ba9146512e6">
		<rdfs:label>article-700bca16-2bbb-48eb-b15d-5ba9146512e6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>It was not quite 30 degrees in Manchester, N.H. — with a wind chill of 19 — but Gov. Chris Sununu looked relieved and happy as the first few health care workers in the state were vaccinated against Covid-19 Tuesday morning outside the Elliot Hospital.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-547aea49-f62b-46fc-b36a-1bb76a5d9284"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-700c19ca-1d5b-47ef-b824-499d60d861ab">
		<rdfs:label>article-700c19ca-1d5b-47ef-b824-499d60d861ab</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The state’s eviction moratorium ends on Thursday.</rdfs:comment>
