	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-71ea5440-f229-4a32-b120-fdb9d65af64c">
		<rdfs:label>article-71ea5440-f229-4a32-b120-fdb9d65af64c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Under impeachment’s arcane rules, senators will submit written queries to be read aloud by the chief justice. Leaders from both parties have strategized for days about what to ask.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-71eccb59-3c38-4b9c-8bfe-610745c4c8c7">
		<rdfs:label>article-71eccb59-3c38-4b9c-8bfe-610745c4c8c7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>For now, the monthly payments apply to 2021 only, although President Biden and some members of Congress hope to extend it for years.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6c995819-c171-430e-a414-f6167b134557"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd42dd7e-7a0d-4a74-908e-252de023edfb"/>
