	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-72a48a7b-fb94-4d43-9ad1-24cbac6ce813">
		<rdfs:label>article-72a48a7b-fb94-4d43-9ad1-24cbac6ce813</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Allegations of bounties paid for the deaths of U.S. soldiers are serious. But the White House ought to stay the course toward a peace deal.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-72ab1099-0647-40a2-8667-68e2215115c5">
		<rdfs:label>article-72ab1099-0647-40a2-8667-68e2215115c5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>House Democrats on Monday rolled out a key plank of President Biden’s stimulus plan, proposing legislation to send direct payments of $1,400 to Americans earning up to $75,000 and households with incomes up to $150,000.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
