	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-788a09cc-32ef-49aa-b505-a8c204794901">
		<rdfs:label>article-788a09cc-32ef-49aa-b505-a8c204794901</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Pete Buttigieg, the transportation secretary, urged Congress on Thursday to make a “generational investment” to improve the nation’s transit and water systems and address climate change and racial inequities, as Democrats began laying the groundwork to pass sweeping infrastructure proposals that could cost $3 trillion to $4 trillion.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-83d40723-6a13-432d-8617-d546a58e6733"/>
