	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-78d981ee-e3a0-4783-9c77-ad592bfad623">
		<rdfs:label>article-78d981ee-e3a0-4783-9c77-ad592bfad623</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In Jackson, residents have long contended with boil-water notices and service disruptions. But now, officials say, the system has been pushed to the brink.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc5a47b7-5e7e-4d58-8ee7-caaf2f703c6a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-78dd86bc-6d1e-4462-ab5b-89763ee466d0">
		<rdfs:label>article-78dd86bc-6d1e-4462-ab5b-89763ee466d0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In an email weeks after the election, another lawyer advising the Trump campaign responded that the prospect of “‘wild’ chaos” on Jan. 6 could lead the Supreme Court to take up a case.</rdfs:comment>
