	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-78ea08ed-202c-447a-8e7e-4aa8cdce4b94">
		<rdfs:label>article-78ea08ed-202c-447a-8e7e-4aa8cdce4b94</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A bipartisan group of governors decided to flex its muscle and get students back into classrooms, despite union resistance and bureaucratic hesitancy.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9ef20237-f390-44c5-8d52-031cdd2c86e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-78ec0088-f131-440e-ba4d-1d65c923e777">
		<rdfs:label>article-78ec0088-f131-440e-ba4d-1d65c923e777</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>If Justice Thomas is genuinely concerned about the eroding faith in his own institution, the first thing he can do is look in the mirror.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fda4452b-3825-4a26-bbb4-46f458379b68"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-78ecfcc1-eba4-47af-98b9-0be558bf6eb8">
		<rdfs:label>article-78ecfcc1-eba4-47af-98b9-0be558bf6eb8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Immediately after the attack on the U.S. Capitol, all corners of the political spectrum repudiated the mob of President Trump’s supporters. Yet within days, prominent Republicans, party officials, conservative media voices and rank-and-file voters began making a rhetorical shift to try to downplay the group’s violent actions.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4504805-5b5f-41c7-b157-41ff04a342ad"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-78ee020e-a913-453a-9315-c99b9ac49ac9">
		<rdfs:label>article-78ee020e-a913-453a-9315-c99b9ac49ac9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>What if early results in swing states on Nov. 3 show President Trump ahead, and he declares victory before heavily Democratic mail-in votes, which he has falsely linked with fraud, are fully counted?</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c2e66850-f7bc-45ca-83ed-c0a1f8490a14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-78ee380f-8026-40b9-b2dd-f9c94b8c4e7d">
		<rdfs:label>article-78ee380f-8026-40b9-b2dd-f9c94b8c4e7d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The White House wants more money for treatments, tests, vaccines and research, but Republicans in Congress insist the administration will have to repurpose existing funds.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-78eea1ec-02b6-4953-b89a-c94b5a0e1e27">
		<rdfs:label>article-78eea1ec-02b6-4953-b89a-c94b5a0e1e27</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president informed the National Archives that it should turn over the logs sought by the Jan. 6 committee within 15 days.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2c183a13-1898-4deb-ad56-cc02fd034eaf"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-78eedfb2-7f56-4f02-9460-0d480664e493">
		<rdfs:label>article-78eedfb2-7f56-4f02-9460-0d480664e493</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Two House committees were so concerned by the explanation that they requested an array of internal documents related to the reports on sexual misconduct and domestic violence.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e0dfbf0e-c179-4f28-a968-4570f9209555"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-78fbd1bf-68d2-4f31-831a-ce57a8b7f855">
		<rdfs:label>article-78fbd1bf-68d2-4f31-831a-ce57a8b7f855</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Officials said they objected to the inclusion of social-emotional learning and critical race theory in the books but did not share information on the specific content.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b84d8bda-1ee4-435d-8105-15b48a6a482f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-79026d4b-d9d8-42a4-8bf7-8ddb06bf597c">
		<rdfs:label>article-79026d4b-d9d8-42a4-8bf7-8ddb06bf597c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Millions of Americans in trouble can’t wait while lawmakers take the rest of the summer off.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-79037f17-5aa1-49ec-87ec-ed374ec6ce2a">
		<rdfs:label>article-79037f17-5aa1-49ec-87ec-ed374ec6ce2a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Senate candidate keeps telling puzzling stories about his poultry business.</rdfs:comment>
