		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7ac97edb-f018-4cfc-92dd-3f5ad6f6f5bf">
		<rdfs:label>article-7ac97edb-f018-4cfc-92dd-3f5ad6f6f5bf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With the threat of the pandemic all but banished from its shores, New Zealand approached the holiday season much as it ordinarily does.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b8a76374-cc93-49e2-8cd7-2af40aec7022"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7acebeaa-164d-4b67-b234-0eb185a75ea9">
		<rdfs:label>article-7acebeaa-164d-4b67-b234-0eb185a75ea9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Senate’s plan is flawed. Doing nothing would be much worse.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7acf3dc0-4be7-4b29-8b2c-ce7fb2c639e3">
		<rdfs:label>article-7acf3dc0-4be7-4b29-8b2c-ce7fb2c639e3</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>How both sides are choosing the people who will make their case before the Senate.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e4ac7a5-be1a-4937-b91e-66276e5f8dd9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7ad3775e-c9a2-457e-ae4b-15416d533e26">
		<rdfs:label>article-7ad3775e-c9a2-457e-ae4b-15416d533e26</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As paid family leave and other priorities were taken out of the president’s plan, the largest piece became a $555 billion plan to fight climate change.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c55cfad1-37a4-40de-ab47-b363a537db6a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7ad953b9-4a2e-4e80-9a61-a7a8bf31ae7b">
		<rdfs:label>article-7ad953b9-4a2e-4e80-9a61-a7a8bf31ae7b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>On topics from climate change to leadership, most Americans say they prefer Joe Biden over President Trump.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-887d1269-7020-4c8e-8dfc-eae7c464f3cb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7ada40b1-a2e5-4fbe-903a-4b6cfede3f04">
		<rdfs:label>article-7ada40b1-a2e5-4fbe-903a-4b6cfede3f04</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>White House officials dismiss criticism that President Biden’s comments on booster shots amount to undue pressure on public health experts.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7adaa5b5-4bd0-4e82-b1ae-4736632bc8e9">
		<rdfs:label>article-7adaa5b5-4bd0-4e82-b1ae-4736632bc8e9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>North Dakota’s top election official said on Wednesday that it was too late to remove from the ballot the name of a candidate for State Legislature who died Monday from Covid-19.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4bd1aa5-c807-421e-b8ae-1b3824d70300"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7adddf6b-8a1d-4548-ac5d-f032eedc3558">
		<rdfs:label>article-7adddf6b-8a1d-4548-ac5d-f032eedc3558</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>When Senator Ted Cruz of Texas spoke with President Trump on the phone last week, he congratulated him on his debate performance, nudged him to keep driving policy-oriented attacks against his opponent, Joseph R. Biden Jr., and relayed one more message.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7ae7beff-13b3-4128-91e9-223cad746263">
		<rdfs:label>article-7ae7beff-13b3-4128-91e9-223cad746263</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>At beaches, seaside arcades and other attractions, many people hoped to turn the page from the past few months. Still, moving past the pandemic is a long way off.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-48e200fd-02da-4ffc-8666-066f9561a258"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ea9dbbc7-267d-46dd-9bad-620f876af0ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7aec85c4-1ad3-4f4c-9075-9a5c5202f3fd">
		<rdfs:label>article-7aec85c4-1ad3-4f4c-9075-9a5c5202f3fd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With inflation, war and the pandemic looming larger, Democrats who hope that the browbeating of Ketanji Brown Jackson will rally Black voters behind their candidates may be disappointed.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-803bdb8f-8c3c-4210-80c9-22b0af3fd2ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a0f415ea-f8d1-4b12-b0c0-6cb1a91c315d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7aed454b-a0e3-4713-97d2-99425548afd8">
		<rdfs:label>article-7aed454b-a0e3-4713-97d2-99425548afd8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Education Secretary Betsy DeVos has informed Congress that she will not seek to grant waivers from special education requirements under federal law.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b782e9c4-4c0a-4c6c-aa6e-ee0fb7623560"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7aedab95-e018-4007-a9f5-9e693c40bc4a">
		<rdfs:label>article-7aedab95-e018-4007-a9f5-9e693c40bc4a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president is also considering deploying warships and aircraft to NATO allies, in what would be a major shift from its restrained stance on Ukraine.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-46b2f3e2-fc43-4d1f-8134-a17365f8ec33"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5a3094b1-6bc7-47d7-8f53-c56fd8ed0c59"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7af0f8a4-a82d-4daf-a00b-bf18e495035c">
		<rdfs:label>article-7af0f8a4-a82d-4daf-a00b-bf18e495035c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Health officials say rising case counts are fueled in part by more contagious coronavirus variants, particularly B.1.1.7, the variant first found in Britain.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-456258fe-24f9-4e37-a244-c99808a00014"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7af28bae-4fe9-4256-888c-e18d984f2ce5">
		<rdfs:label>article-7af28bae-4fe9-4256-888c-e18d984f2ce5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Federal Reserve will backstop credit markets through 2020, and is expected to pledge continued economic help at its Wednesday meeting.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-19a7fb6b-a5ad-4f65-8d9c-b053a6ce8ab9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7af3c273-d593-4584-97c2-f9aef6b09003">
		<rdfs:label>article-7af3c273-d593-4584-97c2-f9aef6b09003</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>While most arrests in the Capitol riot have been individuals, new charges accused three people tied to a right-wing militia of conspiring to commit violence.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-17d88f11-8c44-408d-8ac2-945b979b26ce"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3a4b0b1a-f7a7-498e-8805-48a907d13871"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7af71261-98eb-4af8-b8be-128ef0313091">
		<rdfs:label>article-7af71261-98eb-4af8-b8be-128ef0313091</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The disclosure was the latest involving aggressive steps the Justice Department took in leak inquiries late in the Trump administration.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7af71b86-74d2-4531-b753-23afbe1cba23">
		<rdfs:label>article-7af71b86-74d2-4531-b753-23afbe1cba23</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The attorney general accused several companies by name of appeasing an authoritarian government to preserve access to a huge consumer market.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7afaf6b8-8812-4df0-b0d4-8f52f7bf872f">
		<rdfs:label>article-7afaf6b8-8812-4df0-b0d4-8f52f7bf872f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Students who were in the classroom with the gunman called 911 several times, including a lengthy call during which some shooting and other sounds of the attack could be heard, according to Steven McCraw, director of the Texas Department of Public Safety.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8cddda8e-bf27-443d-ab88-1512a3ebc5de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7afb5d1a-4130-45fa-8157-65bebfa8bc68">
		<rdfs:label>article-7afb5d1a-4130-45fa-8157-65bebfa8bc68</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The former vice president was the first of several prominent Republicans who will visit before Election Day in support of Mr. Kemp.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a0f415ea-f8d1-4b12-b0c0-6cb1a91c315d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7afc6afd-56bc-43b0-aeee-dabf89c5febb">
		<rdfs:label>article-7afc6afd-56bc-43b0-aeee-dabf89c5febb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The police in Austin, Texas, have not identified the motorist who fatally shot a protester after driving his car in the direction of marchers.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-781f7c76-864b-4901-8b16-90c83d96e113"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fd2d6ec4-4aa3-452f-8e17-99a953af7b67"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7afd8ab9-7f9c-4c64-afa8-8703b6f122f1">
		<rdfs:label>article-7afd8ab9-7f9c-4c64-afa8-8703b6f122f1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The F.B.I. scored two major victories, recovering a Bitcoin ransom and tricking lawbreakers with an encryption app. But criminals may still have the upper hand.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2c183a13-1898-4deb-ad56-cc02fd034eaf"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-98b172aa-f38f-48e7-9579-8bc1078c88f1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7b06a999-ecb2-4f20-a7ac-551b52225a51">
		<rdfs:label>article-7b06a999-ecb2-4f20-a7ac-551b52225a51</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The West Virginia Democrat’s decision dealt a crushing blow to President Biden’s domestic agenda, effectively ruling out action on anything beyond prescription drug pricing and health care subsidies.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b1afb246-66b2-4eea-8ebc-1b5c7f6c7900"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7b0728eb-59b9-4b4e-bc3d-2391c682a191">
		<rdfs:label>article-7b0728eb-59b9-4b4e-bc3d-2391c682a191</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In Northern California, a region troubled by fire, many people with disabilities live in rural areas that lack the resources to support them during disasters.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0a19ff37-a276-4081-944e-e43f9f3234c8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7b073f8c-a34b-45c2-9551-c84f3e2fbf73">
		<rdfs:label>article-7b073f8c-a34b-45c2-9551-c84f3e2fbf73</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A small circle of Republican lawmakers, working closely with President Donald J. Trump’s chief of staff, took on an outsize role in pressuring the Justice Department, amplifying conspiracy theories and flooding the courts in an attempt to overturn the 2020 election.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-90788841-2a13-4598-abd3-3b677caff4d4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd522e1c-57a0-49bc-9835-fae39d9d58a6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-12-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7b0b0acb-10d3-41bd-9e9b-bce7ce7dd584">
		<rdfs:label>article-7b0b0acb-10d3-41bd-9e9b-bce7ce7dd584</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The department’s leaders declined to publish a memo describing Russian attempts to question Joseph R. Biden Jr.’s health, prompting new scrutiny of political influence at the department.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7b0e826e-03f3-4593-b40c-0b19f84e6871">
		<rdfs:label>article-7b0e826e-03f3-4593-b40c-0b19f84e6871</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Delaware Democrat, who once interned for President Biden, is now his main conduit to senators in both parties who hold the key to moving his agenda.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7b0eda15-fad6-4c98-a00b-47667eb51dec">
		<rdfs:label>article-7b0eda15-fad6-4c98-a00b-47667eb51dec</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Election deniers’ doubts about voting made for compelling conspiracy theories, but proved to be a bad get-out-the-vote strategy.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-93d154d3-6d3d-4599-ac55-e63a146d8d6f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-982bde63-8146-432c-a09a-c9cac220ddaa"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7b1037b6-529a-46a9-a6d6-883d674a750a">
		<rdfs:label>article-7b1037b6-529a-46a9-a6d6-883d674a750a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>While Democrats celebrated the election of the Rev. Raphael Warnock to the Senate, Georgia’s second Senate runoff race — which will determine which party will control the Senate — remained too close to call on Wednesday. The Democratic candidate, Jon Ossoff, was leading his Republican challenger, David Perdue, by thousands of votes with thousands more that still need to be counted, many of them from Democratic-leaning areas.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dad1523a-f983-4f0f-af53-0061c7165e91"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
