	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7befd52e-8b93-4786-a394-59a9ca4b1f74">
		<rdfs:label>article-7befd52e-8b93-4786-a394-59a9ca4b1f74</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The $1.9 trillion package is a big bet by the party that it will restore a sense of normalcy by the 2022 elections and that voters will defy history and reward Democrats with more seats in Congress.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7bf25fb2-0a70-412b-819e-e111104ed3b1">
		<rdfs:label>article-7bf25fb2-0a70-412b-819e-e111104ed3b1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Even a large state that emphasized vaccinations in combating the coronavirus can be crushed by the Delta variant when no other measures are put in place.</rdfs:comment>
