		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-7ffcdc46-a6df-4328-8aae-d2b6eccce52d">
		<rdfs:label>article-7ffcdc46-a6df-4328-8aae-d2b6eccce52d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Shortly after the last U.S. troops left Afghanistan, the secretary of state outlined a plan to use diplomacy to try to extract remaining Americans and Afghan allies.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-80042cc3-4ada-4e1c-b1a5-284903bec5ba">
		<rdfs:label>article-80042cc3-4ada-4e1c-b1a5-284903bec5ba</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>When Georgia’s Senate runoff polls close tonight, elections officials will begin reporting three sets of vote totals: 2.1 million cast at in-person early-voting sites, 1 million cast by mail and those cast at Election Day precincts, a figure that officials estimate could be anywhere from 500,000 to 800,000.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-80069147-6e0f-4b5d-90a1-c22bd5349b21">
		<rdfs:label>article-80069147-6e0f-4b5d-90a1-c22bd5349b21</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The man accused of walking into a King Soopers grocery store in Boulder, Colo., on Monday and killing 10 people was armed with a military-style semiautomatic rifle and a pistol, law enforcement officials said.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0d6427ef-da1b-4d64-8c55-4f2b53f3bd95"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-524922c4-c335-4218-b145-d4752931be34"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-70fc2fbe-5dc6-43cd-9be6-39b7edf94c07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-8008b8a7-05bb-4196-b58a-233a8f013508">
		<rdfs:label>article-8008b8a7-05bb-4196-b58a-233a8f013508</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Energy Department on Wednesday announced a new effort to tackle one of the toughest technical challenges facing President Biden’s push for an electric grid dominated by solar and wind power — namely, what to do when the sun stops shining and the wind stops blowing.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d8148593-227b-4889-ae70-592b440737ae"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-801012d6-2aca-4980-9718-a2faf819f119">
		<rdfs:label>article-801012d6-2aca-4980-9718-a2faf819f119</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President-elect Joseph R. Biden Jr. on Wednesday formally introduced Pete Buttigieg as his nominee for transportation secretary, a role that will be key to advancing Mr. Biden’s ambitious agenda on rebuilding the nation’s infrastructure and on climate change.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7da4dfa6-58ba-4b1b-8d80-6c39df820022"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dad1523a-f983-4f0f-af53-0061c7165e91"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-80116d4f-d5e9-4d6f-a499-408b9f08aa03">
		<rdfs:label>article-80116d4f-d5e9-4d6f-a499-408b9f08aa03</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Voters and poll workers in Texas will be required to wear masks at election precincts after a federal judge blocked the governor, a Republican, from exempting them.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4bd1aa5-c807-421e-b8ae-1b3824d70300"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-801327ae-3444-404b-b09f-d14950e29b47">
		<rdfs:label>article-801327ae-3444-404b-b09f-d14950e29b47</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With the pandemic heading into its third year, much of the money that Congress has allocated for coronavirus response has been spent.</rdfs:comment>
