	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81a444d8-115e-4d3f-9e35-3ced695fa1d9">
		<rdfs:label>article-81a444d8-115e-4d3f-9e35-3ced695fa1d9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Investigators believe a woman with a background in military counterintelligence was sent to Texas to recruit migrants for the flights to Martha’s Vineyard.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81a4ab56-31eb-46f5-94cb-34c0f02268d0">
		<rdfs:label>article-81a4ab56-31eb-46f5-94cb-34c0f02268d0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A new study finds that if fossil fuel emissions continue apace, the oceans could experience a mass extinction by 2300. There is still time to avoid it.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2afe2750-7a7d-460f-b9fb-4feddaf4f58b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81a5e6a5-c5f5-4152-8fb9-0a70886c4d14">
		<rdfs:label>article-81a5e6a5-c5f5-4152-8fb9-0a70886c4d14</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After sporting events were canceled in Iowa, Mark Woodley was pressed into service covering the storm. “I didn’t realize that there was a 3:30 also in the morning until today,” he said.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2be727fb-cf41-4818-994b-9c1be76cc392"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81a62160-a4c0-4084-b707-7b981abcf2b0">
		<rdfs:label>article-81a62160-a4c0-4084-b707-7b981abcf2b0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A series of strong special election showings, culminating in a New York win, have buoyed Democratic confidence, but a daunting map may still cost them the House.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-803bdb8f-8c3c-4210-80c9-22b0af3fd2ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81a7bdf1-c23b-4529-b1e4-6ee04ccba740">
		<rdfs:label>article-81a7bdf1-c23b-4529-b1e4-6ee04ccba740</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Donald Harris and Shyamala Gopalan grew up under British colonial rule on different sides of the planet. They were each drawn to Berkeley, and became part of an intellectual circle that shaped the rest of their lives.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-91caa243-6ff4-4c6d-affc-51bd8da8617d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81ab1db0-34c0-444c-a40a-c72639c7d9fa">
		<rdfs:label>article-81ab1db0-34c0-444c-a40a-c72639c7d9fa</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As climate change opens up the Arctic for transit and exploration, Russia has increasingly militarized the region. The U.S. is preparing a more aggressive presence of its own.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-becd702f-c674-4653-9a6c-90ee51977e85"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81aea5e5-c8ed-4416-b9ba-ab37a49738f4">
		<rdfs:label>article-81aea5e5-c8ed-4416-b9ba-ab37a49738f4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>For two months, Michael Bloomberg’s campaign has been preparing for a moment it knew would come: when decades of impolitic and insensitive remarks would face renewed scrutiny.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ef6cc7eb-b6e8-4dba-84e0-6b42579e91d0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81aeb3dd-a7d8-4141-83a2-ce09be84be8e">
		<rdfs:label>article-81aeb3dd-a7d8-4141-83a2-ce09be84be8e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>His voting over the years was generally similar to that of other Democratic appointees, if perhaps a little more conservative.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-947ed571-ad87-49fb-b59a-9372d166d3c7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81b1bab3-12a8-4a23-a9ce-1fa264cc51b6">
		<rdfs:label>article-81b1bab3-12a8-4a23-a9ce-1fa264cc51b6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A federal judge ruled on Tuesday that Texas’ procedure for reviewing — and in some cases rejecting — mail-in ballots was unconstitutional and ordered the state to change its process before Election Day.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-577cfa39-5806-4396-ae24-cdf4ba406715"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81b3044d-f868-4c6a-a69d-790dcec66f4a">
		<rdfs:label>article-81b3044d-f868-4c6a-a69d-790dcec66f4a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Trump campaign is spending millions on ads that promote a dark and exaggerated portrayal of Democratic-led cities, a tactic that reinforces his “law and order’’ campaign message.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-93d154d3-6d3d-4599-ac55-e63a146d8d6f"/>
