		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81befc14-9687-4219-80b4-4a3e5a74d005">
		<rdfs:label>article-81befc14-9687-4219-80b4-4a3e5a74d005</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Most egregious nepo couple, most stylish exit, top con man and more.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd146215-8c12-40b0-bfb7-0d9c07c5e63d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81bf6777-0ce4-4db6-a833-9015fcfc8fee">
		<rdfs:label>article-81bf6777-0ce4-4db6-a833-9015fcfc8fee</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democratic candidates are either avoiding border issues or talking about them on Republicans’ terms. And the party’s grass-roots allies are struggling for cash and battling burnout.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6fcc2118-4d59-415b-8f82-fd519f6b2d34"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81c1f93d-2b12-4c89-9eaf-42f3bcd96539">
		<rdfs:label>article-81c1f93d-2b12-4c89-9eaf-42f3bcd96539</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>There is not much data yet from polls conducted after the final presidential debate, but what there is shows no real sign of movement. With the clock ticking down, that is good news for Joseph R. Biden Jr. and unwelcome news for President Trump.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-17ddcb21-b8ba-45a7-8e71-073c17f7026b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81c2db72-89b2-4f8a-91e1-865bc3760ce2">
		<rdfs:label>article-81c2db72-89b2-4f8a-91e1-865bc3760ce2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Cases are rising again in parts of the country, but more people are traveling, and health officials have largely stopped telling people to skip celebrations.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-de093669-b27a-4345-ac65-683caba65a27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81c4719f-6c58-4174-8c60-b8a96d118af3">
		<rdfs:label>article-81c4719f-6c58-4174-8c60-b8a96d118af3</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A witness broke down in sobs as he recounted his memory of George Floyd’s arrest. Jurors watched the fatal incident from the perspective of the police officers’ body cameras.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-38612bef-d331-4b4e-8a11-2278ecc52a9a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81c4bf37-4798-4cc3-8cb2-e815dbf3e6a8">
		<rdfs:label>article-81c4bf37-4798-4cc3-8cb2-e815dbf3e6a8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As polls show President Trump significantly trailing his rival, Joseph R. Biden Jr., his campaign is spending heavily in states, like Ohio, that it had hoped would not be competitive at all this year.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3488268a-8b17-411a-8185-6859abbab9a8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81c7b8fa-b7e0-4ed8-abfa-5c8126519421">
		<rdfs:label>article-81c7b8fa-b7e0-4ed8-abfa-5c8126519421</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A day after a key Senate official ruled that a provision increasing the federal minimum wage would need to be removed as written from President Biden’s $1.9 trillion stimulus plan, Democrats were scrambling to salvage the critical progressive priority.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81cb6e14-f761-4949-bfa2-366f06748d45">
		<rdfs:label>article-81cb6e14-f761-4949-bfa2-366f06748d45</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Hours after body camera video of the killing was released, protesters gathered outside the Brooklyn Center police station despite a new curfew for much of the Twin Cities region.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-204cd1d8-9d72-4785-968e-7d68ce7d17d7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3d0d7757-313d-444e-a4df-32876c51aaa0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e993acb7-fd71-489b-b569-b6b6d449dfe5"/>
