	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81dc6eaf-3005-4a30-8343-4eefd25719c2">
		<rdfs:label>article-81dc6eaf-3005-4a30-8343-4eefd25719c2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Gov. Greg Abbott of Texas on Tuesday called a special session of the Texas Legislature that will begin on July 8, a move that revives Republicans’ effort to enact what are expected to be some of the most far-reaching voting restrictions in the country.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-93d154d3-6d3d-4599-ac55-e63a146d8d6f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-81de1143-8eac-4334-9dc9-08a27eb24899">
		<rdfs:label>article-81de1143-8eac-4334-9dc9-08a27eb24899</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Depleting emergency oil reserves spurs criticism that the White House is trying to lower gas prices with midterm election politics in mind.</rdfs:comment>
