	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-827653ed-0066-423e-82c6-25fbffd3f640">
		<rdfs:label>article-827653ed-0066-423e-82c6-25fbffd3f640</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In a highly unusual legal maneuver, the Justice Department moved on Tuesday to replace President Trump’s private lawyers and defend him against a defamation lawsuit brought in state court by the author E. Jean Carroll, who has accused him of raping her in a Manhattan department store in the 1990s.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-90788841-2a13-4598-abd3-3b677caff4d4"/>
