		<rdfs:comment>Future Forward, a relatively new Democratic super PAC, made waves this summer when it booked $20 million in television advertisements for the final five weeks of the election cycle. That number has since increased to $57 million, and the group aired its first ads of the fall sprint on Tuesday, including one that focused on the coronavirus pandemic.</rdfs:comment>
