	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-85e2271b-858c-4aee-880c-2ba443a755b5">
		<rdfs:label>article-85e2271b-858c-4aee-880c-2ba443a755b5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>HONG KONG — China’s state news media reacted with cautious optimism to former Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr.’s victory in the United States’ presidential election, expressing hope that he would stabilize the fast-deteriorating relations between the two countries.</rdfs:comment>
