	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-88d76c87-7966-43c1-ae68-7f45c91c0cbf">
		<rdfs:label>article-88d76c87-7966-43c1-ae68-7f45c91c0cbf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>More than three decades after his first presidential run, in the midst of a deadly pandemic and without his son Beau at his side, the former vice president has met his moment.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f33dc887-a9a6-4b4f-adce-fc81b6f27a0c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-88d7f9e4-3e5b-427e-b6c6-2b4f55eac9a5">
		<rdfs:label>article-88d7f9e4-3e5b-427e-b6c6-2b4f55eac9a5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In April, a jury found El Shafee Elsheikh guilty on four counts of hostage-taking and four counts of conspiracy after a two-week trial.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3a4b0b1a-f7a7-498e-8805-48a907d13871"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7479f929-0522-4f1f-a391-dcdb5f4e726c"/>
