	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-88f7e873-d2cf-4d40-91fb-a7ed82928c52">
		<rdfs:label>article-88f7e873-d2cf-4d40-91fb-a7ed82928c52</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>For our podcast The Run-Up, Astead Herndon and his team are talking with voters of all stripes. For many of them, frustration with politics is tied to their worries about democracy.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e9c4025-7dbe-4808-a3d4-b9d25fa14354"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-88f9a098-ea94-4b1c-9912-a882c1fc9806">
		<rdfs:label>article-88f9a098-ea94-4b1c-9912-a882c1fc9806</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden’s nominee for attorney general told the Senate Judiciary Committee that investigating the Capitol riot would be his first priority.</rdfs:comment>
