	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-892b1714-86aa-4b3b-b511-17635cfb526b">
		<rdfs:label>article-892b1714-86aa-4b3b-b511-17635cfb526b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>More than one out of every 10 flights in the United States was affected by the winter weather on Thursday.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-892b7478-bbad-4fbb-a9a8-7de4cbdc24b2">
		<rdfs:label>article-892b7478-bbad-4fbb-a9a8-7de4cbdc24b2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Urban transportation is central to the effort to slow climate change. It can’t be done by just switching to electric cars. Several cities are starting to electrify mass transit.</rdfs:comment>
