	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-8a138e54-33d8-46d4-b03e-e08af07af550">
		<rdfs:label>article-8a138e54-33d8-46d4-b03e-e08af07af550</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The impeachment of President Trump for a second time — in a Capitol ringed by troops — seemed like the almost inevitable culmination of four years that left the nation fractured, angry and losing its sense of self.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-922ad7b9-e6de-456a-9bc2-69207748d175"/>
