		<rdfs:label>article-8ad54bf3-1325-4032-bd03-675df1211d38</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Republican state senators overseeing a review of the 2020 election in Arizona’s most populous county must make public the records of private companies hired to conduct the audit, a county judge ruled on Thursday, emphatically rejecting a bid by the senators to keep the documents secret.</rdfs:comment>
