	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-8b0f59a5-2c09-4960-9f67-7f227d52dc89">
		<rdfs:label>article-8b0f59a5-2c09-4960-9f67-7f227d52dc89</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mr. Allen, a retired four-star general, had been on administrative leave amid a federal inquiry into whether he had secretly lobbied for the government of Qatar.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4ba1c7ec-56dd-4804-9436-b85ef07cc18e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-8b166666-92c4-4f30-88ae-45565b428f91">
		<rdfs:label>article-8b166666-92c4-4f30-88ae-45565b428f91</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Since Russia’s invasion of Ukraine, Pentagon officials have sent the Ukrainian military an array of equipment totaling billions of dollars. But one powerful weapon, called the Army Tactical Missile System, has become part of a debate about the limits of U.S. support for its ally.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-524922c4-c335-4218-b145-d4752931be34"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-8b1c1c71-9040-4f89-b7bd-4f61ac9fa216">
		<rdfs:label>article-8b1c1c71-9040-4f89-b7bd-4f61ac9fa216</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>From voting rights to the culture wars, state legislatures controlled by Republicans are playing a role well beyond their own state borders.</rdfs:comment>
