		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-8fccfbd2-9a5e-4bfa-a2fd-906f60a02392">
		<rdfs:label>article-8fccfbd2-9a5e-4bfa-a2fd-906f60a02392</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The editorial board of The Wall Street Journal, the American flagship of Rupert Murdoch’s newspaper empire, denounced President Trump on Thursday for inciting a mob of his supporters to storm the U.S. Capitol, declaring his behavior “impeachable” and encouraging Mr. Trump to resign his office to prevent a second impeachment by the Democratic-controlled House.</rdfs:comment>
