	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-8fd10098-20a6-4ab3-91a9-c1639205cccf">
		<rdfs:label>article-8fd10098-20a6-4ab3-91a9-c1639205cccf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Even as scores of President Trump’s usually unfailing loyalists condemned him for failing to call off the swarm of lawless demonstrators storming and ransacking the Capitol, many of his most vocal and visible defenders still could not bring themselves to fault the president for the surreal and frightening attack carried out in his name.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ef6cc7eb-b6e8-4dba-84e0-6b42579e91d0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-8fd124dc-d5ee-4646-b86a-be0b3bbab75b">
		<rdfs:label>article-8fd124dc-d5ee-4646-b86a-be0b3bbab75b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Even after his retirement a decade ago, the former pope remained the unofficial figurehead of the conservative wing of the American church.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-1f4003c3-78bb-4191-901d-febdb359732e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c9e39358-a975-42ba-a74a-ab413e845336"/>
