		<rdfs:label>article-921245b3-4694-4d26-97a1-1302d0655af6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The sergeants-at-arms of the Senate and House, Michael C. Stenger and Paul D. Irving, have resigned from their posts and are now facing intense scrutiny over the security failure last week that led to the deadly siege of the Capitol, its first occupation since the War of 1812.</rdfs:comment>
