		<rdfs:label>article-970b22be-3747-4c12-acf4-a661b060c6e6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>People with low incomes who are eligible to vote are much less likely to do so in national elections than those with higher incomes, and are more often constrained from casting ballots by transportation issues, illness or other problems out of their control, according to a study released Tuesday by the Poor People’s Campaign.</rdfs:comment>
