		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9788013b-ace7-4639-a36f-c15f6a2f31b5">
		<rdfs:label>article-9788013b-ace7-4639-a36f-c15f6a2f31b5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Speaking in Tulsa, Okla., a day after the Juneteenth holiday, the president mocked the coronavirus that has killed 121,000 Americans and claimed he wanted to slow down testing.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-978c80e2-99f1-4a48-9c73-eeb44779266c">
		<rdfs:label>article-978c80e2-99f1-4a48-9c73-eeb44779266c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With immigration leveling off and a declining birthrate, the United States may be entering an era of substantially lower population growth, demographers said.</rdfs:comment>
