	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-97cf16aa-e257-4e2b-9dea-f91b4f907117">
		<rdfs:label>article-97cf16aa-e257-4e2b-9dea-f91b4f907117</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>WASHINGTON — The Biden administration is planning to give Americans age 50 or older the option of a second booster of the Pfizer-BioNTech or Moderna coronavirus vaccine without recommending outright that they get one, according to several people familiar with the plan.</rdfs:comment>
