		<rdfs:label>article-987a705b-76ac-4f0f-8db4-72a234d04c17</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Two Republican senators on the pivotal Judiciary Committee have tested positive for the coronavirus after attending White House events last week announcing President Trump’s nominee for the Supreme Court, Judge Amy Coney Barrett, throwing the future of her Supreme Court confirmation hearings into question.</rdfs:comment>
