		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dbfbae54-8da6-457d-b696-ea1216a321d5"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9b4e0bcc-ce63-4818-8d00-6e4749650154">
		<rdfs:label>article-9b4e0bcc-ce63-4818-8d00-6e4749650154</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>College in a pandemic was not the experience that most students had in mind. But at year’s end, some see positive experiences and insights that came out of it.</rdfs:comment>
