		<rdfs:label>article-9c68c211-a71a-4c4f-a85c-b158310cd4d7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Republican lawmakers in Texas, following in the footsteps of their counterparts across the country, are pressing forward with a voting bill that could impose harsh penalties on election officials or poll workers who are thought to have committed errors or violations. And the nationwide effort may be pushing poll workers to reconsider serving their communities.</rdfs:comment>
