		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9cb07331-1d6d-4ec5-923d-37d737c7355a">
		<rdfs:label>article-9cb07331-1d6d-4ec5-923d-37d737c7355a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As Democrats ponder cutting a $3.5 trillion social safety net bill down to perhaps $2 trillion, a proposal to limit programs to the poor has rekindled a debate on the meaning of government itself.</rdfs:comment>
