	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9e99aa4d-aa12-4d92-8994-0e80b851a493">
		<rdfs:label>article-9e99aa4d-aa12-4d92-8994-0e80b851a493</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Senate will hold its first public inquiry next week into the security failures that led to the Jan. 6 breach of the Capitol by a mob of former President Donald J. Trump’s supporters seeking to disrupt certification of President Biden’s election victory.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9e9c14b5-f13b-4aa3-8657-4d8d040f68bd">
		<rdfs:label>article-9e9c14b5-f13b-4aa3-8657-4d8d040f68bd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Concern turns to industrial sites and huge farms farther north as the storm heads toward South Carolina.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-912ab23e-cdd9-4a6c-8c3e-574664292078"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9e9f6f66-03f3-4922-8a46-d322fb2f3fce">
		<rdfs:label>article-9e9f6f66-03f3-4922-8a46-d322fb2f3fce</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With his poll numbers fading after a rally-around-the-leader bump, the president is stoking protests against stay-at-home orders.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ea56c16-be07-4571-91d6-3c42a7c2964e">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ea56c16-be07-4571-91d6-3c42a7c2964e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel, a staunch ally of President Trump’s who had a chilly relationship with former President Barack Obama, congratulated Joseph R. Biden Jr. early Sunday, despite Mr. Trump’s insistence that the U.S. election was not over.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0f6bb398-25ac-4b26-bd40-56d320f59168"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6bf4af99-38f0-4df7-94f4-82a6657aa590"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-72d6d153-fe7a-4dc0-9948-feb902e0ad6a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-76b712db-a748-409b-a3f6-0d8f098e54f6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7d7e5500-c552-439e-8b54-0438ccca9c6e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ea6df0a-593f-49c4-b51e-353dcec1192f">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ea6df0a-593f-49c4-b51e-353dcec1192f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>People with compromised immune systems are getting unapproved fourth or fifth Covid-19 shots, despite uncertainty about their safety or effectiveness.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0a19ff37-a276-4081-944e-e43f9f3234c8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ea88b6f-4d1a-439d-82b0-e85ec02a7c9d">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ea88b6f-4d1a-439d-82b0-e85ec02a7c9d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Louisiana senator, usually a reliable conservative vote, angered Republicans by voting to continue with the impeachment trial. But he has increasingly shown an inclination toward pragmatism.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ead226b-9fe9-4cd4-8187-cfdb31cecae6">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ead226b-9fe9-4cd4-8187-cfdb31cecae6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president’s stark departure from his message on Thursday night, when he announced guidelines for governors to reopen their states and said they would “call your own shots,” suggested he was ceding any semblance of national leadership on the pandemic.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9eaf8ae5-7449-4dcf-a709-47b23e2099a7">
		<rdfs:label>article-9eaf8ae5-7449-4dcf-a709-47b23e2099a7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The state flag, which features the blue bars and white stars of the Confederate battle flag, had flown over Mississippi for 126 years. It must be removed within 15 days.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc5a47b7-5e7e-4d58-8ee7-caaf2f703c6a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9eb1adf5-475b-4c5e-b187-f61e41cb7a5f">
		<rdfs:label>article-9eb1adf5-475b-4c5e-b187-f61e41cb7a5f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>State and local costs of dealing with the pandemic are skyrocketing as revenues plunge.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9eb2a4b8-a063-4b6c-8a15-5fce791a25b4">
		<rdfs:label>article-9eb2a4b8-a063-4b6c-8a15-5fce791a25b4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Republicans are reuniting — and re-energized — as they pursue a longstanding political goal.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-887d1269-7020-4c8e-8dfc-eae7c464f3cb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9eb3833e-3728-4f26-b548-1a3e4b34160e">
		<rdfs:label>article-9eb3833e-3728-4f26-b548-1a3e4b34160e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The national security adviser, Robert C. O’Brien, reiterated a plan to draw down troops to 2,500 by early 2021, sidestepping President Trump’s call for a Christmas exit.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc2c2b47-32c2-43a0-8e5f-dd4e72335932"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9eb7db8f-1416-43ea-b1db-847bd21fdd2b">
		<rdfs:label>article-9eb7db8f-1416-43ea-b1db-847bd21fdd2b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The report sidesteps a decision on what to do about troop numbers in Somalia, after President Donald J. Trump’s decision to pull out last year.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-46b2f3e2-fc43-4d1f-8134-a17365f8ec33"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ebd5435-7ff8-4773-a07b-af680c94382b">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ebd5435-7ff8-4773-a07b-af680c94382b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In Los Angeles, homeless deaths soared during the pandemic, doubling from prepandemic numbers. In New York, it was a different story.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2bfc1d86-f654-490c-ae5c-efaa41acbbe5"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ec2599d-12cd-4c67-b32d-759512be9f63">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ec2599d-12cd-4c67-b32d-759512be9f63</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Machines that examine samples of drugs can cost tens or even hundreds of thousands of dollars, but experts say they are an increasingly vital tool in stemming overdoses.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e4ac7a5-be1a-4937-b91e-66276e5f8dd9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9eceea49-4041-4f08-8461-6d4d58128ee2">
		<rdfs:label>article-9eceea49-4041-4f08-8461-6d4d58128ee2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Officials in the Biden administration expect plenty of complications, including summons to hearings over the U.S. withdrawal from Afghanistan.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc2c2b47-32c2-43a0-8e5f-dd4e72335932"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ed3c0af-5437-4d76-aff9-f67c3d1dc150">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ed3c0af-5437-4d76-aff9-f67c3d1dc150</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Around the country, but mostly in small towns in the West, hundreds of professional rodeos have been canceled.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-49d710e9-eb6c-42b2-9dd4-c680376fd332"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ed6bd51-56ef-4a85-aa4f-93f9cb11cb1f">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ed6bd51-56ef-4a85-aa4f-93f9cb11cb1f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As Americans prepare for out-of-state travel and multigenerational indoor gatherings over the holidays, many people who need to get tested for the coronavirus are running into shortages, long lines and other deterrents — while many others are avoiding getting tested altogether.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-078e57d0-5b20-48e9-b039-c2569b2acb05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-38e018f4-62fb-4f61-bfa4-3c5e99b30a3c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-12-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ed7a002-e344-4d05-8af7-899c6eea3560">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ed7a002-e344-4d05-8af7-899c6eea3560</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>We’re on top of the latest extreme weather in the U.S. and around the world. Follow here for news on heat waves, wildfires, floods and more.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ed7f49d-9c84-44c7-aabf-e419590dae92">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ed7f49d-9c84-44c7-aabf-e419590dae92</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Meet the two Democratic operatives battling President Trump since before he was president.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9edcc5cb-36d8-4013-b375-de4f4fb59ec5">
		<rdfs:label>article-9edcc5cb-36d8-4013-b375-de4f4fb59ec5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats have signed on to a resolution that would for the first time give House aides the same organizing protections other federal government employees enjoy.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-011ddbd5-8a1e-4932-8bfc-bad05d0ca67f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9d70ec7c-4469-4070-b704-f06eb556d22a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9edd87e8-fa91-4d89-9eca-7bf7a656ced9">
		<rdfs:label>article-9edd87e8-fa91-4d89-9eca-7bf7a656ced9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Without evidence, President Trump accused the chairman of the House Intelligence Committee of leaking intelligence.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dad1523a-f983-4f0f-af53-0061c7165e91"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ee37f45-b988-48c0-9cba-642d0eca47d2">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ee37f45-b988-48c0-9cba-642d0eca47d2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Republicans sought to use the Black congresswoman’s comments to racial justice protesters as a political weapon, claiming she had incited violence and daring Democrats to stand by her. They did.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ee49939-ec8b-4df2-8c95-ff2cf7d17957">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ee49939-ec8b-4df2-8c95-ff2cf7d17957</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Days after floods ravaged the eastern part of the state, the governor said that hundreds of people remained unaccounted for.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ae47edf3-29dc-462d-b74b-f886ebf56402"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc5a47b7-5e7e-4d58-8ee7-caaf2f703c6a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9eebf7fc-0141-4052-88b2-3c4c8910aca4">
		<rdfs:label>article-9eebf7fc-0141-4052-88b2-3c4c8910aca4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A State Department inspector general’s report found that Mr. Pompeo had deployed government employees to perform personal tasks.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-83d40723-6a13-432d-8617-d546a58e6733"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f4f38f08-6492-4112-8b82-52bd8aa6b34f"/>
