		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9eed3743-34c3-45f3-9f35-d6a0aa3a2e07">
		<rdfs:label>article-9eed3743-34c3-45f3-9f35-d6a0aa3a2e07</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Eric J. Nelson, a lawyer for Mr. Chauvin, returned again to the people who had watched Mr. Chauvin kneel on George Floyd, suggesting that the crowd was an aggressive and unpredictable group.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3d0d7757-313d-444e-a4df-32876c51aaa0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9eee50f1-b583-4c80-aee8-abd34284b6fd">
		<rdfs:label>article-9eee50f1-b583-4c80-aee8-abd34284b6fd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A Texas death row inmate, John H. Ramirez, asked the justices to let spiritual advisers pray with and lay hands on prisoners as they await execution.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-947ed571-ad87-49fb-b59a-9372d166d3c7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ef4bdc8-be4c-47d3-9d41-a424daae7051">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ef4bdc8-be4c-47d3-9d41-a424daae7051</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As states begin to loosen restrictions, the act of reopening will be carried out not by governors or the president, but the millions of individuals being asked to do it.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-81f0af94-b9cf-4dcb-8ae5-91c423d251ff"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b0d8acac-ba33-4091-b922-0eb5b9ab904d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e993acb7-fd71-489b-b569-b6b6d449dfe5"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ef77a2e-8bed-49f5-b5a3-e02f23cfb0e4">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ef77a2e-8bed-49f5-b5a3-e02f23cfb0e4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Georgia Democrats named Nikema Williams as successor to John Lewis. President Trump threatened to send federal troops to cities run by the “radical left” to temper unrest. And the Jacksonville sheriff said the city was not ready to provide security for the Republican convention.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ef9306b-3a38-4476-9976-ccc8f5e9a003">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ef9306b-3a38-4476-9976-ccc8f5e9a003</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As the administration sends up to $16 billion in additional subsidies, critics are concerned that the funds could be used to ensure that the president maintains the backing of one of his key voting blocs.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3263b980-a580-440f-bdd2-6d7fa7bb3fab"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9efddf5a-fca3-491e-a7d7-0856be76a434">
		<rdfs:label>article-9efddf5a-fca3-491e-a7d7-0856be76a434</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With the United States reaching a once-unthinkable coronavirus pandemic death toll of 400,000 people on Tuesday, the eve of his inauguration as president, Joseph R. Biden Jr. is assuming the role of mourner in chief and projecting an air of command of the issue that has vexed the Trump administration for the past year.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f800cdb3-ad0c-4b7e-81cb-a52efab2aad2"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9f088d37-8322-47b1-8df3-159feb1d42f3">
		<rdfs:label>article-9f088d37-8322-47b1-8df3-159feb1d42f3</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Hurricane Bob, which caused the deaths of more than a dozen people and hundreds of millions of dollars in damage in 1991, remains the last hurricane to make landfall in New England.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4d4e3743-3cf6-49c9-beea-1b12b8881a42"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-91caa243-6ff4-4c6d-affc-51bd8da8617d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9f0a70e6-d132-43bd-8901-e1cfca0d1872">
		<rdfs:label>article-9f0a70e6-d132-43bd-8901-e1cfca0d1872</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The lawyers represent Travis McMichael, who fatally shot Mr. Arbery, and his father. The lawyer for the third defendant deferred his opening statement until later in the trial.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5f497c4d-378e-4c6b-a1e7-70ebd6812d68"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d7a0b17f-e0aa-44c5-a995-e81e028fa879"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9f0c467e-6459-42d1-b2c1-f0eebde9f297">
		<rdfs:label>article-9f0c467e-6459-42d1-b2c1-f0eebde9f297</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Patricia Mazzei has spent nearly 15 years covering Miami. The experience helped her make sense of a controversy swirling around the city’s new police chief.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9f0f8edb-03ff-4928-86ce-a7b82076c0a1">
		<rdfs:label>article-9f0f8edb-03ff-4928-86ce-a7b82076c0a1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>At least 21 people were confirmed dead and about 10 remained unaccounted for after catastrophic flash flooding that scientists say climate change makes more common.</rdfs:comment>
