	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9fc43e70-6119-4118-8546-35f0a400d45d">
		<rdfs:label>article-9fc43e70-6119-4118-8546-35f0a400d45d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The West Virginia Democrat, who dashed President Trump’s hopes for a bipartisan acquittal, said his vote to convict was not about politics.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9fc8f803-11f4-497f-8f52-37d825fc5ae2">
		<rdfs:label>article-9fc8f803-11f4-497f-8f52-37d825fc5ae2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In this world — where tuition runs as high as $58,000 — the topic has become flammable. Parents, faculty, students and alumni have all entered the fray.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-12de0d3c-4c34-4f95-85a8-abb5edb86193"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
