	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9fd4e59f-77fc-4c43-a109-b9c846c53fc3">
		<rdfs:label>article-9fd4e59f-77fc-4c43-a109-b9c846c53fc3</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The economy is in dire shape. Millions of Americans are about to lose federal aid. The Senate is going on vacation.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9fdb5542-1a9e-49e2-a77d-49a3fdfd101b">
		<rdfs:label>article-9fdb5542-1a9e-49e2-a77d-49a3fdfd101b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Instead of the usual media circus, this summer’s made-for-TV political confabs will have a whole lot less TV.</rdfs:comment>
