		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9fef28ec-c88c-43f2-81e1-12e421562e31">
		<rdfs:label>article-9fef28ec-c88c-43f2-81e1-12e421562e31</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The goal is to disrupt Russia’s well-honed information-warfare systems, whether they are poised to hack election systems or influence the minds of voters.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fe2bac3e-e6e1-402b-a620-a5226e68a45a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ffab866-c4db-4743-bb8a-f8a274af0118">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ffab866-c4db-4743-bb8a-f8a274af0118</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Opposition from Republicans and some of their own senators has left Democrats struggling to determine whether they should try to nix the filibuster to save a top priority.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ffabd39-4226-47b0-8dfc-9443c5b58d32">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ffabd39-4226-47b0-8dfc-9443c5b58d32</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Biden administration announced the new guidelines as it continued to work to get coronavirus tests to people regardless of their insurance status.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e4ac7a5-be1a-4937-b91e-66276e5f8dd9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c0f96d-1b8c-4214-8727-29573022489d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ffaed10-03e1-4409-8ef8-83119fc1e8fb">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ffaed10-03e1-4409-8ef8-83119fc1e8fb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Donor money is helping pay for a dizzying array of litigation filed by the president or against him.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2098993a-1d86-4c6d-b5b9-c15f8e12852e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ffc3bc4-c13f-4644-80d0-556f096ab50c">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ffc3bc4-c13f-4644-80d0-556f096ab50c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A vast majority of undocumented teenagers are graduating high school this year without protection from deportation and the ability to legally work.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4b043cde-c9ac-41fc-91ae-7eae6c420e38"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ffd38ae-1199-4fea-a2a1-32135d15b127">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ffd38ae-1199-4fea-a2a1-32135d15b127</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>But he cautioned that the pandemic is not over and that the state lags far behind in vaccinations.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e2ba983e-eb48-483d-afa1-e67b02e88f99"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-9ffdd591-8cde-4521-bf2d-a868326d24ee">
		<rdfs:label>article-9ffdd591-8cde-4521-bf2d-a868326d24ee</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Everyone at the first night of the Democrats’ virtual gathering could at least agree that Mr. Biden should be the next president. They can worry about the rest later.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-577cfa39-5806-4396-ae24-cdf4ba406715"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4504805-5b5f-41c7-b157-41ff04a342ad"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a0016450-e56d-48d8-b473-6b7fa26a753c">
		<rdfs:label>article-a0016450-e56d-48d8-b473-6b7fa26a753c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The White House’s approach to avoiding accountability for its record is becoming clearer than ever, and it was on display as Mike Pence faced Kamala Harris.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a0025b04-6d8c-4226-8e84-b3a8642bc47c">
		<rdfs:label>article-a0025b04-6d8c-4226-8e84-b3a8642bc47c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump accepted the Republican Party’s nomination for a second term on Thursday, joining a general-election contest against Joseph R. Biden Jr. that he and his party cast this week as a crusade against left-wing ideology and violent social disorder, fought against the backdrop of a virus that Republicans largely described as a temporary handicap on the economy.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3488268a-8b17-411a-8185-6859abbab9a8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a0037792-5567-43db-8c18-6771e59fced1">
		<rdfs:label>article-a0037792-5567-43db-8c18-6771e59fced1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After ending stimulus talks via Twitter on Tuesday, the president reversed course, proposing a plan his own party may reject, and giving Democrats fresh leverage to dictate the terms of a deal.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4b06f805-a6f6-4cda-9908-3f8ddd3a0432"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a00aaf0b-e8e8-4200-8810-b1e966e29952">
		<rdfs:label>article-a00aaf0b-e8e8-4200-8810-b1e966e29952</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>These were the moments that defined President Trump’s first presidential debate against Joe Biden.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ebf4f94d-a728-4327-b424-d347782b7b17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a00c8a7f-0bf3-4ed7-8aa9-8fc8246c2126">
		<rdfs:label>article-a00c8a7f-0bf3-4ed7-8aa9-8fc8246c2126</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Some U.S. lawmakers say they have not given up on the idea of a tax on planet-warming carbon dioxide pollution, which would help meet the president’s promise to sharply cut U.S. emissions.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c55cfad1-37a4-40de-ab47-b363a537db6a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a00cb261-f605-4aed-9e69-73428e0415c4">
		<rdfs:label>article-a00cb261-f605-4aed-9e69-73428e0415c4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>What happens when intelligence officials warn that Russia is meddling in American politics again? Donald Trump gets mad — at the intelligence officials.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a0103b3c-363a-4530-a197-1ff4777bdb86">
		<rdfs:label>article-a0103b3c-363a-4530-a197-1ff4777bdb86</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>We’re seeing a breakdown of internal norms that tracks with the broader erosion of American institutions in recent years.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fda4452b-3825-4a26-bbb4-46f458379b68"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a0127834-b1af-4a91-ac8b-cb12f8ca5c26">
		<rdfs:label>article-a0127834-b1af-4a91-ac8b-cb12f8ca5c26</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats lead in overall numbers, as well as early voting, but voter registration gains in three critical states have given Republicans a cause for hope.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-21d856ad-a6ae-406e-a9e4-9707218ad815"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a015a5ab-9fbc-4e23-9f22-a81a079c8da9">
