	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a1f9b677-c287-495b-aeed-19d152de86cc">
		<rdfs:label>article-a1f9b677-c287-495b-aeed-19d152de86cc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The last time Representative Liz Cheney of Wyoming was staring down an attempt to purge her from House Republican leadership, as punishment for having voted to impeach former President Donald J. Trump, she whipped the vote herself, privately calling almost every member of her party to lock up support until she was confident the challenge would fail.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-12"/>
