		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2098993a-1d86-4c6d-b5b9-c15f8e12852e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a3a49de2-84b6-412f-a029-1dde6847ca04">
		<rdfs:label>article-a3a49de2-84b6-412f-a029-1dde6847ca04</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Trump team wants one more debate than is typically held in the general election, and argued that they should start earlier because the coronavirus may prompt an increase in early voting.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a3a59deb-415c-4150-92d1-4941f4248b32">
		<rdfs:label>article-a3a59deb-415c-4150-92d1-4941f4248b32</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Vincent Chin, a Chinese immigrant, was beaten to death after being pursued by two white Detroit autoworkers in 1982. On the 40th anniversary of his death, many hear frightening echoes.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-de093669-b27a-4345-ac65-683caba65a27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a3ad9f7a-e82d-4017-81bc-59d7e62a9ae4">
		<rdfs:label>article-a3ad9f7a-e82d-4017-81bc-59d7e62a9ae4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia, whose government was accused by American officials of interfering in the 2016 American election to help the Trump campaign, gave a wide-ranging interview on American politics on Wednesday in which he spoke warmly about Democrats.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ec0467d4-d43c-4871-810c-674e62f64e4b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a3ae8d25-98b9-4464-bc0c-643b3bbd7a96">
		<rdfs:label>article-a3ae8d25-98b9-4464-bc0c-643b3bbd7a96</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Protests following the death of George Floyd in Minneapolis swept across the state, prompting at least two countywide curfews in parts of Northern and Southern California.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
