	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a41fc523-4fff-42e2-93ad-5fe4c7505784">
		<rdfs:label>article-a41fc523-4fff-42e2-93ad-5fe4c7505784</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Former prisoners can now go to the polls. But fines remain one obstacle. Believing anything will make a difference is another. That’s where Julius Irving comes in.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-25fcb72a-e7e8-44a3-a824-63d53b97bc1e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a421256d-425d-49f7-a7fa-8964c296c810">
		<rdfs:label>article-a421256d-425d-49f7-a7fa-8964c296c810</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With Republicans taking control of the House in January, the chances that Congress will consider any added restrictions in next two years are also exceedingly slim.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0e84c75e-7bc1-4744-83f1-7496fcf4721d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a421c5bc-4986-4e32-9733-6c9ede0a10b6">
		<rdfs:label>article-a421c5bc-4986-4e32-9733-6c9ede0a10b6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump said he was giving an additional $13 billion of aid to America’s farmers at a campaign rally in Wisconsin on Thursday night, doling out government resources to key supporters as he looks to solidify his rural base ahead of Election Day.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4b06f805-a6f6-4cda-9908-3f8ddd3a0432"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a4234c8c-248a-4ff7-9415-4b99a286eac8">
		<rdfs:label>article-a4234c8c-248a-4ff7-9415-4b99a286eac8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As births drop, deaths accelerate and immigration slows, the country is closer than ever to an overall decline.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-81f0af94-b9cf-4dcb-8ae5-91c423d251ff"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a42b0fa1-55c5-4439-8c38-26c748c3b803">
		<rdfs:label>article-a42b0fa1-55c5-4439-8c38-26c748c3b803</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Why we won’t — and shouldn’t — declare one now.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9a4aaa82-7a6e-4284-937d-4c8810026f4d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a42be6aa-be4b-4fa5-965c-7182a389f527">
		<rdfs:label>article-a42be6aa-be4b-4fa5-965c-7182a389f527</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The administration’s measured response to a rocket attack in Erbil sharply contrasts with a Trump-era campaign against Iran that, more often than not, caught Iraq in the crossfire.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5a3094b1-6bc7-47d7-8f53-c56fd8ed0c59"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f4f38f08-6492-4112-8b82-52bd8aa6b34f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a4303e13-ea27-43a2-b3ae-d47a846be6fa">
		<rdfs:label>article-a4303e13-ea27-43a2-b3ae-d47a846be6fa</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Journeys through two states found Americans leading starkly different lives in the pandemic. New Mexico feels at a standstill. In South Dakota, life is going right on.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a43774cf-b044-4a18-a820-41f073b41954">
		<rdfs:label>article-a43774cf-b044-4a18-a820-41f073b41954</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>It’s not just Gavin Newsom’s problem. The state’s recall system is strange and troubling.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd146215-8c12-40b0-bfb7-0d9c07c5e63d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a43b6b83-6c27-492f-b830-5c365eafde63">
		<rdfs:label>article-a43b6b83-6c27-492f-b830-5c365eafde63</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The morning after Hurricane Zeta’s forceful winds downed power lines, toppled trees and caused road closures across the state of Georgia, widespread outages left more than 600,000 Georgians without electricity and took some of the state’s advanced voting locations offline Thursday — the penultimate day for early, in-person voting.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-000b9f5f-58e8-4c63-96ac-45f669ecbe29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a448adc5-636e-42c3-b5dd-826f15225134">
		<rdfs:label>article-a448adc5-636e-42c3-b5dd-826f15225134</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As cases soar in Texas, hospitals are filling up from El Paso to Lubbock. The Big Bend region is especially vulnerable, with just one hospital for 12,000 square miles.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d0804387-7ba1-4df8-b8ae-a8a9c6bfc424"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a44c5ced-0efc-4c77-9160-404c8b7495d7">
		<rdfs:label>article-a44c5ced-0efc-4c77-9160-404c8b7495d7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As the fallout from the assault on the Capitol sparks fresh concerns of new violence and Washington heightens security ahead of Joseph R. Biden Jr.’s inauguration on Jan. 20, the president-elect is gearing up to assume office at a tenuous moment for the nation.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9d70ec7c-4469-4070-b704-f06eb556d22a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a44c6c66-59cd-4f2e-b61f-045d899aead8">
		<rdfs:label>article-a44c6c66-59cd-4f2e-b61f-045d899aead8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Supreme Court’s decision on voting rights suggests that limits to the convenience of voting methods may be relatively permissible, while new burdens on casting a ballot in-person might be more vulnerable.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-17ddcb21-b8ba-45a7-8e71-073c17f7026b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a44df5ff-f501-4225-8516-367062fec947">
		<rdfs:label>article-a44df5ff-f501-4225-8516-367062fec947</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>David Malpass has faced continuing criticism from those who question his commitment to climate action as well as the bank’s track record.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-80938ccc-3865-4478-bf4f-7759ead7221e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a45493df-03f3-4f92-b70d-51610b4295f4">
		<rdfs:label>article-a45493df-03f3-4f92-b70d-51610b4295f4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Maya Wiley is a longtime civil rights lawyer who served as counsel to Mayor Bill de Blasio and oversaw the city’s Civilian Complaint Review Board.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a455de7d-1e0e-458f-afd1-70b5a1ded96f">
		<rdfs:label>article-a455de7d-1e0e-458f-afd1-70b5a1ded96f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The announcement by the Justice Department was an abrupt turnaround a month after the high-profile arrest of a former defense minister.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2c183a13-1898-4deb-ad56-cc02fd034eaf"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a47e8931-f51e-4343-a990-2c520552325e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a460c9b9-33b9-41ae-9fcb-fb2ca3ec2b07">
		<rdfs:label>article-a460c9b9-33b9-41ae-9fcb-fb2ca3ec2b07</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In the days since a mob of Trump supporters stormed the U.S. Capitol, federal and local authorities have arrested almost 100 people who they said were involved in the attack.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0d6427ef-da1b-4d64-8c55-4f2b53f3bd95"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fd9f1ad4-cd49-4185-a0bb-a129097c5a29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a4617d0f-de6a-4b73-8324-9412b0f20d6b">
		<rdfs:label>article-a4617d0f-de6a-4b73-8324-9412b0f20d6b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Economic growth is the primary corrective for unemployment, but targeted aid can help people find jobs more quickly.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a463667c-5c57-42ea-a85e-a0fb496c5b1f">
		<rdfs:label>article-a463667c-5c57-42ea-a85e-a0fb496c5b1f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Nikki Haley, the former United Nations ambassador, used a well-timed endorsement of Representative Nancy Mace to get on the opposite side of the former president.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-803bdb8f-8c3c-4210-80c9-22b0af3fd2ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a463c2d1-0f80-4942-aeda-4ddf2db56b59">
		<rdfs:label>article-a463c2d1-0f80-4942-aeda-4ddf2db56b59</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Both President Trump and Joseph R. Biden Jr. have called for justice for Mr. Floyd. Mr. Trump has also called protesters “thugs,” and Mr. Biden has blamed him for “incendiary tweets.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a46915ab-2595-42db-a72f-2a3eefc45c79">
		<rdfs:label>article-a46915ab-2595-42db-a72f-2a3eefc45c79</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Rising seas, raging fires, hotter temperatures — and a bit of positivity.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
