	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a5ae8e18-aa69-4151-9c24-ce6a22b6e6e1">
		<rdfs:label>article-a5ae8e18-aa69-4151-9c24-ce6a22b6e6e1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The coronavirus has created new tensions. Staying at home has worsened abusive situations. Shelters worry about the spread of the virus.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3d0d7757-313d-444e-a4df-32876c51aaa0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a5b09ae5-b4d0-4f3e-b13d-bdca16dcd08e">
		<rdfs:label>article-a5b09ae5-b4d0-4f3e-b13d-bdca16dcd08e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>An unsealed court filing shows that the social media company fought the subpoena, which the Biden administration is said to have withdrawn.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a5b33ccb-4476-493c-ab90-8931984a46fe">
		<rdfs:label>article-a5b33ccb-4476-493c-ab90-8931984a46fe</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>New research shows that all groups are behind in math and reading after disruptions during the pandemic. But it’s the most vulnerable students who experienced the steepest setbacks.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d0804387-7ba1-4df8-b8ae-a8a9c6bfc424"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a5b9ea23-83b8-49b1-9ec3-679e92b8bb71">
		<rdfs:label>article-a5b9ea23-83b8-49b1-9ec3-679e92b8bb71</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Once regarded as the most vulnerable incumbents, many Democrats who carried Trump districts in 2018 are poised to win re-election, boosting the party’s chances of building its House majority.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-26"/>
