	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a5c27c0c-5e89-4af6-be65-b426c81a499f">
		<rdfs:label>article-a5c27c0c-5e89-4af6-be65-b426c81a499f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president’s threat to use troops against largely peaceful protesters, as well as other attempts to politicize the military, have unsettled a number of current and former members and their families.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-20ac5364-1758-414f-ab86-a88673954008"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a5c29949-60f5-431a-8883-d7269490b7bd">
		<rdfs:label>article-a5c29949-60f5-431a-8883-d7269490b7bd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The suit is the third case brought since Georgia’s Republican governor signed a bill curtailing voting access and rights.</rdfs:comment>
