		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd522e1c-57a0-49bc-9835-fae39d9d58a6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a5e3344b-6f3e-4895-84e5-ef5d49244614">
		<rdfs:label>article-a5e3344b-6f3e-4895-84e5-ef5d49244614</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Some in the G.O.P. want President Trump to endorse the opponent of Kris Kobach, who they worry could cost them a traditionally safe Senate seat. So far, the White House has declined to do so.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8eb0923f-854c-4241-9d79-040d1aeeb0c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a5e5e08c-7ef5-47c6-b003-fbb8801bab9d">
		<rdfs:label>article-a5e5e08c-7ef5-47c6-b003-fbb8801bab9d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Senate Republican leader proposed impeachment trial rules that push the 1999 precedent toward President Trump’s preferences.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a5e5e857-278a-476a-ab38-200b3f215528">
		<rdfs:label>article-a5e5e857-278a-476a-ab38-200b3f215528</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Opening bars and bringing back football teams have led to new outbreaks. Communities that evolved around campuses face potentially existential losses in population, jobs and revenue.</rdfs:comment>
