		<rdfs:label>article-a68c808d-0f48-4aad-9933-c52bd35d485e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In the final stretch before the 2022 midterm elections, some Democrats are pushing for a new message that acknowledges the pain of rising prices.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-803bdb8f-8c3c-4210-80c9-22b0af3fd2ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4bd1aa5-c807-421e-b8ae-1b3824d70300"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-a68e04a9-09c1-4322-b03b-6ba1180076c5">
		<rdfs:label>article-a68e04a9-09c1-4322-b03b-6ba1180076c5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The attorney general is said to have set a deadline over the objections of career lawyers who say they need more time to build the case.</rdfs:comment>
