		<rdfs:label>article-ab15bcfc-be20-480a-8b7c-7765f2eb5101</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As of early Saturday morning, Joseph R. Biden Jr.  led President Trump in Pennsylvania by 28,833 votes, with 96 percent of the state’s ballots counted. The remaining mail ballots are expected to favor Democrats, and officials in Philadelphia have said it could take a few more days to complete the count there.</rdfs:comment>
