	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-afab7d15-fdf8-4711-81dd-285351077a6c">
		<rdfs:label>article-afab7d15-fdf8-4711-81dd-285351077a6c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Election Day is always the Tuesday after the first Monday in November, but the day circled on the calendar every four years is no longer the singular time when American elections happen. That day, Nov. 3 this year, instead represents the end of a six-week sprint during a record number of Americans cast their ballots in advance.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
