	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b222a8ae-e2d3-4ba2-bbc1-80b53ec22d86">
		<rdfs:label>article-b222a8ae-e2d3-4ba2-bbc1-80b53ec22d86</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Michigan’s governor lifted a stay-at-home order as other states announced steps to reopen. A Rohingya Muslim who lived in a Bangladeshwe  refugee camp died of the coronavirus.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b22c9305-5567-4ab3-93a9-f6b503492c73">
		<rdfs:label>article-b22c9305-5567-4ab3-93a9-f6b503492c73</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump long ago redefined what constitutes normal in the White House, but with 77 days left in the campaign he is pushing all the boundaries at once.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-922ad7b9-e6de-456a-9bc2-69207748d175"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-17"/>
