		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b3007a49-9fcd-4305-9514-37a57639ddf5">
		<rdfs:label>article-b3007a49-9fcd-4305-9514-37a57639ddf5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Reports of infections are falling in Cleveland, Newark and Washington, suggesting that a national peak may be approaching.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-67a92994-4180-4c15-8d35-e19200044979"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ae47edf3-29dc-462d-b74b-f886ebf56402"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-de093669-b27a-4345-ac65-683caba65a27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b301048a-ffe1-490b-a627-5f7ef00857c6">
		<rdfs:label>article-b301048a-ffe1-490b-a627-5f7ef00857c6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Last week alone, three federal rulings set election parameters in three states. And scores of legal fights spawned by the pandemic are shaping who will vote and how.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-be4a3e54-4b34-4f4b-b446-90f3692a587d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b3063670-97ea-4a1a-a764-046066ced4ea">
		<rdfs:label>article-b3063670-97ea-4a1a-a764-046066ced4ea</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In Arizona and Nevada, Republicans’ path to victory appeared to narrow, though both races remain close. The G.O.P.’s odds of success are greater in the House.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e9c4025-7dbe-4808-a3d4-b9d25fa14354"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b307a6b7-c27f-48d3-997d-fd2aac8afc7c">
		<rdfs:label>article-b307a6b7-c27f-48d3-997d-fd2aac8afc7c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>WinRed, the donation-processing digital platform created last year to help Republicans catch up with Democrats’ online fund-raising, announced this week that it had passed the $1 billion mark in only 15 months.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b309fa8f-5fa9-4000-9a1e-3e7029920b6c">
		<rdfs:label>article-b309fa8f-5fa9-4000-9a1e-3e7029920b6c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president has employed the same kind of inflammatory language as George Wallace did in the 1968 campaign. Richard Nixon ran that year seeking the middle between the Alabama governor and Hubert Humphrey.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-922ad7b9-e6de-456a-9bc2-69207748d175"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b30e0474-378d-44e4-8042-a6b88ba8a69f">
		<rdfs:label>article-b30e0474-378d-44e4-8042-a6b88ba8a69f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>ATLANTA — Georgia officials on Friday certified President-elect Joseph R. Biden Jr.’s victory in the state, hours after a staffer mistakenly sent out a statement saying the process had been completed — a surreal last-minute glitch in a critical and closely watched battleground state.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d7a0b17f-e0aa-44c5-a995-e81e028fa879"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b31014dc-44e1-480e-881b-a6c8e9d9cf33">
		<rdfs:label>article-b31014dc-44e1-480e-881b-a6c8e9d9cf33</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>New York Times readers describe the ways the pandemic first hit them and upended their lives, in their own words.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d0804387-7ba1-4df8-b8ae-a8a9c6bfc424"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b31112ff-95e6-4ffb-872b-f1a22322251a">
		<rdfs:label>article-b31112ff-95e6-4ffb-872b-f1a22322251a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump is reporting “no symptoms” of the coronavirus and doing “extremely well,” according to the White House physician, Dr. Sean P. Conley.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc2c2b47-32c2-43a0-8e5f-dd4e72335932"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b312dd27-e8e0-4424-8370-7ec7099f478e">
		<rdfs:label>article-b312dd27-e8e0-4424-8370-7ec7099f478e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In a sign of the Trump era’s lingering alternate realities, Republicans in the struggling state party are refusing to move forward with a new system for choosing nominees.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b3177139-2609-495a-b80b-5b67699e3e77">
		<rdfs:label>article-b3177139-2609-495a-b80b-5b67699e3e77</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Resistance to vaccine mandates, once a fringe position, has entered the Republican mainstream. But the governors fighting President Biden’s Covid-19 requirements impose mandates of their own.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b3196661-8bce-4466-a406-d0343101d63f">
		<rdfs:label>article-b3196661-8bce-4466-a406-d0343101d63f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Representative Joseph P. Kennedy III is trailing Senator Edward J. Markey in every poll ahead of the Democratic Senate primary in Massachusetts on Tuesday, and may become the first Kennedy to lose a race in the state.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b31a92fa-7a17-4527-9632-cdd138f2f2f7">
		<rdfs:label>article-b31a92fa-7a17-4527-9632-cdd138f2f2f7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The chairwoman of the House Oversight Committee said the postmaster general had withheld requested documents, telling her panel his verbal testimony should suffice.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b31b614b-f064-4921-8c52-6dfb6c8bb5f0">
		<rdfs:label>article-b31b614b-f064-4921-8c52-6dfb6c8bb5f0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Families of some who perished have written pointedly about the virus in remembrances. They tell of agonizing final days. They plead for wearing of masks.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3d0d7757-313d-444e-a4df-32876c51aaa0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b31c0a1d-dd34-42fe-99cc-0d730ca2d820">
		<rdfs:label>article-b31c0a1d-dd34-42fe-99cc-0d730ca2d820</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Here’s what key votes around the world mean for climate action. Or inaction.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ec0f6572-4696-4e2e-b261-57f3ee9a323f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b31ead02-84a6-4f21-9317-22e706d67b4f">
		<rdfs:label>article-b31ead02-84a6-4f21-9317-22e706d67b4f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The West Virginia Democrat said he had relented and agreed to sign on to a climate, energy and tax package after returning to negotiations to draft a version that would combat inflation.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c67a9047-7b94-4e45-aaa9-c820c2b967de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b32501a1-c301-4d8c-a405-bd305af7b1da">
		<rdfs:label>article-b32501a1-c301-4d8c-a405-bd305af7b1da</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The idea after the Watergate scandals was to keep government honest. President Trump’s goal seems to be to ensure its loyalty.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b327f84f-e73e-49d4-b3d4-f088dbd056b8">
		<rdfs:label>article-b327f84f-e73e-49d4-b3d4-f088dbd056b8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A giant pool of industrial waste almost burst in Florida this week. There are thousands more around the country.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b328e143-6541-410b-9cdd-42ff6424bae5">
		<rdfs:label>article-b328e143-6541-410b-9cdd-42ff6424bae5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The secretary of state will also use his trip to the region this week to work on humanitarian aid for Gaza but has no plans to pursue full-fledged peace talks.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-24dad853-b94f-42bd-b7ab-eb1c31627e37"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8574c955-119c-4367-887c-af2f24f35fd3"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f4f38f08-6492-4112-8b82-52bd8aa6b34f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b3298c35-a506-4043-a0bf-2c4b6eac0950">
		<rdfs:label>article-b3298c35-a506-4043-a0bf-2c4b6eac0950</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden has served in elected office for almost four decades. He has interacted with nine presidents. He is accustomed to staff waiting on him, traveling by motorcade, and he learned his way around the Oval Office and the mazelike layout of the West Wing from his eight years as vice president.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c67a9047-7b94-4e45-aaa9-c820c2b967de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b32be1be-4505-404f-903d-99f5fbc08ec4">
		<rdfs:label>article-b32be1be-4505-404f-903d-99f5fbc08ec4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A managing editor of the right-wing website RedState appeared to attack Dr. Anthony S. Fauci and spread misinformation about the coronavirus pandemic while working for Dr. Fauci’s agency.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-011ddbd5-8a1e-4932-8bfc-bad05d0ca67f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b331895a-8ab4-4f78-a8e9-427bfff61c2d">
		<rdfs:label>article-b331895a-8ab4-4f78-a8e9-427bfff61c2d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>When he was winning primaries, many in the Democratic Party were wary of the Vermont senator. Now, he’s a friend, chess-playing companion and “American original.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-577cfa39-5806-4396-ae24-cdf4ba406715"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b337de59-1830-482d-86b8-aac2ac5a3255">
		<rdfs:label>article-b337de59-1830-482d-86b8-aac2ac5a3255</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Across 48 television ads in seven competitive Senate races, the Republican incumbents haven’t mentioned the president once.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-93d154d3-6d3d-4599-ac55-e63a146d8d6f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b338b112-afd9-4452-9bc0-6ea99e65da82">
		<rdfs:label>article-b338b112-afd9-4452-9bc0-6ea99e65da82</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A super PAC announced late Thursday that it was buying $9 million in television and digital ads. It will be one of the largest ad buys by a super PAC in the 2020 Democratic primary.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b33afa61-625f-4592-8953-1cc63898e61e">
		<rdfs:label>article-b33afa61-625f-4592-8953-1cc63898e61e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>It’s hard to find a single street in the working-class town of Manville that was not severely affected by flooding connected to Hurricane Ida.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f6ea6cc9-1772-4484-b9f9-6ba0f1b77f27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b33c9a8c-03f6-4216-8f62-f6dc62096867">
		<rdfs:label>article-b33c9a8c-03f6-4216-8f62-f6dc62096867</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Records kept by medical examiners in Florida offer a window into how the coronavirus has killed more than 1,600 people there. Many died at home.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-48e200fd-02da-4ffc-8666-066f9561a258"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-61755e58-5eb6-4c77-ae88-fc39fa95b82a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b33e43a1-a9e8-4a2f-be20-eb0454e79acb">
		<rdfs:label>article-b33e43a1-a9e8-4a2f-be20-eb0454e79acb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats’ quest to expand their control of the Senate in 2022 heated up late Thursday with the entry of a second high-profile candidate seeking to claim the seat of Senator Patrick J. Toomey of Pennsylvania, a Republican who is retiring.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c2e66850-f7bc-45ca-83ed-c0a1f8490a14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
