		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b4392985-392d-479e-9186-250304aef5f2">
		<rdfs:label>article-b4392985-392d-479e-9186-250304aef5f2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A bipartisan alliance is trying to topple the state’s ban on fusion voting, a system under which third-party groups like the Working Families Party in New York have gained influence.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e9c4025-7dbe-4808-a3d4-b9d25fa14354"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b43a0c24-8192-4146-aeab-5e7ac5ebcc58">
		<rdfs:label>article-b43a0c24-8192-4146-aeab-5e7ac5ebcc58</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Cutting interest rates is weak medicine. The best way to limit the economic impact of coronavirus is a strong public health response.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45dcdf16-b5a1-43ae-b828-c69e316ccb32"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
