	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b44f4232-c517-469b-88ed-3199855acb94">
		<rdfs:label>article-b44f4232-c517-469b-88ed-3199855acb94</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Countries have made insufficient progress on international goals designed to halt a catastrophic slide, a new report found.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2afe2750-7a7d-460f-b9fb-4feddaf4f58b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b44f57f4-ac5b-4567-90e9-69d0687564dd">
		<rdfs:label>article-b44f57f4-ac5b-4567-90e9-69d0687564dd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A military judge said he would decide before the trial of five men accused of plotting the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks whether their treatment in C.I.A. prisons amounted to torture.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4bd6cfaa-ebec-415a-8c53-2870f770bfa7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b450ede1-e90b-4c32-9551-7047f79829ea">
		<rdfs:label>article-b450ede1-e90b-4c32-9551-7047f79829ea</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump gave 18 interviews to the famed Watergate journalist, gambling that he could control the narrative. Instead, he undermined himself shortly before an election.</rdfs:comment>
