		<rdfs:label>article-b49894d7-1413-46b2-8492-2717b72cd306</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With no winner in the 2020 race and votes still being counted in several battleground states, President Trump entered the East Room of the White House at 2:21 a.m. on Wednesday and asserted without evidence that the election was being taken from him by “a very sad group of people.”</rdfs:comment>
