	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b4d942ab-941a-434a-92f6-c30710faeed8">
		<rdfs:label>article-b4d942ab-941a-434a-92f6-c30710faeed8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The states are asking voters whether to amend constitutions that have exceptions to slavery bans. Some hope that the changes could allow prisoners to challenge the practice of being forced into labor for little or no pay.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e993acb7-fd71-489b-b569-b6b6d449dfe5"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b4dd4d58-c735-426c-b1a5-c58e923053ca">
		<rdfs:label>article-b4dd4d58-c735-426c-b1a5-c58e923053ca</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The legislation, which the president is expected to sign quickly, lifts the debt ceiling until early December, when another congressional showdown looms.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b4dfea07-29c1-4db9-b91d-278e2aae4a08">
		<rdfs:label>article-b4dfea07-29c1-4db9-b91d-278e2aae4a08</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>“Glasgow was never ever going to get every country joining up,” Mr. Kerry said. He’s already looking to next year to build on pledges that nations have made and push them to do more.</rdfs:comment>
