		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b4dffe20-1671-46c6-9372-e99b2d8eab81">
		<rdfs:label>article-b4dffe20-1671-46c6-9372-e99b2d8eab81</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>WASHINGTON — Gov. Doug Ducey of Arizona sued the Biden administration on Friday to block its efforts to claw back pandemic relief money that the state has been using to undercut mask requirements in schools.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4b06f805-a6f6-4cda-9908-3f8ddd3a0432"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b4e3c4b1-8e18-4761-ad12-25e9c8233576">
		<rdfs:label>article-b4e3c4b1-8e18-4761-ad12-25e9c8233576</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Fauci plans to issue a stark warning on reopening the country: This is your morning tip sheet.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-887d1269-7020-4c8e-8dfc-eae7c464f3cb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b4f37e07-6c51-41b2-808b-324d1212b0bb">
		<rdfs:label>article-b4f37e07-6c51-41b2-808b-324d1212b0bb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>All but three of 20 claims the president made were accurate, demonstrating his regard for basic facts and his proclivity to err when speaking off the cuff.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-be4afe5b-5317-4441-a7de-57071d96016d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b4f4a803-0478-4493-804b-13b606179944">
		<rdfs:label>article-b4f4a803-0478-4493-804b-13b606179944</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Ukrainian soldiers are firing thousands of shells daily, forcing the U.S. to replace gun barrels across the border in Poland.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3bea54bd-f3ee-4712-b704-2739e55e376e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-524922c4-c335-4218-b145-d4752931be34"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b4f95f4c-dcc0-45de-bf80-761fb9c43645">
		<rdfs:label>article-b4f95f4c-dcc0-45de-bf80-761fb9c43645</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Getting into one of the Democratic debates is like getting a ticket to the Super Bowl or the World Series.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ef6cc7eb-b6e8-4dba-84e0-6b42579e91d0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b4fb39c4-32e6-4023-b15d-1c12de46fe83">
		<rdfs:label>article-b4fb39c4-32e6-4023-b15d-1c12de46fe83</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>She hoped Jan. 6 would be a turning point for Republicans. And while it did prove to be a dividing line, it was those who crossed Donald J. Trump who have faced electoral consequences.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b500a0dc-16bb-482e-b329-c79d59f9e207">
		<rdfs:label>article-b500a0dc-16bb-482e-b329-c79d59f9e207</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Ed Gainey won the Democratic primary in a city that is roughly a quarter Black. The incumbent, Bill Peduto, is the first Pittsburgh mayor to lose a bid to stay in office since 1933.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ae47edf3-29dc-462d-b74b-f886ebf56402"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b504b308-aa70-40cd-addd-b58c4eba8764">
		<rdfs:label>article-b504b308-aa70-40cd-addd-b58c4eba8764</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>One defense lawyer objected to the Rev. Jesse Jackson’s presence in court. Another said jurors looked sympathetically at Ahmaud Arbery’s mother as she sobbed at the sight of her son’s photo.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5f497c4d-378e-4c6b-a1e7-70ebd6812d68"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d7a0b17f-e0aa-44c5-a995-e81e028fa879"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b504b600-fcc1-4fba-a699-021f38428d75">
		<rdfs:label>article-b504b600-fcc1-4fba-a699-021f38428d75</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A Jamaican couple spent nearly two and a half years inside Philadelphia churches, isolated even further by the pandemic. This month, U.S. immigration officials relented.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-edd059c5-3ec4-4bec-b45e-ca6834a9e51c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b5059df7-184b-4995-a38f-39628f172340">
		<rdfs:label>article-b5059df7-184b-4995-a38f-39628f172340</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The New York Times asked poets laureate from across the country what the people in their states had to be thankful for in this difficult year.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b5096144-c5aa-4244-bc10-76153f227b1e">
		<rdfs:label>article-b5096144-c5aa-4244-bc10-76153f227b1e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>For both Democrats and Republicans, there is a sense of foreboding about what the next few months could bring a country already battered by a virus and economic devastation.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ae47edf3-29dc-462d-b74b-f886ebf56402"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b50a6507-6568-4e21-8422-f7018419feee">
		<rdfs:label>article-b50a6507-6568-4e21-8422-f7018419feee</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Few prognostications give Democrats a chance to hold onto their narrow margin in the House, and Republicans hope to make gains in traditionally bedrock blue states.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-803bdb8f-8c3c-4210-80c9-22b0af3fd2ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b50b12e5-51ab-4648-b849-76bab04497bf">
		<rdfs:label>article-b50b12e5-51ab-4648-b849-76bab04497bf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president has reversed or limited efforts at reform that his predecessor enacted.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-be4afe5b-5317-4441-a7de-57071d96016d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b50d3b69-39a8-4eab-a463-3b67a0d5dfaf">
		<rdfs:label>article-b50d3b69-39a8-4eab-a463-3b67a0d5dfaf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The state has been a center of efforts by right-wing activists and some Republican officials that disrupt voting in the name of election integrity.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b510e1b2-87f4-4a09-a41f-5d3c19c95c7d">
		<rdfs:label>article-b510e1b2-87f4-4a09-a41f-5d3c19c95c7d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In a culture-war brawl that has spilled into the country’s educational system, Republicans at the local, state and national levels are trying to block curriculums that emphasize systemic racism.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b84d8bda-1ee4-435d-8105-15b48a6a482f"/>
