		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b7752f73-3fff-47d9-8ebb-3569a4f5cc20">
		<rdfs:label>article-b7752f73-3fff-47d9-8ebb-3569a4f5cc20</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Rallying supporters in Bullhead City, Ariz., the first of two stops in the state on Wednesday, President Trump claimed that a vaccine for the coronavirus would be available “momentarily,” speeding up an already exaggerated timeline in the final days of the presidential race.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c67a9047-7b94-4e45-aaa9-c820c2b967de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b779dbd7-9dc5-4a1b-8da4-b5333042d5ce">
		<rdfs:label>article-b779dbd7-9dc5-4a1b-8da4-b5333042d5ce</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Joseph R. Biden Jr., in his first public address of a former Senate aide’s accusation that he sexually assaulted her in 1993, called on the National Archives to release any document related to the allegation.</rdfs:comment>
