	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b7c0029c-781a-4fdc-aaa2-5aabbe09b637">
		<rdfs:label>article-b7c0029c-781a-4fdc-aaa2-5aabbe09b637</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>When President-elect Joseph R. Biden Jr. takes the oath of office on Wednesday, he may be accompanied by a familial artifact that has followed him throughout his 50-year political career: a hefty Bible, accented with a Celtic cross, that has been in his family since 1893.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ab0366b9-dff5-47f7-930e-f33129e54673"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b7c2fa25-31de-423e-bb17-c8f77ac6f0fd">
		<rdfs:label>article-b7c2fa25-31de-423e-bb17-c8f77ac6f0fd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>2019 was a very hot year, with global average temperatures the second highest on record,by less than one-tenth of a degree Fahrenheit behind 2016. </rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e17310c8-39f3-4c91-8224-a91b0b94e409"/>
