	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b855ca51-09bd-4f88-93d3-43ce453964bc">
		<rdfs:label>article-b855ca51-09bd-4f88-93d3-43ce453964bc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>YUMA, Ariz. — President Trump on Tuesday accused Joseph R. Biden Jr. of seeking to throw open the United States’ borders to criminals and disease, using the backdrop of a border city to stoke fears of immigrants as Democrats prepared for the second day of the party’s nominating convention.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-19"/>
