	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b8c4c0e9-e7f7-49f6-9106-c1d8a3c0256d">
		<rdfs:label>article-b8c4c0e9-e7f7-49f6-9106-c1d8a3c0256d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Dr. Deborah Birx, who helped run the pandemic response for former President Donald J. Trump, lashed out at Dr. Scott Atlas, a former Stanford neuroradiologist who advised Mr. Trump and advocated for allowing the virus to spread through much of the population.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b8c771c5-b4bb-42b5-a1af-d3c0d2b01a7e">
		<rdfs:label>article-b8c771c5-b4bb-42b5-a1af-d3c0d2b01a7e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As President Trump continues to litigate the 2020 election, some judges have lost all patience. Here are some excerpts of their rulings.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-011ddbd5-8a1e-4932-8bfc-bad05d0ca67f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-90788841-2a13-4598-abd3-3b677caff4d4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b8cb3568-8acc-432e-9ccd-579a6058ab0b">
		<rdfs:label>article-b8cb3568-8acc-432e-9ccd-579a6058ab0b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>It will be the first solo trip abroad for Dr. Biden, a first lady whose traveling schedule currently outpaces her husband’s.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd42dd7e-7a0d-4a74-908e-252de023edfb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b8cc2152-092a-4fc4-8a12-1607e2a763a8">
		<rdfs:label>article-b8cc2152-092a-4fc4-8a12-1607e2a763a8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The investigation was a sign that President Biden intends to wield federal law enforcement as a tool to combat police abuses.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd522e1c-57a0-49bc-9835-fae39d9d58a6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b8ce75ea-6cdd-4e97-88eb-c54e4ae0e8a5">
		<rdfs:label>article-b8ce75ea-6cdd-4e97-88eb-c54e4ae0e8a5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>David DePape’s life was unstable when he embraced Gamergate and far-right conspiracy theories. He is now accused of breaking into Speaker Nancy Pelosi’s home and assaulting her husband.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-10ac2d2b-df6f-4f6e-81ed-6043c29aa826"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-1e5cee4f-82a8-44a6-9cc0-9285f4da7bf4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6ebd0cd5-ea30-4810-9596-627dcc7bde1b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9a5389b6-c0ea-4275-8951-1523cfe86f87"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b8d2dcb0-6600-4de2-93b6-eab4bdf659e3">
		<rdfs:label>article-b8d2dcb0-6600-4de2-93b6-eab4bdf659e3</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats in New Jersey are voting at higher rates than Republicans in conservative strongholds with three weeks to go before Election Day.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a52c39d4-8674-490c-863d-f51d898f0567"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b8d5671b-1719-47fc-a261-bacaa4aacede">
		<rdfs:label>article-b8d5671b-1719-47fc-a261-bacaa4aacede</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Demand is rising for nurses who work on contract. It is a nomadic existence and, in a pandemic, a high-risk one. “I was totally unprepared for the reality,” one recalled.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3d0d7757-313d-444e-a4df-32876c51aaa0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-42b477b0-b77c-4cfb-a2a2-1c4a689eab0d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b8d9213d-d59b-4cf1-86b1-82320465bedb">
		<rdfs:label>article-b8d9213d-d59b-4cf1-86b1-82320465bedb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Before Stacey Abrams was a prominent figure on the national political stage, she was known to romance readers under another name — Selena Montgomery. Under her pen name, Ms. Abrams, the voting rights activist and former candidate for governor in Georgia, has published eight romance novels, with titles like “Reckless” and “Deception.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9373374d-0dd4-449a-b6ac-ad42e3a2a5cd"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b8d94bbf-d4ea-44e3-a4d8-5bc80ebcc2b9">
		<rdfs:label>article-b8d94bbf-d4ea-44e3-a4d8-5bc80ebcc2b9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The company has also requested authorization of its Covid vaccine for 6- to 11-year-olds and 12- to 17-year-olds.</rdfs:comment>
