	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b905f293-29a9-429b-9bd7-aa23c77176f6">
		<rdfs:label>article-b905f293-29a9-429b-9bd7-aa23c77176f6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As the number of coronavirus deaths in the city reached 1,000 this week, three-fourths of the dead were Black.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ae47edf3-29dc-462d-b74b-f886ebf56402"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e993acb7-fd71-489b-b569-b6b6d449dfe5"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b9089023-9dd1-4705-8428-fa5dfb47fd5e">
		<rdfs:label>article-b9089023-9dd1-4705-8428-fa5dfb47fd5e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The U.S. says that lifting stay-at-home rules too soon could result in a spike in infections. Apple and Google are working on a cellphone feature to help with contact tracing.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b90b1043-d09f-4c3a-93bb-19c092227f5a">
		<rdfs:label>article-b90b1043-d09f-4c3a-93bb-19c092227f5a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Senator Chuck Schumer, the majority leader, offered draft legislation to remove marijuana from the list of controlled substances and begin regulating and taxing it.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b90bfb30-1aaa-4a13-9578-1c226e7ff22e">
		<rdfs:label>article-b90bfb30-1aaa-4a13-9578-1c226e7ff22e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Government lawyers said the transfer of Majid Khan was a high priority because he pleaded guilty to war crimes and his sentence at Guantánamo Bay had ended.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4bd6cfaa-ebec-415a-8c53-2870f770bfa7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
