		<rdfs:label>article-b93080f9-ae2e-493e-b398-c23fb96e19fc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mr. Thune, the No. 2 Republican in the Senate, is considering giving up his South Dakota seat because of both family concerns and Donald Trump’s enduring hold on the G.O.P.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-12-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-b931421e-f968-4862-8d61-6f264c820e1b">
		<rdfs:label>article-b931421e-f968-4862-8d61-6f264c820e1b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>David DePape, the man accused of bludgeoning the husband of Nancy Pelosi, told the police that he also had Gavin Newsom and Tom Hanks on his target list.</rdfs:comment>
