		<rdfs:label>article-ba91d313-aa67-4a8e-8b52-c6630e4b3c42</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A Queens man who told federal agents he wanted to join the far-right Proud Boys group was charged with a weapons offense on Wednesday after messages he posted on social media around the time of the Capitol riot raised alarms, according to prosecutors and court documents.</rdfs:comment>
