		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bb0c64fb-d7db-4d0f-869d-80d9df29f8fe">
		<rdfs:label>article-bb0c64fb-d7db-4d0f-869d-80d9df29f8fe</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump won a series of key battlegrounds early on Wednesday morning, including Florida, Ohio and Iowa, as Joseph R. Biden Jr. expressed confidence he would ultimately prevail across key Northern states and Arizona as the presidential contest turned into a state-by-state slog that could drag deeper into the week.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ebf4f94d-a728-4327-b424-d347782b7b17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bb11978d-1ef3-48f3-b313-8a406730783e">
		<rdfs:label>article-bb11978d-1ef3-48f3-b313-8a406730783e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The case, from California, could affect the regulation of “dark money” in political contests.</rdfs:comment>
