	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-be934906-c75f-4a7a-8baf-588696a99027">
		<rdfs:label>article-be934906-c75f-4a7a-8baf-588696a99027</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>At 1:51 p.m. on Jan. 6, a right-wing radio host named Michael D. Brown wrote on Twitter that rioters had breached the United States Capitol — and immediately speculated about who was really to blame. “Antifa or BLM or other insurgents could be doing it disguised as Trump supporters,” Mr. Brown wrote, using shorthand for Black Lives Matter. “Come on, man, have you never heard of psyops?”</rdfs:comment>
