	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bf71e028-519b-4e08-8062-fe93716b5f50">
		<rdfs:label>article-bf71e028-519b-4e08-8062-fe93716b5f50</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Manhattan district attorney can enforce a subpoena seeking President Trump’s personal and corporate tax returns, a federal appeals panel ruled on Wednesday, dealing yet another blow to the president’s yearlong battle to deny prosecutors his financial records.</rdfs:comment>
