	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bfe7bc98-c35b-4b04-80b4-c5c401167002">
		<rdfs:label>article-bfe7bc98-c35b-4b04-80b4-c5c401167002</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Former President Donald J. Trump’s lawyers denied on Tuesday that he incited the deadly assault on the Capitol and argued that the Senate had no power to try a former president, as House prosecutors made their case that Mr. Trump was “singularly responsible” for the Jan. 6 rampage and must be convicted and barred from holding any future office.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bfe99ec2-60d9-4288-a882-0574771d30cb">
		<rdfs:label>article-bfe99ec2-60d9-4288-a882-0574771d30cb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Tuesday: An update on the state’s plagued unemployment system. Also: California’s changing of the guard.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-14f82d09-3a15-43b0-8f6d-ebdb1405d989"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-738c55e5-1f96-4b93-8c70-fc8c1c8c9119"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bfea5fb8-a07f-41c2-b69f-cdc89872c0b5">
		<rdfs:label>article-bfea5fb8-a07f-41c2-b69f-cdc89872c0b5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Sue Biniaz is considered one of the most innovative American legal minds when it comes to climate negotiations. She once rescued a collapsing deal by using quotation marks.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b1afb246-66b2-4eea-8ebc-1b5c7f6c7900"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bfeca6ed-6888-40b3-8108-74668c14761d">
		<rdfs:label>article-bfeca6ed-6888-40b3-8108-74668c14761d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The vote in the Senate was 98-0. The House voted 411-11; the opponents were six progressive Democrats known as “the Squad” and five ultra-conservative Republicans.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bfedd04a-22ae-4a6e-9242-98d2ca1e7f0d">
		<rdfs:label>article-bfedd04a-22ae-4a6e-9242-98d2ca1e7f0d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Ms. Winfrey was instrumental in the rise of Dr. Mehmet Oz, the celebrity television doctor and Republican Senate nominee, but she has announced her support for John Fetterman, his Democratic opponent.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8eb0923f-854c-4241-9d79-040d1aeeb0c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c2e66850-f7bc-45ca-83ed-c0a1f8490a14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bfedd0d9-bfde-4124-aad6-3e1c1c0a8253">
		<rdfs:label>article-bfedd0d9-bfde-4124-aad6-3e1c1c0a8253</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mr. Collins, a former Republican congressman and ardent defender of former President Trump, was seen as an experienced potential challenger to Senator Raphael Warnock or Gov. Brian Kemp.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-93d154d3-6d3d-4599-ac55-e63a146d8d6f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d7a0b17f-e0aa-44c5-a995-e81e028fa879"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bff0a603-508c-43e3-a0c7-b508b8b03e8a">
		<rdfs:label>article-bff0a603-508c-43e3-a0c7-b508b8b03e8a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The civil rights leader was eulogized by former presidents and family in Atlanta, the city he represented in Congress for more than three decades.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d7a0b17f-e0aa-44c5-a995-e81e028fa879"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc5a47b7-5e7e-4d58-8ee7-caaf2f703c6a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bff1923a-8eac-4080-92dc-2711af50b3cc">
		<rdfs:label>article-bff1923a-8eac-4080-92dc-2711af50b3cc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats on Tuesday night are seeking to straddle themes of national security, American unity and generational change, with an array of speakers from the Democratic Party’s past — like Bill Clinton and John F. Kerry — and a few who appear to represent its future, like Representative Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3488268a-8b17-411a-8185-6859abbab9a8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bffa453e-eb1f-4b4d-93e7-449a2d5577a9">
		<rdfs:label>article-bffa453e-eb1f-4b4d-93e7-449a2d5577a9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Officials recommend donning a long-sleeved shirt and heavy-work gloves to avoid cuts while gathering debris and household waste.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-74fe9339-5cba-4d49-b38d-2ccc7bfafd17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bffaa54d-575b-490c-aab2-37d163dd33b9">
		<rdfs:label>article-bffaa54d-575b-490c-aab2-37d163dd33b9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Only two provisions in a once-sprawling social spending package have survived; they would lower prescription drug prices in Medicare and insurance premiums for millions of Americans.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-576a9017-d1c0-4a28-b730-97415c0f4ae4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-bffbf91e-a048-41d6-b0a8-fd4e28e4bc76">
		<rdfs:label>article-bffbf91e-a048-41d6-b0a8-fd4e28e4bc76</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After the mass shooting at an elementary school in his home state, the senator called for armed law enforcement on campuses and faulted Democrats for politicizing the issue.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c003e12a-b47e-4b99-ac96-3199a4745632">
		<rdfs:label>article-c003e12a-b47e-4b99-ac96-3199a4745632</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>South Dakota has four dead presidents carved in stone on Mount Rushmore. But good luck getting real, live presidential hopefuls to come visit.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-25bd1b00-90b4-453a-8e46-dfb93ba723f0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c003f0e0-d749-40d1-aa9c-e1d384e12f8f">
		<rdfs:label>article-c003f0e0-d749-40d1-aa9c-e1d384e12f8f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Republican senator from Wisconsin is known for regularly promoting fringe theories favored by the right, most recently questioning the fact that pro-Trump rioters attacked the Capitol.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c009811f-6310-49a0-a66c-1b9bb7df3cce">
		<rdfs:label>article-c009811f-6310-49a0-a66c-1b9bb7df3cce</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Nadima Sahar, a government official, was determined to stay. But then she learned the palace staff, and maybe even the president, had already fled.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-456258fe-24f9-4e37-a244-c99808a00014"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c00aba0d-e32f-436b-b49f-2269518184ec">
		<rdfs:label>article-c00aba0d-e32f-436b-b49f-2269518184ec</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The majority leader’s announcement ratchets up pressure for Republicans and Democrats to finalize the details of the still-unfinished bipartisan infrastructure deal.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c00f24cc-c721-45f0-9bde-8ebf2864a326">
		<rdfs:label>article-c00f24cc-c721-45f0-9bde-8ebf2864a326</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The court cited “persuasive evidence” that the state legislature had rushed the law to passage at least in part to make it harder for Black voters to cast ballots.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-be4a3e54-4b34-4f4b-b446-90f3692a587d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c00f6d4f-0167-4cea-a1c6-587904676633">
		<rdfs:label>article-c00f6d4f-0167-4cea-a1c6-587904676633</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The former president and his allies have given often conflicting defenses of his retention of classified documents, without addressing why he had kept them.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c010dfbb-5fc8-4ad6-b108-af76f6d05bb1">
		<rdfs:label>article-c010dfbb-5fc8-4ad6-b108-af76f6d05bb1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As a case before the Supreme Court threatens Roe v. Wade and Democrats’ urgency grows, many activists believe the president needs to be bolder in defending reproductive rights.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c01129c1-9131-478d-a258-4a5f830d5288">
		<rdfs:label>article-c01129c1-9131-478d-a258-4a5f830d5288</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Before senators could get started on the charge against former President Donald J. Trump, they spent the afternoon on Tuesday debating whether they had the right to try a former president in the first place.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dad1523a-f983-4f0f-af53-0061c7165e91"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c014e0ab-8639-4aef-ac49-774004f1c027">
		<rdfs:label>article-c014e0ab-8639-4aef-ac49-774004f1c027</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Can sports fandom teach us how to depolarize the country?</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-175a5716-4ad1-49dd-b8f5-c08af878b76d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c0159122-e2d6-4a6a-9433-877d2be63feb">
		<rdfs:label>article-c0159122-e2d6-4a6a-9433-877d2be63feb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Representative Elaine Luria of Virginia knows the coming hearings could be a political liability for her in a Republican-leaning district. “If I don’t get re-elected because of this, that’s OK.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-803bdb8f-8c3c-4210-80c9-22b0af3fd2ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c0172585-9244-45af-95dc-c83a7e27a3a0">
		<rdfs:label>article-c0172585-9244-45af-95dc-c83a7e27a3a0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The former New York mayor’s dirt-digging effort on Hunter Biden in 2019 ended with President Trump’s impeachment. Now he is back with new associates. So far it is not going exactly as planned.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-982bde63-8146-432c-a09a-c9cac220ddaa"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9fcaaf17-51fe-4de9-aec7-f53a415e4396"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c0196120-2f0f-4815-95e5-729891fe67af">
		<rdfs:label>article-c0196120-2f0f-4815-95e5-729891fe67af</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A civil war broke out in the group as it antagonized Donald Trump, with leaders splintering over financial arrangements and revelations of online harassment by a top official.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8a5b6958-a2db-4e3b-991a-f44ef9ac57d0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ac748b00-7205-45e9-ba20-53ddfa903a7f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c01fa0a0-771a-441c-b314-9eef763477e0">
		<rdfs:label>article-c01fa0a0-771a-441c-b314-9eef763477e0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden acknowledged that the immediate demands of the presidency, including the pandemic and war in Ukraine, have taken him away from his domestic agenda.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd42dd7e-7a0d-4a74-908e-252de023edfb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c021516e-a7e9-4129-9a50-6901a0b1be4e">
		<rdfs:label>article-c021516e-a7e9-4129-9a50-6901a0b1be4e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Ahead of Tuesday’s primary, about 30 percent of absentee ballots were rejected in the state’s most populous counties. In 2020, the statewide rejection rate was less than 1 percent.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-93d154d3-6d3d-4599-ac55-e63a146d8d6f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c029b7b8-d13a-42d6-9a04-8d858b01d0f2">
		<rdfs:label>article-c029b7b8-d13a-42d6-9a04-8d858b01d0f2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>He lied about the coronavirus anyway.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c02d0d96-eb49-487a-bc95-b215725ff419">
		<rdfs:label>article-c02d0d96-eb49-487a-bc95-b215725ff419</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After Virginia passed gun laws, conservatives began invoking the state’s colonial-era constitution, which calls for a “well regulated militia.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ae47edf3-29dc-462d-b74b-f886ebf56402"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c0339466-218f-407e-827a-b1b9d1b7f327">
		<rdfs:label>article-c0339466-218f-407e-827a-b1b9d1b7f327</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president’s result came after he spent months playing down the severity of the outbreak that has killed more than 207,000 in the United States and hours after insisting that “the end of the pandemic is in sight.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-922ad7b9-e6de-456a-9bc2-69207748d175"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c036b229-ae0b-4fcf-99cc-4bff7d7cdbe2">
		<rdfs:label>article-c036b229-ae0b-4fcf-99cc-4bff7d7cdbe2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Officials in Surfside, Fla., now estimate that the total number of dead will be between 95 and 99 people.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c03da15d-41b6-4a99-93cb-324f89805754">
		<rdfs:label>article-c03da15d-41b6-4a99-93cb-324f89805754</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Her status is the consequence of Justice Stephen G. Breyer’s early and conditional announcement of his retirement.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-947ed571-ad87-49fb-b59a-9372d166d3c7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c03e3396-36b2-4d28-a52c-221d452fbdbc">
		<rdfs:label>article-c03e3396-36b2-4d28-a52c-221d452fbdbc</rdfs:label>
