	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c0d20c22-34e7-46ea-89a1-0f1d839391ff">
		<rdfs:label>article-c0d20c22-34e7-46ea-89a1-0f1d839391ff</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Senator Mitt Romney called the commutation an act of “unprecedented, historic corruption.” Attorney General William P. Barr privately argued against clemency for the president’s friend.</rdfs:comment>
