		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c22e0214-f34c-488f-bc94-c7cd85e320e4">
		<rdfs:label>article-c22e0214-f34c-488f-bc94-c7cd85e320e4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Judge Ketanji Brown Jackson, after hours of intense questioning during her confirmation hearing last month, delivered a message to young people who hoped to follow her path: “I want them to know that they can do and be anything.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-be4afe5b-5317-4441-a7de-57071d96016d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c2389c34-1d10-42e4-aa7a-91ad9ffec0f5">
		<rdfs:label>article-c2389c34-1d10-42e4-aa7a-91ad9ffec0f5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Workers at one restaurant decided they would serve dinner in a kind of defiant love for their community, which has not always felt welcome in a conservative area that was once a center of anti-gay activism.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b0d8acac-ba33-4091-b922-0eb5b9ab904d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
