	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c28099d2-d11c-47ed-90d4-30f1b7572e93">
		<rdfs:label>article-c28099d2-d11c-47ed-90d4-30f1b7572e93</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump comfortably carried Chaska, Minn., in 2016. This time, he lost by nine percentage points — a dramatic shift that similarly played out in suburban counties across the country.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-295dc04c-bd5c-4dba-9271-bfd8a89ba851"/>
