	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c28763c2-8ea8-4b86-b1aa-5c03a583d66c">
		<rdfs:label>article-c28763c2-8ea8-4b86-b1aa-5c03a583d66c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Brett Hankison, the only officer who was charged after the police raid, fired 10 bullets into Ms. Taylor’s apartment. Three pierced a wall and flew into another apartment where a family slept.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e993acb7-fd71-489b-b569-b6b6d449dfe5"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c28f08fb-bfaa-4edd-90d9-bf56b15999fa">
		<rdfs:label>article-c28f08fb-bfaa-4edd-90d9-bf56b15999fa</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After decades of betrayals and broken treaties, the Supreme Court ruled that much of Oklahoma is their land, after all.</rdfs:comment>
