	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c29cd094-ebc6-4df9-a27e-acfe0f6f0e5a">
		<rdfs:label>article-c29cd094-ebc6-4df9-a27e-acfe0f6f0e5a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats are defending more than a dozen seats in which the incumbent has said they will not run for re-election, complicating their effort to stop Republicans from reclaiming the House majority.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c2a0375b-a2b0-4f2c-a5c3-77fba13b494a">
		<rdfs:label>article-c2a0375b-a2b0-4f2c-a5c3-77fba13b494a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The state has passed a flurry of pro-housing laws in recent years. But there was little enforcement — until recently.</rdfs:comment>
