	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c3ae8012-8317-4ba8-bc6f-6402dd0aac91">
		<rdfs:label>article-c3ae8012-8317-4ba8-bc6f-6402dd0aac91</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The conditions at the prison, while extreme, reflect wider problems in the Bureau of Prisons’ sprawling network of 122 facilities housing about 158,000 inmates.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7479f929-0522-4f1f-a391-dcdb5f4e726c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c3b071d7-ff80-4dce-9534-987462cc5a49">
		<rdfs:label>article-c3b071d7-ff80-4dce-9534-987462cc5a49</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats increasingly regard winning the Senate as their last remaining check on President Trump, should he win re-election, while Republicans fight to maintain power in Congress.</rdfs:comment>
