	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c3bd07ff-87bb-4fbd-b2d4-3ef8aa0cbe08">
		<rdfs:label>article-c3bd07ff-87bb-4fbd-b2d4-3ef8aa0cbe08</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Vice President Mike Pence, in a bold statement on Wednesday afternoon, rejected President Trump’s pressure to block congressional certification of President-elect Joseph R. Biden Jr.’s victory in the presidential election, claiming that he lacked the “unilateral authority” to decide the outcome of the presidential election.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c67a9047-7b94-4e45-aaa9-c820c2b967de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c3c0101e-28c7-4b7a-a91d-eea87bce3e9c">
		<rdfs:label>article-c3c0101e-28c7-4b7a-a91d-eea87bce3e9c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>We spoke with Kendra James, the author of “Admissions: A Memoir of Surviving Boarding School.”</rdfs:comment>
