	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c45d9964-ffd9-4430-98cc-7f21fdff5a27">
		<rdfs:label>article-c45d9964-ffd9-4430-98cc-7f21fdff5a27</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>American officials said China had insisted that the Justice Department not proceed with cases against the arrested scholars, who are in the Chinese military and face charges of visa fraud.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b32f6625-044c-4b5c-a23c-681cb2a901f9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c45dbd3a-c126-439c-8c9c-7c42e262567f">
		<rdfs:label>article-c45dbd3a-c126-439c-8c9c-7c42e262567f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Senator David Perdue, one of two Republican senators from Georgia facing runoff elections in January, began making large and ultimately profitable purchases of shares in a Navy contractor in 2018 just before taking over as chair of a Senate subcommittee overseeing the Navy fleet.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-21d856ad-a6ae-406e-a9e4-9707218ad815"/>
