		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4656e90-e608-49a0-a324-73e17e7f9958">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4656e90-e608-49a0-a324-73e17e7f9958</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Tennessee Valley Authority, an electric utility, quickly said it would reconsider its move to shift some work to contractors outside the United States.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c468d240-42c6-4a9e-ba12-88c567bd2f32">
		<rdfs:label>article-c468d240-42c6-4a9e-ba12-88c567bd2f32</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The justices appeared ready to rule that people and companies need not wait for administrative rulings to press constitutional claims in federal court.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-947ed571-ad87-49fb-b59a-9372d166d3c7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f9cc56c-65dd-4b26-8e31-cb0c48bf78ea"/>
