		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c46b0ec2-4a5d-41f4-a00a-1a9ebbe607f4">
		<rdfs:label>article-c46b0ec2-4a5d-41f4-a00a-1a9ebbe607f4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president issued calls to ‘LIBERATE’ states, and several announced plans to ease restrictions. At least 7,000 of the virus deaths in the U.S. are connected to nursing homes.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c46b875d-ef3b-4453-aa3d-f609a6d82803">
		<rdfs:label>article-c46b875d-ef3b-4453-aa3d-f609a6d82803</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The ad, which calls Joe Biden soft on China and falsely suggests a former governor of Washington is Chinese, shows that President Trump plans to continue exploiting racial discord in his re-election bid.</rdfs:comment>
