		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4d392ab-4139-436b-90ab-8b3ec735d124">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4d392ab-4139-436b-90ab-8b3ec735d124</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With nearly two-thirds of House Republicans supporting Texas’s lawsuit seeking to overturn the election in the U.S. Supreme Court, a Democratic House member on Friday called the Republicans “traitors” and urged the House’s Democratic leadership not to seat the Republicans when the 117th Congress convenes in January.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e008be05-6dcb-45fe-a5d2-1657eb3a638f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e0dfbf0e-c179-4f28-a968-4570f9209555"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4da6aca-e641-4ea9-8387-cf8c8e9fec65">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4da6aca-e641-4ea9-8387-cf8c8e9fec65</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The owner said he and his employees were paying close attention.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-897bdd49-0795-48a5-8ca5-c72b9463a727"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4df97eb-2261-473d-9fe6-f931aaa16f29">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4df97eb-2261-473d-9fe6-f931aaa16f29</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Justice Ruth Bader Ginsburg broke one final barrier on Friday, becoming the first woman and the first Jewish American to lie in state in the United States Capitol.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4e0cd8d-efeb-48a2-921a-0a75bce2330a">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4e0cd8d-efeb-48a2-921a-0a75bce2330a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Dr. Anthony S. Fauci said the administration was optimistic that “we’re not going to see a repeat of what we saw last year,” when the Omicron variant swept through the country.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3263b980-a580-440f-bdd2-6d7fa7bb3fab"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-42dfcd52-8183-4ae1-ba08-c61dc31db2c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4e0d95c-9c0a-4f8b-b959-88b14f1c53ff">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4e0d95c-9c0a-4f8b-b959-88b14f1c53ff</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The annual total of shootings involving an attacker “attempting to kill people in a populated area” has nearly doubled since 2017.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7479f929-0522-4f1f-a391-dcdb5f4e726c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4e18653-470e-4573-87bd-6354ab34cdf7">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4e18653-470e-4573-87bd-6354ab34cdf7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>An American military official said the warplanes were conducting combat missions in support of Kremlin-backed private security forces, and extending Moscow’s influence in Africa.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5a3094b1-6bc7-47d7-8f53-c56fd8ed0c59"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4e400b5-deca-46c5-ac1f-0f59e912b049">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4e400b5-deca-46c5-ac1f-0f59e912b049</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The general election began another phase tonight, with Joseph R. Biden Jr. holding a town hall and President Trump following with an outdoor rally — events that reflected the starkly different approach each man has taken to the coronavirus pandemic.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-577cfa39-5806-4396-ae24-cdf4ba406715"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4e62385-f3e4-4b62-874e-8d96ff110c83">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4e62385-f3e4-4b62-874e-8d96ff110c83</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With international travel returning to prepandemic levels, these floppy-eared hounds are sniffing out deadly diseases and pests at border crossings one mango or sausage at a time.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-be4afe5b-5317-4441-a7de-57071d96016d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4e79224-5af3-4f47-8eef-f7b8f7a235c9">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4e79224-5af3-4f47-8eef-f7b8f7a235c9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Vladimir V. Putin long dismissed the threat posed by global warming. But fires, disasters and foreign pressure have prompted him to change course.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3736c242-e9c8-48de-a3ec-df1ab3191621"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fa61234c-4421-402f-96fd-769b4698358d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4e79fee-2200-44fa-92b8-4720e9a40a83">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4e79fee-2200-44fa-92b8-4720e9a40a83</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>American manufacturers are worried that China’s zero-tolerance coronavirus policy could throw a wrench in the global conveyor belt for goods this year.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-94d58c04-d925-44a3-9534-35b73b8dc25d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f2af28a7-8b31-4967-88f9-b1f127e77a58"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4ef2ed9-ed29-4e6b-bde9-ec7c3130618d">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4ef2ed9-ed29-4e6b-bde9-ec7c3130618d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The administration is closing in on deals with some close allies, but agreements with powers like China, Brazil and India are proving difficult.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b1afb246-66b2-4eea-8ebc-1b5c7f6c7900"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4f2d3a3-381d-45a0-bb26-2749bf6bb5dc">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4f2d3a3-381d-45a0-bb26-2749bf6bb5dc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In recent months, Republican skepticism of Covid vaccines and their rollout has grown louder: One recent poll found that 47 percent said they weren’t likely to get vaccinated.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4f54315-fcbc-401e-ad09-281ca0e24d9a">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4f54315-fcbc-401e-ad09-281ca0e24d9a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In a test of its power to impose indefinite detention, the administration asked two appeals courts to stop a lower court from freeing a stateless man who has completed his prison term.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4bd6cfaa-ebec-415a-8c53-2870f770bfa7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4f9288d-3fde-4bd7-ab2e-2c803776fc3b">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4f9288d-3fde-4bd7-ab2e-2c803776fc3b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Kremlin is trying to find enough reinforcements to conduct the next phase of the war, according to military and intelligence officials.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-46b2f3e2-fc43-4d1f-8134-a17365f8ec33"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5a3094b1-6bc7-47d7-8f53-c56fd8ed0c59"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6f60db0f-4977-4567-b7bd-9abe5d4a35e8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4feea80-575f-41cc-9a3e-5ec7eafa2023">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4feea80-575f-41cc-9a3e-5ec7eafa2023</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Researchers are drilling down into the ways life on a hotter planet will tax our bodies, and looking for protections that, unlike air-conditioning, don’t make the problem worse.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f47e8c73-b108-4497-8696-b024a69f280e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c4ffde8f-5bc8-467a-b864-c245e0fd6896">
		<rdfs:label>article-c4ffde8f-5bc8-467a-b864-c245e0fd6896</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>There were worrisome signs for the president in a State Supreme Court race in a key battleground state, but also a few cautionary signals for Democrats looking to seize on the result as a glimmer of good news.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ebf4f94d-a728-4327-b424-d347782b7b17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-04-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c50488a7-0749-4202-a09e-57b27d22c97a">
		<rdfs:label>article-c50488a7-0749-4202-a09e-57b27d22c97a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Tuesday’s appearance by Defense Secretary Lloyd J. Austin III, Gen. Mark A. Milley and Gen. Kenneth F. McKenzie, Jr. was the start of back-to-back Senate and House hearings.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-46b2f3e2-fc43-4d1f-8134-a17365f8ec33"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5a3094b1-6bc7-47d7-8f53-c56fd8ed0c59"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c5077084-e5c7-4c29-b37b-a4813efd8b56">
		<rdfs:label>article-c5077084-e5c7-4c29-b37b-a4813efd8b56</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Two Trump administration officials have been reassigned over the posting of debunked papers, with the imprimatur of the White House, that questioned the scientific consensus on climate change.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-74659e03-2c48-4140-91f4-08e5d544f77a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b1afb246-66b2-4eea-8ebc-1b5c7f6c7900"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c508a637-3c73-42c1-8199-d724354c54ed">
		<rdfs:label>article-c508a637-3c73-42c1-8199-d724354c54ed</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The number of people still unaccounted for is 156. The mayor of Miami-Dade County said three bodies have been identified.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c509cab0-9e70-45c3-b0d2-63b79a888453">
		<rdfs:label>article-c509cab0-9e70-45c3-b0d2-63b79a888453</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The billionaire former New York City mayor has concentrated largely on Florida in the general election. But his private polling found President Trump vulnerable in two of the country’s biggest red states.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3488268a-8b17-411a-8185-6859abbab9a8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c50d2b5c-1a30-433b-87cf-36c72655e103">
		<rdfs:label>article-c50d2b5c-1a30-433b-87cf-36c72655e103</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As of Friday afternoon, the National Network of Abortion Funds had received more than $3 million from about 33,000 new donations.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0d90a39b-aa49-4139-9fd4-2b321395efa6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c50e82ef-11d1-4a50-b9b5-e3c42f20a4ca">
		<rdfs:label>article-c50e82ef-11d1-4a50-b9b5-e3c42f20a4ca</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Louisiana is leading the nation in an explosion of new cases. Hospitals are overflowing and admitting more young people than before. But the crisis is also driving some to get vaccinated.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc5a47b7-5e7e-4d58-8ee7-caaf2f703c6a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c50f3d94-0243-4f67-9093-378ded19b16f">
		<rdfs:label>article-c50f3d94-0243-4f67-9093-378ded19b16f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The International Criminal Court has collected evidence of what it says is torture, rape and other crimes by American forces during the war in Afghanistan.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f4f38f08-6492-4112-8b82-52bd8aa6b34f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc2c2b47-32c2-43a0-8e5f-dd4e72335932"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c511cffa-7b67-48ea-aefe-970b0c6760b7">
		<rdfs:label>article-c511cffa-7b67-48ea-aefe-970b0c6760b7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Policies passed in 2020 included universal background checks, reporting requirements for lost or stolen firearms, a limit of one handgun purchase per month for most people, and a red-flag law.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c5126a46-3642-4191-8486-38f9de7c774f">
		<rdfs:label>article-c5126a46-3642-4191-8486-38f9de7c774f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Massachusetts and Michigan this week joined the parade of U.S. states that have introduced lotteries for residents who get Covid-19 shots, seeking to bolster vaccinations with titles like “Shot of a Lifetime,” “Vax for the Win,” “Comeback Cash” and even “Do It for Babydog” (thanks, West Virginia).</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c431cec6-53e9-48e0-a3c8-38432e75646c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e2ba983e-eb48-483d-afa1-e67b02e88f99"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c5131477-693b-419b-be2a-eca9d9bfb696">
		<rdfs:label>article-c5131477-693b-419b-be2a-eca9d9bfb696</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Gutted by the Trump administration, the refugee resettlement system is unable to quickly process tens of thousands of the world’s neediest people.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f4f38f08-6492-4112-8b82-52bd8aa6b34f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c513b44e-6706-4a72-b283-63918701d30e">
		<rdfs:label>article-c513b44e-6706-4a72-b283-63918701d30e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>WILMINGTON, Del. — Joseph R. Biden Jr. was elected president of the United States on Saturday, defeating President Trump after campaigning on a promise to restore civility and stability to American politics and to expand the government’s role in guiding the country through the surging coronavirus pandemic.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8eb0923f-854c-4241-9d79-040d1aeeb0c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c51455e2-362f-427d-9658-1a94c03e84db">
		<rdfs:label>article-c51455e2-362f-427d-9658-1a94c03e84db</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Amid a record spike of coronavirus cases, President Trump and his administration have expressed increasing helplessness at containing the virus, focusing instead on improvements in survivability and trying to hold the economy together.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-becd702f-c674-4653-9a6c-90ee51977e85"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c51b379c-2936-4f54-b471-ad8dedc5d106">
		<rdfs:label>article-c51b379c-2936-4f54-b471-ad8dedc5d106</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president had hoped to win credit for ending one of America’s “forever wars.” But new risks are coming into view.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc2c2b47-32c2-43a0-8e5f-dd4e72335932"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c5201c00-b5e1-44ae-a81c-9ce22b6b44de">
		<rdfs:label>article-c5201c00-b5e1-44ae-a81c-9ce22b6b44de</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Thousands of demonstrators poured into streets across the nation, marching over the Brooklyn Bridge and gathering outside City Hall in Seattle.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c5225776-0096-4ac2-87c0-a99ce1aa1ed5">
		<rdfs:label>article-c5225776-0096-4ac2-87c0-a99ce1aa1ed5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mixing, matching and twisting facts about the coronavirus online, Mr. Kirk has created a template for a new kind of political agitator.</rdfs:comment>
