		<rdfs:label>article-c53313c4-b977-4370-9cfe-e797d98fb394</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Nearly 80 percent of American high school juniors and seniors say the coronavirus pandemic has affected their plans after graduation, and 72 percent of 13- to 19-year-olds have struggled with their mental health, a new survey shows.</rdfs:comment>
