		<rdfs:label>article-c70e068d-5021-4a4a-bac2-2fb6b08b6b2f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Senator David Perdue, the Georgia Republican facing a runoff election that could determine the control of the Senate, made 2,596 stock trades in one term in office, including, at times, 20 or more transactions in a single day.</rdfs:comment>
