		<rdfs:label>article-c71409d5-171d-4207-bea3-bf2f5831a6db</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>One of Washington’s leading conservative constitutional lawyers publicly broke on Sunday with the main Republican argument against convicting former President Donald J. Trump in his impeachment trial, asserting that a former president can indeed be tried for high crimes and misdemeanors.</rdfs:comment>
