	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c7228b3a-9ef2-4d3b-b09d-e7e01bded90c">
		<rdfs:label>article-c7228b3a-9ef2-4d3b-b09d-e7e01bded90c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Faced with soaring coronavirus caseloads, some universities told students to “stay put” for 14 days. College journalists report from their quarantined campuses.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-c7266c22-d6f6-40a4-9a7f-b63e10d52c99">
		<rdfs:label>article-c7266c22-d6f6-40a4-9a7f-b63e10d52c99</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>An initiative to define what makes jobs bad or good is long overdue.</rdfs:comment>
