		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-cac489a0-29c0-4c58-b6c5-e57172bcc983">
		<rdfs:label>article-cac489a0-29c0-4c58-b6c5-e57172bcc983</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Hillary Clinton, speaking candidly during an online fund-raiser Monday, counseled Kamala Harris to “modulate” her responses during her upcoming debate with Vice President Mike Pence to avoid a sexist “double standard” that portrays strong female leaders as frightening.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7479f929-0522-4f1f-a391-dcdb5f4e726c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-cac6d0df-ad30-4cf7-83d3-7aa3e9be6671">
		<rdfs:label>article-cac6d0df-ad30-4cf7-83d3-7aa3e9be6671</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Joe Biden leads President Trump, 50 percent to 41 percent, a New York Times/Siena College poll shows, with voters favoring him by wide margins on the coronavirus and law and order.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3488268a-8b17-411a-8185-6859abbab9a8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
