		<rdfs:label>article-cb976d5d-8557-423c-8f50-c78d71a45391</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As jockeying begins for 2024, rank-and-file Republicans say they are most drawn to leaders who both pledge fealty to the former president and appear to showcase a distinct political identity.</rdfs:comment>
