	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d143b769-a5e8-4c01-b556-6bc9676822e6">
		<rdfs:label>article-d143b769-a5e8-4c01-b556-6bc9676822e6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The $900 billion stimulus bill passed by Congress this week is meant to address the needs of millions of Americans who have weathered the effects of the coronavirus pandemic for months, even as many federal programs to provide aid ran thin or expired.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-011ddbd5-8a1e-4932-8bfc-bad05d0ca67f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d14f768d-e596-4066-9172-af87bb49ce7d">
		<rdfs:label>article-d14f768d-e596-4066-9172-af87bb49ce7d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The House panel painted a detailed picture of how, as officials rushed to respond to an attack on the United States government, the commander in chief chose for hours to do nothing.</rdfs:comment>
