		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d17f75b2-b63c-421f-9aa0-376f50bc88f9">
		<rdfs:label>article-d17f75b2-b63c-421f-9aa0-376f50bc88f9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Prosecutors said Mr. Flynn, President Trump’s first national security adviser, had “chosen to reverse course” on cooperating and accepting guilt after they had previously argued for a lenient sentence.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3a4b0b1a-f7a7-498e-8805-48a907d13871"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d1857ced-c176-4ece-9463-052093ee0376">
		<rdfs:label>article-d1857ced-c176-4ece-9463-052093ee0376</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>House Republicans on the Intelligence Committee expressed support for law enforcement. As for lawmakers saying otherwise? “Question them, not us.”</rdfs:comment>
