	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d2798a0b-a963-46ad-99e7-e487305bc0ea">
		<rdfs:label>article-d2798a0b-a963-46ad-99e7-e487305bc0ea</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A caravan of semis, pickups and R.V.s that had driven across the United States to protest vaccine mandates and other Covid restrictions reached the capital region this week, but as the convoy circled the city, downtown Washington was business as usual.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-12f05d49-4556-4d47-ade2-4ee0e5fd9494"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-90788841-2a13-4598-abd3-3b677caff4d4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ae47edf3-29dc-462d-b74b-f886ebf56402"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d27be284-35d8-4250-8df5-5cc61a07f8a6">
		<rdfs:label>article-d27be284-35d8-4250-8df5-5cc61a07f8a6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After Lt. Gov. John Fetterman’s stroke in May, the campaigns agreed that questions and statements will also be displayed on large monitors.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c2e66850-f7bc-45ca-83ed-c0a1f8490a14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d27ceb18-58fa-4113-8354-df320925654d">
		<rdfs:label>article-d27ceb18-58fa-4113-8354-df320925654d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The decision dealt a blow to Joe Biden, who had hoped his longstanding ties to organized labor would win him the union’s coveted support.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d27f15d3-cb37-4a99-8498-7333daeb1998">
		<rdfs:label>article-d27f15d3-cb37-4a99-8498-7333daeb1998</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Charlene and James Slaugh were both wounded at Club Q. Families impacted by hundreds of mass shootings this year face a tough holiday season.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b0d8acac-ba33-4091-b922-0eb5b9ab904d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-26"/>
