	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d28da386-2b1d-433f-86ef-f5882aab6556">
		<rdfs:label>article-d28da386-2b1d-433f-86ef-f5882aab6556</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>PERRY, GA — Republican senators toed a careful line in central Georgia on Thursday, seeking to rally their base for the January runoff without acknowledging the reality that President Trump lost his bid for re-election.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4504805-5b5f-41c7-b157-41ff04a342ad"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d28e99a6-4528-4297-86ed-8e7a9cd1fa25">
		<rdfs:label>article-d28e99a6-4528-4297-86ed-8e7a9cd1fa25</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>It might be burning, drying up, wildly expensive and slipping into the sea, but our readers adore it all the same.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-1e5cee4f-82a8-44a6-9cc0-9285f4da7bf4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d29440cc-53bc-4b51-8936-064cd71a69bf">
		<rdfs:label>article-d29440cc-53bc-4b51-8936-064cd71a69bf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Most Americans say the former president bears responsibility for the Capitol attack by his supporters, but a slimmer majority is in favor of convicting him at the Senate’s impeachment trial.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-887d1269-7020-4c8e-8dfc-eae7c464f3cb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d298cd64-1c7d-4151-9099-7f1ab7243f4a">
		<rdfs:label>article-d298cd64-1c7d-4151-9099-7f1ab7243f4a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Dr. Anthony S. Fauci, 81, said he expected to see out President Biden’s current term.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d29b2a6f-bdb3-43a3-b13e-b3932dd54bb1">
		<rdfs:label>article-d29b2a6f-bdb3-43a3-b13e-b3932dd54bb1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The chief executives of the country and its biggest city have found themselves diminished as leaders, lacking the trust of the people they serve.</rdfs:comment>
