	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d3e42eea-e723-421a-8f35-79393e62bd34">
		<rdfs:label>article-d3e42eea-e723-421a-8f35-79393e62bd34</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Twitter said on Friday that it had permanently suspended President Trump from its service “due to the risk of further incitement for violence,” effectively cutting him off from his favorite method of communicating with the public and capping a series of actions by mainstream sites to limit his online reach.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-191d01a1-fded-4f58-8cc1-12c80f5f00df"/>
