		<rdfs:label>article-d56eed81-6a3c-444a-8458-41c740d29f59</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>MADISON, Wis. — Wisconsin’s municipal clerks are nearly finished counting the state’s ballots, and former Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. has a lead of slightly more than 20,000 votes over President Trump, said Ann Jacobs, the chairwoman of the Wisconsin Elections Commission.</rdfs:comment>
