		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d64a49d7-d9ab-4957-8cd6-91419f0c3e1e">
		<rdfs:label>article-d64a49d7-d9ab-4957-8cd6-91419f0c3e1e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In a wealthy suburban Philadelphia district, schools are struggling with shortages of all sorts. Behavioral problems have mushroomed. “We are in triage mode,” one teacher said.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ae47edf3-29dc-462d-b74b-f886ebf56402"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-12-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d64c175e-5697-4108-a52c-007ef78c7ee2">
		<rdfs:label>article-d64c175e-5697-4108-a52c-007ef78c7ee2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The military’s first active-duty case, in South Korea, has commanders preparing a battle plan. But steps meant to stave off the virus may also compromise training and readiness.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fd9f1ad4-cd49-4185-a0bb-a129097c5a29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d64c837a-f29f-4f28-b21c-2d4241173ada">
		<rdfs:label>article-d64c837a-f29f-4f28-b21c-2d4241173ada</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>What happens when the biggest election reform bill in half a century runs into one of the most formidable barriers to American governance?</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d64cb4a0-608e-4616-b1df-f33e1f3d83e6">
		<rdfs:label>article-d64cb4a0-608e-4616-b1df-f33e1f3d83e6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The former news anchor is running on falsehoods about the 2020 election. She is undeterred about her chances in November: ‘I am beloved by people.’</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d8482953-a125-4fa7-a4ef-dc645e3472e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-10"/>
