	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d6acda38-62c1-4154-998e-2af5b66f90bb">
		<rdfs:label>article-d6acda38-62c1-4154-998e-2af5b66f90bb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Dixie Fire has devoured acre after acre of rugged wildland to become the second largest blaze in California history. But it and other megafires in the West have left a footprint much larger than the evergreen forests they level and the towns they decimate.</rdfs:comment>
