	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d71db93e-de7f-41bc-8d1a-7d2992c6addd">
		<rdfs:label>article-d71db93e-de7f-41bc-8d1a-7d2992c6addd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The White House on Thursday stepped into the fragmented market for disposable virus-filtering N95 masks, moving to connect medical supply companies with mask manufacturers who say they are loaded with inventory but can’t find buyers — even in the midst of a pandemic in which doctors and nurses are desperate for the protective gear.</rdfs:comment>
