	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d8844d0f-4415-44af-9822-ca8391d63938">
		<rdfs:label>article-d8844d0f-4415-44af-9822-ca8391d63938</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Getting a vaccination remains the best line of defense against Covid-19, the nation’s top two health leaders said on Sunday.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8cddda8e-bf27-443d-ab88-1512a3ebc5de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d88964cc-ba31-475c-b624-96b5319801c1">
		<rdfs:label>article-d88964cc-ba31-475c-b624-96b5319801c1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The warning followed reports that apartment building owners were seeking to evict tens of thousands of renters despite a federal halt on evictions during the pandemic.</rdfs:comment>
