		<rdfs:label>article-d972b791-5dbb-4ea9-b1e0-065625a13f18</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Just days before the Biden administration’s first face-to-face encounter with Beijing, two senior American envoys used a visit to Tokyo on Tuesday to set a confrontational tone for the talks, rebuking what they called “coercion” and “destabilizing actions” by China in its increasingly aggressive military forays in the region.</rdfs:comment>
