	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-d98e174e-0bef-4075-96f9-1063ab138cf0">
		<rdfs:label>article-d98e174e-0bef-4075-96f9-1063ab138cf0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Federal district courts have tended to rule for Democrats in litigation over how to run the election, but appeals courts, well stocked with the president’s nominees, are blocking them.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-864756c8-4d62-42e5-a6e4-482550bf62a9"/>
