		<rdfs:comment>The former president is trying to reshape the battleground state in his image. But his false claims about the 2020 election are driving a wedge between loyalists and those who are eager to move on.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6fcc2118-4d59-415b-8f82-fd519f6b2d34"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-93d154d3-6d3d-4599-ac55-e63a146d8d6f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db7a2d25-b735-4364-9c3e-a1f8dd3a7151">
		<rdfs:label>article-db7a2d25-b735-4364-9c3e-a1f8dd3a7151</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A suspect was located, the authorities said. Last year, a police shooting in Kenosha was followed by protests and the killings of two demonstrators.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0137c8d2-ca42-438d-b365-ccce9f61d31b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6bf4af99-38f0-4df7-94f4-82a6657aa590"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db7d4dc8-71fd-4c4a-bddf-91f2afb52691">
		<rdfs:label>article-db7d4dc8-71fd-4c4a-bddf-91f2afb52691</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The initial police account of the death of a Minneapolis man did not mention that an officer’s knee pinned him to the ground. “Please, I can’t breathe,” he said.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ea9dbbc7-267d-46dd-9bad-620f876af0ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db7e8a4e-bed5-4046-968e-f54107f51168">
		<rdfs:label>article-db7e8a4e-bed5-4046-968e-f54107f51168</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Pulling Ukrainians out of battle to train them could accelerate Russia’s gains, officials say. The Pentagon is also monitoring the levels of its own stockpiles.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5a3094b1-6bc7-47d7-8f53-c56fd8ed0c59"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6f60db0f-4977-4567-b7bd-9abe5d4a35e8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db805b1e-39d1-4e40-9da4-b6d7660b171b">
		<rdfs:label>article-db805b1e-39d1-4e40-9da4-b6d7660b171b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As the Uvalde, Texas, massacre raises questions about the police response, experts describe complex, shifting circumstances. Speed, they say, is essential.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-becd702f-c674-4653-9a6c-90ee51977e85"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ccf12c09-bb92-47bc-afe9-b31ea5914e31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e2a444d6-76b3-4fc5-9655-0178ae16f402"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db809b8d-ba53-4b52-a601-5a50d5637ac9">
		<rdfs:label>article-db809b8d-ba53-4b52-a601-5a50d5637ac9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The lack of race results in New York and Kentucky this week is a prelude for the presidential election, as officials strain to deal with a deluge of absentee ballots and a jumble of voting deadlines.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db80ff15-7881-4f8b-bb06-5865b309ee61">
		<rdfs:label>article-db80ff15-7881-4f8b-bb06-5865b309ee61</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The move clears the way for greater security cooperation and investment at a time when President Biden is seeking help boosting natural gas supplies in Europe.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db854785-a3e8-496f-b867-05d2170c94ca">
		<rdfs:label>article-db854785-a3e8-496f-b867-05d2170c94ca</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Declassified portions of a report presented to President Biden revealed divisions among federal agencies over whether the virus came from a lab leak or emerged more naturally.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6f60db0f-4977-4567-b7bd-9abe5d4a35e8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db875335-cb1b-47ae-a2a2-a68f1d0d2faf">
		<rdfs:label>article-db875335-cb1b-47ae-a2a2-a68f1d0d2faf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Texas law limits punitive damages to far below what a jury awarded in a lawsuit brought by the parents of a Sandy Hook victim, but the judge called it “a rare case.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5f60b7f2-92f5-4980-9c8e-e8bf01cdb98f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db8871f3-953d-4fde-9ad2-fa034a383455">
		<rdfs:label>article-db8871f3-953d-4fde-9ad2-fa034a383455</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mr. Feenstra, a state senator who defeated Mr. King in the primary, shares many of the incumbent’s policy views but not his history of incendiary and racist remarks.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db8897c0-9c0f-4953-9c9d-1118a6847157">
		<rdfs:label>article-db8897c0-9c0f-4953-9c9d-1118a6847157</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>For all the drama around the presidential race, the biggest surprise of the 2020 election may have been in the House, as Republicans gained eight seats and cut into the Democratic majority after a campaign in which officials in both parties expected the G.O.P. to come up short.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db8c7d99-e640-43f7-ac8a-213cff25b27d">
		<rdfs:label>article-db8c7d99-e640-43f7-ac8a-213cff25b27d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Despite their disparate backgrounds, the Illinois Democrat has carved out a public life most evocative of the man she could join on the presidential ticket.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f33dc887-a9a6-4b4f-adce-fc81b6f27a0c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db8f33e6-64e5-4a2d-a008-45891185da3f">
		<rdfs:label>article-db8f33e6-64e5-4a2d-a008-45891185da3f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Also this week, learning to live with smoke. And, climate experts talk about the future.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-34b65400-07ab-404a-9fe3-c1a27b1be114"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b1afb246-66b2-4eea-8ebc-1b5c7f6c7900"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d8148593-227b-4889-ae70-592b440737ae"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db91e418-d975-45f6-95af-385adff84679">
		<rdfs:label>article-db91e418-d975-45f6-95af-385adff84679</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The lack of power and safe water for millions of people in Texas may be compounded on Thursday by a band of foul weather stretching from the Rio Grande to New York.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-2bfc1d86-f654-490c-ae5c-efaa41acbbe5"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db930bee-5fbb-47fb-a4e6-7b49c17a0585">
		<rdfs:label>article-db930bee-5fbb-47fb-a4e6-7b49c17a0585</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After the recent absentee ballot debacle, anyone who is able ought to take advantage of early in-person voting.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db951398-bd5f-4e85-88b2-dd694a0e3113">
		<rdfs:label>article-db951398-bd5f-4e85-88b2-dd694a0e3113</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Louisiana and other Republican-led states challenged a federal working group’s efforts to develop standards for agencies to use in quantifying the harms caused by emissions.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-947ed571-ad87-49fb-b59a-9372d166d3c7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db9abcca-3d33-40ef-b44f-b9be0b6f7e90">
		<rdfs:label>article-db9abcca-3d33-40ef-b44f-b9be0b6f7e90</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The decision will keep more water in Lake Powell on the Arizona-Utah border, instead of releasing it downstream to Lake Mead. Both reservoirs are at their lowest points.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e17310c8-39f3-4c91-8224-a91b0b94e409"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db9b5c83-9579-4f16-86a2-82b8d3217227">
		<rdfs:label>article-db9b5c83-9579-4f16-86a2-82b8d3217227</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president-elect has long tried to keep from being sucked into President Trump’s dramas. He may find that posture hard to maintain when he takes office and the Senate puts Mr. Trump on trial.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db9c39d7-0357-4fc0-a356-be2a6e7ef115">
		<rdfs:label>article-db9c39d7-0357-4fc0-a356-be2a6e7ef115</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Voting has appeared to unfold without any major problems in Georgia on Tuesday. Democrats may have claimed a bigger share of the early vote than they did in November’s election, election data shows.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db9c7ea2-7d75-4b77-b6c9-b02eb15c96f2">
		<rdfs:label>article-db9c7ea2-7d75-4b77-b6c9-b02eb15c96f2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>WASHINGTON — The nation’s coronavirus testing capacity, already straining to keep up with demand, is facing enormous new pressure, with holiday travelers waiting in long lines to be tested, overworked laboratories struggling to keep up and rapid at-home diagnostics flying off pharmacy shelves as the Omicron variant fuels a rapid spike in Covid-19 cases.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3263b980-a580-440f-bdd2-6d7fa7bb3fab"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-12-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db9d1b3a-52d4-42eb-b3b4-8ff6cb1542e2">
		<rdfs:label>article-db9d1b3a-52d4-42eb-b3b4-8ff6cb1542e2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The meeting was a big foreign policy test for President Biden, with consequences for the stability of Europe, the credibility of American threats and the future of Ukraine.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc2c2b47-32c2-43a0-8e5f-dd4e72335932"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-12-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db9de6a8-af99-43e0-b28e-4a9aa2a93072">
		<rdfs:label>article-db9de6a8-af99-43e0-b28e-4a9aa2a93072</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Some veterans have started businesses that draw from their experiences in Iraq and Afghanistan, and thrived.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-20ac5364-1758-414f-ab86-a88673954008"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-db9e7038-f4ce-4b21-9f97-0d2ff4ba9bbf">
		<rdfs:label>article-db9e7038-f4ce-4b21-9f97-0d2ff4ba9bbf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Lawmakers are coalescing around a deal to suspend a $10,000 cap on state and local tax deductions that was imposed during the Trump administration.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4b06f805-a6f6-4cda-9908-3f8ddd3a0432"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dba0499c-f39f-48de-a53c-22d173eb3713">
		<rdfs:label>article-dba0499c-f39f-48de-a53c-22d173eb3713</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Monday: Social distancing and other restrictions that have defined life in the pandemic will disappear on June 15, state health officials said.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-781f7c76-864b-4901-8b16-90c83d96e113"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dba49f29-f845-498a-975c-f6be0da33d2a">
		<rdfs:label>article-dba49f29-f845-498a-975c-f6be0da33d2a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Senator Raphael Warnock will face Herschel Walker, the Republican nominee, in a general election race with enormous stakes for the Senate.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-803bdb8f-8c3c-4210-80c9-22b0af3fd2ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbaa26eb-ad2b-4c8a-8017-d2eacbf86904">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbaa26eb-ad2b-4c8a-8017-d2eacbf86904</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In an abrupt reversal, Gov. Greg Abbott directed Texans in all counties with 20 or more coronavirus cases to wear face masks in public places. He also authorized limits on public gatherings.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-843f7a86-cb21-42c6-b668-9e9388bb54e5"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fd2d6ec4-4aa3-452f-8e17-99a953af7b67"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbaaf6c1-e8f4-40c7-afdf-ab3a8b7b02f5">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbaaf6c1-e8f4-40c7-afdf-ab3a8b7b02f5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Michigan State Capitol Commission voted unanimously on Monday to ban the open carry of weapons in the state Capitol in Lansing. But gun owners with a concealed-weapons permit will still be able to carry concealed guns into the Capitol, and there will be restrictions on carrying guns on the Capitol grounds.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-44926325-5c4f-4e18-89e5-b1470d62842c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbaf7ec9-e98f-4764-b4ce-90625ed7b80a">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbaf7ec9-e98f-4764-b4ce-90625ed7b80a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The former president’s instincts for red-meat political fights over governing and policymaking have left party leaders in a state of confusion over what they stand for.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbb0b2f1-874e-4177-b353-a6f29bb9fff8">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbb0b2f1-874e-4177-b353-a6f29bb9fff8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Amid a pandemic that has highlighted the importance of medical care even as millions of Americans who lost their jobs also lost their insurance, some of the most emotionally resonant moments of the second night of the Democratic convention came in discussions of health care.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e008be05-6dcb-45fe-a5d2-1657eb3a638f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbb295d4-4bb7-4438-9a99-25ca63991583">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbb295d4-4bb7-4438-9a99-25ca63991583</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>If you need to take advantage of same-day registration, do it in person. Here’s what else to know.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4d1965e-83d5-427c-92cb-8140b08c5176"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbb9a816-38bb-4152-b700-0f10c39ba45f">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbb9a816-38bb-4152-b700-0f10c39ba45f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Momentum is shifting toward a clean-car future as more automakers end their legal efforts to block California’s tough fuel economy standards.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c55cfad1-37a4-40de-ab47-b363a537db6a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbba8822-1424-488e-b945-38ab481059d2">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbba8822-1424-488e-b945-38ab481059d2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Representative Tom O’Halleran of Arizona is seeking re-election as his district leans further toward Trump. His strategy? Don’t change. “I am,” he says, “who I am.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-89135d87-ed63-4619-a5ce-c3f23d9e6fd4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbbbb480-61d3-41b2-80af-06fe08222982">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbbbb480-61d3-41b2-80af-06fe08222982</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>It’s time for Americans to buckle down for a long struggle with Beijing, the Florida senator will argue in a speech.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e9c4025-7dbe-4808-a3d4-b9d25fa14354"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-89135d87-ed63-4619-a5ce-c3f23d9e6fd4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbbc37bf-1cc1-470a-927b-0283f3a2bf64">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbbc37bf-1cc1-470a-927b-0283f3a2bf64</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Now that Mr. Trump is finally out of office, President Biden has the chance to lead America forward.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fda4452b-3825-4a26-bbb4-46f458379b68"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbbc5ddf-f2b3-40a7-bccb-e7459b573af3">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbbc5ddf-f2b3-40a7-bccb-e7459b573af3</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A legal battle in Oklahoma over whether prisoners feel severe pain after being given the sedative, midazolam, will determine whether its use is constitutional.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e993acb7-fd71-489b-b569-b6b6d449dfe5"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbbf95cd-2566-453d-ad5b-47bf33235a56">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbbf95cd-2566-453d-ad5b-47bf33235a56</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>New York City may overhaul its elementary admissions to the selective track.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f054aa66-2374-4f42-8ea3-5d2fd3c51e19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbc11300-f6f8-4784-8a40-b501dd7614c4">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbc11300-f6f8-4784-8a40-b501dd7614c4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A new report sent to Congress about the drone strike that killed Iran’s top general contradicted the original justification the administration provided.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbc9101a-deaf-4b08-a082-62787e894fbb">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbc9101a-deaf-4b08-a082-62787e894fbb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden, faced with a decision about how to punish Saudi Arabia for its role in the assassination of a dissident journalist, gathered top national security officials in the Oval Office and pushed them at length about their recommended response. Then he sided with a majority of advisers who argued against the most severe action — a direct sanction of Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman, who American intelligence agencies say approved the killing.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbd137eb-e7c1-40ec-b0d9-2c91deb87517">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbd137eb-e7c1-40ec-b0d9-2c91deb87517</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The House committee investigating the Capitol riot called for documents and testimony from Rudolph W. Giuliani and other members of President Donald J. Trump’s legal team.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbd3b734-97ad-49c9-a145-20278bbc1217">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbd3b734-97ad-49c9-a145-20278bbc1217</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The plan to reverse the outcome of the 2020 election by creating slates of electors pledged to Donald Trump in states he had lost was expansive, long-running and often confusing.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-90788841-2a13-4598-abd3-3b677caff4d4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd522e1c-57a0-49bc-9835-fae39d9d58a6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbd53f61-1069-44d9-8d8f-a67a6d17e88c">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbd53f61-1069-44d9-8d8f-a67a6d17e88c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Bob Good, a self-described “biblical conservative” who is the Republican nominee for a House seat in his conservative Central Virginia district, is hoping to rally clergy members with meetings this week attacking a new state law prohibiting discrimination based on sexual orientation and gender identity, which he characterizes as an assault on religious liberty.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-21d856ad-a6ae-406e-a9e4-9707218ad815"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbd6fec1-e33c-4a90-835c-45cc660bb8f8">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbd6fec1-e33c-4a90-835c-45cc660bb8f8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A chief goal of the meetings this week is to show that Russia’s invasion of Ukraine will not lead to sniping and disagreement among the United States and its allies.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbd94cc4-708e-4384-b17d-a9adf2383159">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbd94cc4-708e-4384-b17d-a9adf2383159</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president named Moncef Slaoui, a former pharmaceutical executive, to lead a crash development program that if successful would shatter speed records for vaccine development.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e4ac7a5-be1a-4937-b91e-66276e5f8dd9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbd9ce2c-9474-43d3-8e99-4e2b68080326">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbd9ce2c-9474-43d3-8e99-4e2b68080326</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mitt Romney, Larry Hogan and Liz Cheney — descendants of sometimes rebellious or resolute Republicans of the past — are dissenting voices on a president who has taken over their party.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dcd0eb75-780a-43fe-aa5a-ac14ace05e96"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbdb3872-1832-4262-84c0-7eba2c6f09a4">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbdb3872-1832-4262-84c0-7eba2c6f09a4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Sometimes, they get emotional.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd146215-8c12-40b0-bfb7-0d9c07c5e63d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbdb512a-69fa-4d2f-8caf-f920a50753f5">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbdb512a-69fa-4d2f-8caf-f920a50753f5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The House voted on Monday evening to increase the size of individual stimulus checks to $2,000 from $600, endorsing a measure demanded by President Trump and daring Senate Republicans to either approve the heftier sum or defy the president, whose demands for bigger checks nearly scuttled the entire stimulus package.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbdca3b5-5220-4500-94e3-bb542cf41663">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbdca3b5-5220-4500-94e3-bb542cf41663</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Speaker Nancy Pelosi and Senator Mitch McConnell, the majority leader, spoke on Thursday as Joe Biden’s victory and vaccine breakthroughs added momentum to a push for a stimulus deal.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6c995819-c171-430e-a414-f6167b134557"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbdd7c07-3f7d-4912-941d-054ad893fe4c">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbdd7c07-3f7d-4912-941d-054ad893fe4c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Lawmakers are also considering a proposal to require parents to tell schools if they have firearms in the home.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-1e5cee4f-82a8-44a6-9cc0-9285f4da7bf4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbddbe37-7ea6-4b8b-b6c5-8b6c2b41bc1d">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbddbe37-7ea6-4b8b-b6c5-8b6c2b41bc1d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Barring police and corrections officers from participating in Pride events shows a lack of farsightedness at a critical moment for L.G.B.T.Q. rights and support.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbec80cf-0d80-4049-969d-475c8ad5f80d">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbec80cf-0d80-4049-969d-475c8ad5f80d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Prosecutors said they were wrong by a minute when they described, in court papers, how long a police officer pinned Mr. Floyd to the ground. Videos show it was at least eight minutes and 15 seconds.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e993acb7-fd71-489b-b569-b6b6d449dfe5"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbf0365c-68f5-4098-84e9-1efad63fcc44">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbf0365c-68f5-4098-84e9-1efad63fcc44</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The main House war chests for both Democrats and Republicans have a combined $128 million in the bank — more than double the sum at this point in 2020.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-10-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbf172d3-fe27-40ab-b004-41f7a715411d">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbf172d3-fe27-40ab-b004-41f7a715411d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Union officials at FEMA say they would like to know where they work in order to warn other employees who might  be exposed and to avoid putting the public at added risk.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-74659e03-2c48-4140-91f4-08e5d544f77a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbf3f254-6cc1-42d9-bc61-ba2e2c9b702b">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbf3f254-6cc1-42d9-bc61-ba2e2c9b702b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The president could have used the speech to talk about joining ranks with allies to counter both the virus and the economic impact. He could have talked about sharing public health data and lessons learned from China’s experience. He did not.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbf8120d-f074-455a-a2a9-79e3f49edad7">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbf8120d-f074-455a-a2a9-79e3f49edad7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats enter the final sprint to November more optimistic than expected, especially in the race for the Senate. But Republicans remain bullish that they can sweep into a House majority.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-803bdb8f-8c3c-4210-80c9-22b0af3fd2ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbf90e09-7dc7-410e-97c2-3e6cfa517031">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbf90e09-7dc7-410e-97c2-3e6cfa517031</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Joe Biden wins Pennsylvania’s 20 electoral votes, giving him enough for the presidency.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-42dfcd52-8183-4ae1-ba08-c61dc31db2c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8eb0923f-854c-4241-9d79-040d1aeeb0c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-93d154d3-6d3d-4599-ac55-e63a146d8d6f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dbfc1ce4-0cd4-42a5-8041-956746f0fd5d">
		<rdfs:label>article-dbfc1ce4-0cd4-42a5-8041-956746f0fd5d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The temperatures this weekend weren’t just hot, they were record-breaking, including in Death Valley.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-078e57d0-5b20-48e9-b039-c2569b2acb05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dc0dd442-20f6-48d4-8eca-f0c9fd92e138">
		<rdfs:label>article-dc0dd442-20f6-48d4-8eca-f0c9fd92e138</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Officials said that the drought is also contributing to to the crisis.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-078e57d0-5b20-48e9-b039-c2569b2acb05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dc0dd549-31cf-433d-97cd-ec28de2f082f">
		<rdfs:label>article-dc0dd549-31cf-433d-97cd-ec28de2f082f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden said there was “no need” for former President Donald J. Trump to get the briefings, traditionally given to ex-presidents as a courtesy and to keep them informed if their advice is needed.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dc0e0823-dd66-420c-9fa1-f8fc00ef8dbf">
		<rdfs:label>article-dc0e0823-dd66-420c-9fa1-f8fc00ef8dbf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Magic City Acceptance Academy, a public charter school, finally opened last year after several attempts. Students there have watched state legislators debate their future in real time.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-60369502-b152-49d7-982e-93f0386300f3"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dc0e177a-1aac-4f93-b6f7-5047a8934b63">
		<rdfs:label>article-dc0e177a-1aac-4f93-b6f7-5047a8934b63</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden has been outspoken about George Floyd’s death, and on Tuesday he called it “murder in full light of day.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd42dd7e-7a0d-4a74-908e-252de023edfb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-dc0f9c83-e1d0-444f-826a-0f5a313d1d43">
		<rdfs:label>article-dc0f9c83-e1d0-444f-826a-0f5a313d1d43</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Republicans have offered multiple rationales for why witnesses are unnecessary, but Democrats have counterarguments for all of them.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0e84c75e-7bc1-4744-83f1-7496fcf4721d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-31"/>
