		<rdfs:label>article-dc400590-765c-419c-a678-7039f42c82d9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats and White House officials neared a deal on Friday on a stopgap spending bill to keep the government funded through Dec. 11, according to two people familiar with the plans, but the agreement remained unfinished amid a last-minute dispute over funding for farmers demanded by President Trump.</rdfs:comment>
