		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-df253524-e061-44f8-8259-1b5594b3fffe">
		<rdfs:label>article-df253524-e061-44f8-8259-1b5594b3fffe</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Trump administration is pressing forward with policies limiting transgender rights. Many rules that have been in development for years have now either been finalized or have gone into effect.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e0dfbf0e-c179-4f28-a968-4570f9209555"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-df279702-942d-4e38-bb0a-d9fcc8ec8e48">
		<rdfs:label>article-df279702-942d-4e38-bb0a-d9fcc8ec8e48</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Judge Peter A. Cahill will hear the case of the four police officers charged in the killing of George Floyd, according to court documents filed on Friday. The first hearing is set for June 29.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
