		<rdfs:label>article-df367376-2795-4c39-9f6b-f942c67c9e80</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Executives with companies including Target, Apple, Google and Facebook warned the president that any actions related to DACA would disrupt the economy and affect the battle against the coronavirus.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-df3eeac5-e486-4fa2-9fe6-7dda6f922275">
		<rdfs:label>article-df3eeac5-e486-4fa2-9fe6-7dda6f922275</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Diplomatic sweeteners for joining the Abraham Accords that were offered to Morocco, Sudan and the United Arab Emirates could be rejected by Congress or reversed by the incoming Biden administration.</rdfs:comment>
