	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e00d22d8-3f53-4187-be92-025c996afb4f">
		<rdfs:label>article-e00d22d8-3f53-4187-be92-025c996afb4f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Even when presented with a printout of the president’s incendiary Twitter comment, Republicans toiled to avoid commenting.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e00d2f7a-32d0-44d8-9555-2ff2dbcbf341">
		<rdfs:label>article-e00d2f7a-32d0-44d8-9555-2ff2dbcbf341</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>“People don’t understand how fragile we are,” said one resident of an island off Maine that will turn away visitors. Communities in North Carolina’s Outer Banks will do the same.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-17d88f11-8c44-408d-8ac2-945b979b26ce"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e2ba983e-eb48-483d-afa1-e67b02e88f99"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e011573d-8cb9-4dfd-855b-14dc977686f8">
		<rdfs:label>article-e011573d-8cb9-4dfd-855b-14dc977686f8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Donald Trump Jr. said virus deaths have fallen to “almost nothing” on a day when over 1,000 died in the U.S.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7479f929-0522-4f1f-a391-dcdb5f4e726c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e0156bea-b744-4b16-b272-8f7e79eee71f">
		<rdfs:label>article-e0156bea-b744-4b16-b272-8f7e79eee71f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The demise of Roe v. Wade would make the need for effective birth control more urgent than ever. Yet many American women still have a hard time obtaining it.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e0169308-adec-419b-b683-649e362d1cbe">
		<rdfs:label>article-e0169308-adec-419b-b683-649e362d1cbe</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Also this week, the United States exits the Paris climate agreement</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b1afb246-66b2-4eea-8ebc-1b5c7f6c7900"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e17310c8-39f3-4c91-8224-a91b0b94e409"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e0173f88-71da-455d-a138-4ed7d4f778bc">
		<rdfs:label>article-e0173f88-71da-455d-a138-4ed7d4f778bc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The argument was Justice Stephen G. Breyer’s last, and Chief Justice John G. Roberts Jr. ended it with a fond tribute to his colleague.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-947ed571-ad87-49fb-b59a-9372d166d3c7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-04-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e0181b38-83ee-4f7f-92c9-c89ae7421442">
		<rdfs:label>article-e0181b38-83ee-4f7f-92c9-c89ae7421442</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The group has long been a highly influential voice on politics in their communities and played a key role in mobilizing Black voters.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a0f415ea-f8d1-4b12-b0c0-6cb1a91c315d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e01a0be9-e1a5-4c16-bbbe-3067eb77cf69">
		<rdfs:label>article-e01a0be9-e1a5-4c16-bbbe-3067eb77cf69</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Pentagon is moving up to eight F-35 fighter jets and a slew of other warplanes to Eastern Europe, the Baltics and Poland to shore up support for NATO allies following what President Biden called the beginning of Russia’s invasion of Ukraine.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-46b2f3e2-fc43-4d1f-8134-a17365f8ec33"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e01a5bb2-fabe-43d9-9d55-e96650737600">
		<rdfs:label>article-e01a5bb2-fabe-43d9-9d55-e96650737600</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Georgia Democrat, a child of Methodist preachers, once identified as an abortion foe. Now, she is putting her defense of abortion rights — and the story of her conversion — at the center of her campaign for governor.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a0f415ea-f8d1-4b12-b0c0-6cb1a91c315d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e01cf4e8-9a09-48ce-8d21-eac22979c4f1">
		<rdfs:label>article-e01cf4e8-9a09-48ce-8d21-eac22979c4f1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Coronavirus patients are swamping U.S. hospitals in record numbers, straining the health care system much more widely than the first acute outbreaks did in the spring.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-073a2c11-e123-4e83-900b-90a962ee7e54"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e01d1cb9-194d-40a4-bda2-5fc10e273210">
		<rdfs:label>article-e01d1cb9-194d-40a4-bda2-5fc10e273210</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden had also been in close contact with a staff member who later tested positive.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-12-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e01deee2-5760-4047-9697-7b0662b8b236">
		<rdfs:label>article-e01deee2-5760-4047-9697-7b0662b8b236</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As the nation awaits results in what has turned out to be a historic election in a historic year, we look back to the elections after the Voting Rights Act.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e02035f2-8712-41a1-bcf8-bcb36556345f">
		<rdfs:label>article-e02035f2-8712-41a1-bcf8-bcb36556345f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Empowering Medicare to negotiate prices directly with drug makers has been a Democratic goal for 30 years, one the pharmaceutical industry has fought ferociously.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7cf59892-95ab-4467-bd6d-b2944623f5eb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e0257faa-060b-4471-8321-3b97d513d6ca">
		<rdfs:label>article-e0257faa-060b-4471-8321-3b97d513d6ca</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As coronavirus infection rates decline, fewer are getting tested for the virus. The Biden administration wants to reverse that to ensure that schools and workplaces can reopen safely.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9f6de486-2c48-474d-84c4-ae7a2ad3d34b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e028c67e-882f-44f1-b6ca-d20f1f0c2cfe">
		<rdfs:label>article-e028c67e-882f-44f1-b6ca-d20f1f0c2cfe</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Mr. Quested began spending time with the Proud Boys after the election as part of a project meant to explore the increasing polarization and extremism in American politics.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-90788841-2a13-4598-abd3-3b677caff4d4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e02a5090-08bb-420f-9d6b-d98f7f9a7bb5">
		<rdfs:label>article-e02a5090-08bb-420f-9d6b-d98f7f9a7bb5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Making the digital artworks requires colossal amounts of computing power, and that means greenhouse gases.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e02c142f-2fff-40dc-8129-84e258b48e3c">
		<rdfs:label>article-e02c142f-2fff-40dc-8129-84e258b48e3c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>An inner perimeter will be moved closer to the building and an outer perimeter will be removed altogether as Congress tries to return to normal after the Jan. 6 attack.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e02df70e-6165-427e-ae87-00f7b8be871d">
		<rdfs:label>article-e02df70e-6165-427e-ae87-00f7b8be871d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The former president filed suit against the House committee investigating the attack on the Capitol, seeking to block the panel’s subpoena that required him to testify and hand over documents.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e0316167-6427-48d6-ba69-29cedff13d03">
		<rdfs:label>article-e0316167-6427-48d6-ba69-29cedff13d03</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Secretary of State Mike Pompeo said the U.S. wants multilateralism “to actually work.” Then he issued a series of unilateral sanctions and other punishments against Trump administration adversaries.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f4f38f08-6492-4112-8b82-52bd8aa6b34f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e0320fe7-2c92-4f57-bb32-e52b80ac8753">
		<rdfs:label>article-e0320fe7-2c92-4f57-bb32-e52b80ac8753</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>It is almost certainly a substantial undercount, since many infected people have no symptoms or mistake them for those of another illness, and not everyone gets tested.</rdfs:comment>
