	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e4c4ac27-563d-4077-ae4c-5ec2cc0473cd">
		<rdfs:label>article-e4c4ac27-563d-4077-ae4c-5ec2cc0473cd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As long as Congress has met, votes have been cast only in person. A growing group of lawmakers are pushing to change that in the age of coronavirus.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e4c57b3b-b9d9-4ec0-b4a4-ffb3470cb574">
		<rdfs:label>article-e4c57b3b-b9d9-4ec0-b4a4-ffb3470cb574</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democratic support has plunged nationally in recent months. Exactly how far it has fallen is hotly debated in both parties.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e4c76bf5-30c1-4b11-8dcd-0f646a11a2a9">
