		<rdfs:label>article-e5657dbe-506e-48e5-a77d-35ba840482d5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Internal Revenue Service failed to audit former President Donald J. Trump’s tax filings for his first two years in office despite having a policy that makes the auditing of sitting presidents mandatory, a House committee revealed on Tuesday after an extraordinary vote to make public six years of his tax returns.</rdfs:comment>
