	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e7914adf-8edc-428c-897d-43d77af75aa8">
		<rdfs:label>article-e7914adf-8edc-428c-897d-43d77af75aa8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>NORTH PORT, Fla. — With its blue paint and red trim, Bill Ealahan Jr.’s mobile home used to stick out among the hundreds of beige homes in the trailer park.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e993acb7-fd71-489b-b569-b6b6d449dfe5"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e791d977-0f48-44fd-8096-7c09af561344">
		<rdfs:label>article-e791d977-0f48-44fd-8096-7c09af561344</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The former White House chief of staff told the House panel scrutinizing the Capitol attack that he was no longer willing to be deposed, reversing a commitment he made last week.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-12-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e79988de-53b7-4bdc-b123-e6292ee3a3a4">
		<rdfs:label>article-e79988de-53b7-4bdc-b123-e6292ee3a3a4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Speaker Nancy Pelosi flashed fresh optimism on Friday that the House and Senate could soon reach a bipartisan deal on an elusive pandemic stimulus plan after she and Senator Mitch McConnell, the Senate majority leader, agreed to try to find an agreement that could be merged with an enormous year-end spending package.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e79beae3-49ca-46ec-a706-577c0b963ed5">
		<rdfs:label>article-e79beae3-49ca-46ec-a706-577c0b963ed5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>For most of the past decade, North Carolina was a showcase for the Republican Party’s growth — its strength in the suburbs, in rural areas and in races up and down the ballot proving that it could dominate in parts of the country where demographics favored the Democrats. Now it could be a victim of its own excess.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ef6cc7eb-b6e8-4dba-84e0-6b42579e91d0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e7a2d37d-b889-4967-99b3-043c793f0d68">
		<rdfs:label>article-e7a2d37d-b889-4967-99b3-043c793f0d68</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>An influential system overseen by retailers and clothing makers ranks petroleum-based synthetics like “vegan leather” as more environmentally sound than natural fibers.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c4d98394-1549-4853-be0d-e7afcd8ee238"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-06-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e7a39c01-6372-4743-a63b-a58218a744c2">
		<rdfs:label>article-e7a39c01-6372-4743-a63b-a58218a744c2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The commission will also examine other potential changes such as term limits for justices. Progressives are pushing President Biden to add seats to balance the court’s conservative majority.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e7a4e3ab-75ec-493a-a777-2e8f33b0f034">
		<rdfs:label>article-e7a4e3ab-75ec-493a-a777-2e8f33b0f034</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>At the urging of New York’s attorney general, business leaders in New York pushed for the Trump administration to begin a transfer of power.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ac748b00-7205-45e9-ba20-53ddfa903a7f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-cf1ff93a-790a-4d11-b971-0922d35faa16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e7a63fed-8b05-4d0b-a1ca-ab1e76110f0f">
		<rdfs:label>article-e7a63fed-8b05-4d0b-a1ca-ab1e76110f0f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The fractious race to replace the outgoing Lamar Alexander signified an end to the moderate tenor that has long defined Tennessee Republicanism.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-1a919c05-175d-4b8d-9183-278fc0c9195c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e7a6ca20-2da4-4b6a-8c72-485464097d1b">
		<rdfs:label>article-e7a6ca20-2da4-4b6a-8c72-485464097d1b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Three criminal statutes show the inquiry goes beyond classified information — and that the former president is also suspected of obstructing an unidentified government effort.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-13"/>
