		<rdfs:label>article-e81c0b22-7e49-4167-b94d-4b2b625c42f1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump on Tuesday night fired his administration’s most senior cybersecurity official responsible for securing the presidential election, Christopher Krebs, who had systematically disputed Mr. Trump’s false declarations that the presidency was stolen from him through fraudulent ballots and software glitches that changed millions of votes.</rdfs:comment>
