	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e858dfc8-c64d-41ce-817d-a8072ec29e4d">
		<rdfs:label>article-e858dfc8-c64d-41ce-817d-a8072ec29e4d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Candidates in Virginia, Ohio, New York City and Boston celebrate their victories in Tuesday’s elections.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e8592b18-0893-4c5c-a88d-0604a40486e7">
		<rdfs:label>article-e8592b18-0893-4c5c-a88d-0604a40486e7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The former mayor of Braddock, Pa., is positioning himself as the rarest of figures in 21st American politics — a populist Democrat hoping to unite the party’s left wing with former Trump supporters.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7479f929-0522-4f1f-a391-dcdb5f4e726c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e85935ed-fa20-4d4e-9171-2289d8cbe59a">
		<rdfs:label>article-e85935ed-fa20-4d4e-9171-2289d8cbe59a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In what could be interpreted as an attempt to stoke the flames of a Capitol mob which has begun to disperse, President Trump sent a tweet at around 6 p.m. in which he reiterated the false claim that the election was stolen and encouraged his supporters to “remember this day” going forward.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e85f359f-fd1d-47dc-9174-16e93c1a9af6">
		<rdfs:label>article-e85f359f-fd1d-47dc-9174-16e93c1a9af6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>From lobsters in Maine to ethanol in Iowa to the oil fields of Texas, the president has tried to bolster his case for re-election by promoting localized — and factually challenged — accomplishments.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-be4afe5b-5317-4441-a7de-57071d96016d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e860f93f-875f-47e7-a326-f99295f3e1b5">
		<rdfs:label>article-e860f93f-875f-47e7-a326-f99295f3e1b5</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>There is bipartisan support for this popular, common-sense reform.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e8636237-0e66-4ab2-8e05-0c9082c74722">
		<rdfs:label>article-e8636237-0e66-4ab2-8e05-0c9082c74722</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>A House panel found that the companies have thrived in the past decade by selling and marketing military-grade weapons to civilians, specifically young men.</rdfs:comment>
