		<rdfs:comment>Oregon has an addiction problem. Pockets of rural poverty, chronic homelessness and cities with lots of young people have given the state one of the highest rates of substance abuse in the nation. Because there is so little money allocated to it, it is also one of the toughest places to get treatment.</rdfs:comment>
