		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e9a13025-19ae-49aa-98a7-b7410e106abd">
		<rdfs:label>article-e9a13025-19ae-49aa-98a7-b7410e106abd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Comedy Central raunch-fest didn’t seem like it would be politically relevant two decades later. But that was long before Joe Rogan interviewed presidential candidates and Pete Buttigieg filled in for Jimmy Kimmel.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-05cab340-1083-4afb-b3ad-2204d98f02b4"/>
