	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e9a1d0cd-82bb-466e-bff3-68c0275761c7">
		<rdfs:label>article-e9a1d0cd-82bb-466e-bff3-68c0275761c7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>This Juneteenth, we ask the critical questions: What does it mean to not just survive but to thrive? How can love make us stronger?</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e9a265b2-9871-401b-ae56-f1986a450278">
		<rdfs:label>article-e9a265b2-9871-401b-ae56-f1986a450278</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Bureau of Elections moved to exclude James Craig and Perry Johnson from the primary ballot, finding that they had failed to collect the required signatures.</rdfs:comment>
