	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e9c633ee-b359-4b28-af88-ff82af3f6934">
		<rdfs:label>article-e9c633ee-b359-4b28-af88-ff82af3f6934</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Thomas Lane, J. Alexander Kueng and Tou Thao were charged with aiding and abetting second-degree murder and aiding and abetting second-degree manslaughter and are expected to be tried jointly beginning in August.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-edd059c5-3ec4-4bec-b45e-ca6834a9e51c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-e9ca373d-a735-4e02-bb05-fc86b44a401d">
		<rdfs:label>article-e9ca373d-a735-4e02-bb05-fc86b44a401d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump’s health news brought on, for many, the kind of psychic doom-spiraling that has felt endemic to the era.</rdfs:comment>
