	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb761ce0-290b-4d3d-a837-165661b6798a">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb761ce0-290b-4d3d-a837-165661b6798a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>By the end of Monday, thousands of yellow envelopes mailed to a squat brick building in Birmingham, Ala., will hold the fate of one of the most closely watched union elections in recent history, one that could alter the shape of the labor movement.</rdfs:comment>
