		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb774792-16a3-48e7-a568-99ab2449dcda">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb774792-16a3-48e7-a568-99ab2449dcda</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The conventional wisdom, from a political perspective, is that President Trump’s diagnosis will hurt his re-election chances. But there’s so much we don’t know.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb7cf047-c27e-4448-9ea2-4a7594daab78">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb7cf047-c27e-4448-9ea2-4a7594daab78</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump sought to stoke fear of immigrants by offering a brutal description of a case involving an undocumented immigrant who was included in a jobs program while Kamala Harris was the top prosecutor in San Francisco.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb82a202-4fac-4b59-9e32-dc5094e1a70b">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb82a202-4fac-4b59-9e32-dc5094e1a70b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President-elect Joseph R. Biden Jr. will take office in January with a weak economy weighed down by the coronavirus pandemic, millions of Americans still unemployed and businesses struggling and closing as winter bears down.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-19a7fb6b-a5ad-4f65-8d9c-b053a6ce8ab9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4b06f805-a6f6-4cda-9908-3f8ddd3a0432"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6c995819-c171-430e-a414-f6167b134557"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-94d58c04-d925-44a3-9534-35b73b8dc25d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb82abb7-107e-4759-ac4b-f163399577bf">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb82abb7-107e-4759-ac4b-f163399577bf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Some deaths were not counted as part of prison virus tallies because hospitalized inmates were officially released from custody before they died.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-14927191-e041-48b1-8c30-a344ddfd6a40"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-33709db8-2f1b-4de8-b586-0d050bd917df"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a35fc68d-6dc6-41ea-b14f-29c326040498"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e0da17b5-0302-4e93-b0bf-c765cae9f535"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb84ec44-0b13-4f82-8cc4-340643647289">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb84ec44-0b13-4f82-8cc4-340643647289</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>There are currently no trials underway, making a vaccine unlikely before fall of 2021. And students are missing online school at alarming rates.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8e1f79e3-f439-4e23-a236-360f7482f967"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f054aa66-2374-4f42-8ea3-5d2fd3c51e19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb865764-9762-4d0f-81a3-b58f630168fd">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb865764-9762-4d0f-81a3-b58f630168fd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Senate unanimously approved a nonbinding resolution on Wednesday calling for Secretary of State Antony J. Blinken to designate Russia as a state sponsor of terrorism for actions in Chechnya, Georgia, Syria and Ukraine that resulted “in the deaths of countless innocent men, women and children.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-bc861102-55e0-4752-9370-ad6d58043db1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb868a64-536c-4ac6-b97f-72ab052e883f">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb868a64-536c-4ac6-b97f-72ab052e883f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The judge has set next January to begin jury selection in the long-awaited trial of five men accused of plotting the terrorist attacks. But big logistical challenges remain.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4bd6cfaa-ebec-415a-8c53-2870f770bfa7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb8e0740-9795-40ad-9124-2525b9e193d0">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb8e0740-9795-40ad-9124-2525b9e193d0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>At a rally in Michigan on Friday, President Trump repeated an extraordinary and unfounded claim that American doctors were profiteering from coronavirus deaths.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-60369502-b152-49d7-982e-93f0386300f3"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb9097c2-ac79-453c-9bd7-1ca40737f4ed">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb9097c2-ac79-453c-9bd7-1ca40737f4ed</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Speaker Nancy Pelosi on Friday took the unprecedented step of asking the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff about “available precautions” to prevent President Trump from initiating military action abroad or using his sole authority to launch nuclear weapons in the last days of his term.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5a3094b1-6bc7-47d7-8f53-c56fd8ed0c59"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb90a1b0-2644-42d4-a9b0-f7f9703a4230">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb90a1b0-2644-42d4-a9b0-f7f9703a4230</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Barred from Twitter and Facebook as Trump was, social media’s younger conspiracy theorists are moving to Twitch.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-887d1269-7020-4c8e-8dfc-eae7c464f3cb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb90ec9f-a18c-4048-9a44-76b0b60e1357">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb90ec9f-a18c-4048-9a44-76b0b60e1357</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After winning his G.O.P. Senate primary, Don Bolduc reversed himself on claims the 2020 election was stolen. His comments on a QAnon-aligned podcast were not so straightforward.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4bd1aa5-c807-421e-b8ae-1b3824d70300"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb960a5a-078f-4289-b90a-f726fa178c7b">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb960a5a-078f-4289-b90a-f726fa178c7b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The defeat in a House committee came as President Biden was scheduled to meet with two key moderate senators who have balked at the cost of the overall package.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-576a9017-d1c0-4a28-b730-97415c0f4ae4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb982abe-532c-4168-b20b-5be50d72f716">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb982abe-532c-4168-b20b-5be50d72f716</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Many Republicans are disregarding the deficit impact for the sprawling infrastructure bill, but intend to change course for looming battles on social spending and the debt ceiling.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4b06f805-a6f6-4cda-9908-3f8ddd3a0432"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-803bdb8f-8c3c-4210-80c9-22b0af3fd2ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-06"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb9a055b-ee55-4049-b20d-d921c7014c8c">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb9a055b-ee55-4049-b20d-d921c7014c8c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Representative Jahana Hayes, a former National Teacher of the Year, says that she has many concerns — and that parents need to make their voices heard.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eb9e6442-5a5a-406a-b991-222689914c0c">
		<rdfs:label>article-eb9e6442-5a5a-406a-b991-222689914c0c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In a Fox News interview, Mr. Trump also angrily revived grievances about the special counsel Robert S. Mueller III and promised a swift economic rebound.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fc2c2b47-32c2-43a0-8e5f-dd4e72335932"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eba3213d-6f79-4c4d-9511-520deabedca6">
		<rdfs:label>article-eba3213d-6f79-4c4d-9511-520deabedca6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Partial results for the caucuses were released, and the confusion continued to reverberate around the presidential race.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eba4d65c-0992-478d-aeb3-74714a4f47b6">
		<rdfs:label>article-eba4d65c-0992-478d-aeb3-74714a4f47b6</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With the $2 trillion economic stimulus just signed into law on Friday, Washington is already considering a fourth response package. In an exclusive interview, Speaker Nancy Pelosi detailed what she wants next.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-99c317df-85f6-43ae-a405-4e8c1bdcbc98"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-eba5e064-8e93-406c-afe4-7c0c5377f41c">
		<rdfs:label>article-eba5e064-8e93-406c-afe4-7c0c5377f41c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The vote, 92 to 6, could allow for final passage later this week, though an amendment process could be another roadblock.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-04-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-ebad058c-cc87-4cd9-bae8-63eea0c65d43">
		<rdfs:label>article-ebad058c-cc87-4cd9-bae8-63eea0c65d43</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In statehouse races, suburban voters’ disgust with President Trump failed to translate into a rebuke of other Republicans, ensuring the party’s grip on partisan mapmaking.</rdfs:comment>
