	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-ebea94dc-1017-4ef9-85f4-d4bcde78b30c">
		<rdfs:label>article-ebea94dc-1017-4ef9-85f4-d4bcde78b30c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Vice-presidential debates can often be afterthoughts in a presidential race. But with President Trump in the hospital, Mike Pence and Kamala Harris will now face an unusual amount of scrutiny, and a tricky balancing act.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ebf4f94d-a728-4327-b424-d347782b7b17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-ebed66a5-aaa0-4da1-80f4-e4ecb338c3fc">
		<rdfs:label>article-ebed66a5-aaa0-4da1-80f4-e4ecb338c3fc</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Ms. Duckworth, an Illinois senator who is Thai-American and lost both legs fighting in Iraq, has been the target of two nights of attacks from the Fox News host; some were amplified by President Trump.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-45f2da0f-ff11-4bf4-a433-0a1b35060358"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-07-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
