	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-ed3affca-8482-49cf-b5c8-1e431a9fb466">
		<rdfs:label>article-ed3affca-8482-49cf-b5c8-1e431a9fb466</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Her husband early voted days ago, but Mrs. Trump voted on Election Day at a community center about two miles north of Mar-a-Lago.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c27717ae-a4a7-43e2-a892-7d5659d97cf6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-ed3c565b-b144-4ed9-9d1c-e53b0154368a">
		<rdfs:label>article-ed3c565b-b144-4ed9-9d1c-e53b0154368a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>He’s making overly optimistic promises for the country, but new polling is promising for him.</rdfs:comment>
