		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-edebba26-3eb7-4fd2-a822-a72ff333be1d">
		<rdfs:label>article-edebba26-3eb7-4fd2-a822-a72ff333be1d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The panel recommended against blanket access to Pfizer boosters for those 16 and older, but urged offering them to those 65 and older and “at high risk,” a term that offers the White House some room to expand access.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f800cdb3-ad0c-4b7e-81cb-a52efab2aad2"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-18"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-edec2402-9956-4b77-8e49-79e71ac7425b">
		<rdfs:label>article-edec2402-9956-4b77-8e49-79e71ac7425b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Treasury Secretary Janet Yellen said the U.S. would support a global minimum tax, while top Democrats unveiled their own plan to raise taxes on multinational firms.</rdfs:comment>
