	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-efae7bd3-0c49-4414-bf95-afe8ede0d59d">
		<rdfs:label>article-efae7bd3-0c49-4414-bf95-afe8ede0d59d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As a fast-spreading new strain of the coronavirus swarms across the country, hospitals in Ohio running low on beds and staff recently took out a full-page newspaper advertisement pleading with unvaccinated Americans to finally get the shot. It read, simply: “Help.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4e4ac7a5-be1a-4937-b91e-66276e5f8dd9"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b0d8acac-ba33-4091-b922-0eb5b9ab904d"/>
