	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f0240671-e5a8-4074-9102-4ed54c7d4c72">
		<rdfs:label>article-f0240671-e5a8-4074-9102-4ed54c7d4c72</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The House progressive spoke about “demoralizing” congressional negotiations, how she was told to stay away from Virginia’s elections, and what it means to excite the Democratic base.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4504805-5b5f-41c7-b157-41ff04a342ad"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f02909f8-9342-41a8-ba9c-267c24ca088d">
		<rdfs:label>article-f02909f8-9342-41a8-ba9c-267c24ca088d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>For once, the government tried overheating the economy. For better and worse, it succeeded.</rdfs:comment>
