	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f393ece1-9118-4613-aa9d-d16ba95619cb">
		<rdfs:label>article-f393ece1-9118-4613-aa9d-d16ba95619cb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Pandemic, unemployment, wildfire — Lake Berryessa, Calif., has seen it all this year. A photo from the town that evoked the trauma of 2020 sped across the internet. Here, though, it was real life.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b0d8acac-ba33-4091-b922-0eb5b9ab904d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f3961bff-9780-4ef9-bb74-4c63a3bf06ba">
		<rdfs:label>article-f3961bff-9780-4ef9-bb74-4c63a3bf06ba</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Waterspouts usually occur in the region from August through October, when the water of the Great Lakes is near its warmest, meteorologists said.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a8e16e77-2252-4f28-a3a1-fbe3392ad214"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f39d8869-ade1-4c53-bc6e-1617765afa33">
		<rdfs:label>article-f39d8869-ade1-4c53-bc6e-1617765afa33</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Speaking with Justice Stephen Breyer by his side, Mr. Biden hailed his decades on the federal bench, including almost 28 years on the Supreme Court.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d9dd9624-a9f6-46b2-b101-110db9155c7d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f3a60c38-d723-4efe-9ba8-9bb1dd31ad8f">
		<rdfs:label>article-f3a60c38-d723-4efe-9ba8-9bb1dd31ad8f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President-elect Joseph R. Biden Jr. promised transgender and gender-nonconforming people in the United States and around the world that he would fight for their dignity and safety, signaling a stark shift in policy between the incoming administration and the Trump White House, which has worked to weaken protections.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dad1523a-f983-4f0f-af53-0061c7165e91"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f3a6bf51-2c59-4714-8f16-2bc752c8a304">
		<rdfs:label>article-f3a6bf51-2c59-4714-8f16-2bc752c8a304</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump’s congressional allies had hoped to give the vice president the power to reject electoral votes that were cast for Joseph R. Biden Jr.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f3a840aa-c3d6-4803-81c6-101a850316fb">
		<rdfs:label>article-f3a840aa-c3d6-4803-81c6-101a850316fb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The effort by congressional Republicans to deny the presidential results found an echo in the Pennsylvania legislature on Tuesday, when Republicans voted not to seat a Democratic lawmaker who was elected in November and to remove the lieutenant governor, also a Democrat, as the presiding officer of the State Senate.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c2e66850-f7bc-45ca-83ed-c0a1f8490a14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f3ac4590-8aca-4d6c-922c-eaed9847ae22">
		<rdfs:label>article-f3ac4590-8aca-4d6c-922c-eaed9847ae22</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Kyle Rittenhouse and Ahmaud Arbery cases raise intriguing legal questions about people who take the law into their own hands and then claim self-defense when someone dies.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e2a444d6-76b3-4fc5-9655-0178ae16f402"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f3adf2b1-7b5d-4cc1-a725-51da88bb7e49">
		<rdfs:label>article-f3adf2b1-7b5d-4cc1-a725-51da88bb7e49</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After a stroke in May, Lt. Gov. John Fetterman of Pennsylvania, the state’s Democratic Senate nominee, is slowly re-emerging in public. His first interview since then was with a Pittsburgh paper.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8eb0923f-854c-4241-9d79-040d1aeeb0c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-20"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f3b065ac-e292-4600-9e05-2de8d2132f48">
		<rdfs:label>article-f3b065ac-e292-4600-9e05-2de8d2132f48</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The state has same-day registration, and voters in one district will decide on a special election that overlaps a House primary.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-483ef2a6-c7cc-4f86-aade-006bc30f2e55"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a4d1965e-83d5-427c-92cb-8140b08c5176"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f3b1e2fb-2c9f-4517-b942-d99cb7fc7ac3">
		<rdfs:label>article-f3b1e2fb-2c9f-4517-b942-d99cb7fc7ac3</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Joseph R. Biden Jr. said Americans should “vote their heart,” but also sharpened his criticism of Ms. Reade’s claim. And he made appearances on Thursday with two women in the running to be his vice president.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8eb0923f-854c-4241-9d79-040d1aeeb0c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d3a2df06-dc48-4fab-a9d1-d1d12442e2e1"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f3b268d9-412c-428c-8ced-c5e5a6ffe362">
		<rdfs:label>article-f3b268d9-412c-428c-8ced-c5e5a6ffe362</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The department’s leaders declined to publish a memo describing Russian attempts to question Joseph R. Biden Jr.’s health, prompting new scrutiny of political influence at the department.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-03"/>
