	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f5cb7f4c-636d-4c16-8a28-1d13f24194a7">
		<rdfs:label>article-f5cb7f4c-636d-4c16-8a28-1d13f24194a7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In Rhode Island, health authorities agreed that it was time for “a new balance” in dealing with the coronavirus. In Los Angeles, local officials greeted the easing of mask restrictions with promises to resist. Boston’s mayor laid out benchmarks for a controlled shift in restrictions, while the top civic leader in Duluth, Minn., announced a clean break.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-204cd1d8-9d72-4785-968e-7d68ce7d17d7"/>
