	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f752ed57-bda6-4e14-bf86-ceee35fbe328">
		<rdfs:label>article-f752ed57-bda6-4e14-bf86-ceee35fbe328</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Republicans are fighting over who will take on Senator Maggie Hassan of New Hampshire. Rhode Island and Delaware are also voting. It’s the last primary night before November.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6fcc2118-4d59-415b-8f82-fd519f6b2d34"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f75b61d2-3b45-4d76-b167-a88a809f8276">
		<rdfs:label>article-f75b61d2-3b45-4d76-b167-a88a809f8276</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Gulf nation will also help process visas for thousands of people trying to flee the Taliban.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f4f38f08-6492-4112-8b82-52bd8aa6b34f"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-11-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f75ffdf6-bed5-474c-97a8-2c0350210f9d">
		<rdfs:label>article-f75ffdf6-bed5-474c-97a8-2c0350210f9d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Some experts, especially in the early days of the vaccination campaign, have expressed concern over the idea of paying people to get vaccinated, worrying that it could be perceived as out of step with messaging that vaccines bring enormous benefits on their own.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4b06f805-a6f6-4cda-9908-3f8ddd3a0432"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-07-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f760d38f-7db9-4111-bf9d-29a49fc9f63b">
		<rdfs:label>article-f760d38f-7db9-4111-bf9d-29a49fc9f63b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Two firefighters were injured and about 90,800 people ordered to evacuate near Irvine, Calif., the authorities said. An evacuation warning also went into effect for the area south of Diamond Bar in Los Angeles County.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-38612bef-d331-4b4e-8a11-2278ecc52a9a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-74fe9339-5cba-4d49-b38d-2ccc7bfafd17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d4cc4659-5037-4aab-b198-0a80a11fcdae"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7645652-e22f-46ea-bfe6-06b1ebefe601">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7645652-e22f-46ea-bfe6-06b1ebefe601</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The case was brought by shareholders of Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac, who said the law that created the agency was unconstitutional.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6c995819-c171-430e-a414-f6167b134557"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-947ed571-ad87-49fb-b59a-9372d166d3c7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d2647a35-d767-4ddd-a84d-456d7af5ed17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f767ef8a-c37f-4230-86d7-aa9d9cae4a20">
		<rdfs:label>article-f767ef8a-c37f-4230-86d7-aa9d9cae4a20</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>All eyes are on Pennsylvania, which both presidential campaigns seem to believe could determine the outcome of the race.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-577cfa39-5806-4396-ae24-cdf4ba406715"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7686af1-1989-44d5-942f-9f6bd4ff2e50">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7686af1-1989-44d5-942f-9f6bd4ff2e50</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Until this week, Mr. Parscale, the president’s campaign manager, was one of only three people whose Facebook and Instagram pages had been used by the campaign to display ads. The others were Donald Trump and Mike Pence.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f76bb8f6-815b-456b-807a-29d485492a4f">
		<rdfs:label>article-f76bb8f6-815b-456b-807a-29d485492a4f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Bill Gates, an election supervisor in Maricopa County, says the audit of votes in his state is based on the lie of election fraud, and is “tearing at the foundations of our democracy.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9c6cc67a-b3c2-45c5-af7a-92a423ab1249"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f76dde2b-5279-482d-ae3d-8decfa0e1692">
		<rdfs:label>article-f76dde2b-5279-482d-ae3d-8decfa0e1692</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Floridians are out and about and pandemic restrictions have been lifted. There’s just one problem: The virus never went away.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-120d1588-a290-47a3-9ce4-8cc42139a1ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f779c2ff-5a5f-4576-8447-32fd39abee2f">
		<rdfs:label>article-f779c2ff-5a5f-4576-8447-32fd39abee2f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump trampled decorum at Tuesday’s debate, interrupting Joe Biden and making little attempt to win over undecided voters. Mr. Biden hit back: “This is so unpresidential.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3488268a-8b17-411a-8185-6859abbab9a8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-4a606035-f311-493f-9272-00230e475b23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-09-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f77f32d2-310f-467b-80a8-04cb96e5ab35">
		<rdfs:label>article-f77f32d2-310f-467b-80a8-04cb96e5ab35</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Gen. Charles Q. Brown Jr., who recently released a video about his experience with racism in the military and in America, won unanimous confirmation.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-09"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f781afc5-90ea-4177-8c92-15d6870d9340">
		<rdfs:label>article-f781afc5-90ea-4177-8c92-15d6870d9340</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Republican National Committee says it will require candidates to pledge to not participate in debates run by the Commission on Presidential Debates. What would replace them, if anything, was unclear.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-13"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f782a5f2-4c8d-4e40-b58e-4df271db12a8">
		<rdfs:label>article-f782a5f2-4c8d-4e40-b58e-4df271db12a8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>ICE is boosting its operations in sanctuary cities to arrest and deport undocumented immigrants, conducting round-the-clock surveillance in addition to deploying elite tactical agents.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-6b3ae601-9711-45ef-834d-5ad66589d1a2"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7b7bb5a2-025b-4e18-80c1-9f8ac039593a"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f78c7b08-3f69-4840-8d84-46afcf559e9d">
		<rdfs:label>article-f78c7b08-3f69-4840-8d84-46afcf559e9d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Recent multiple-vehicle pileups amid this year’s brutal weather have underscored the dangers of driving in winter conditions. In 28 hours last week, from early Thursday to Friday morning, the Iowa State Patrol received calls for help at 195 crashes. In Texas, six people were killed and dozens were hospitalized on Thursday in a pileup that involved more than 100 vehicles on Interstate 35.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b17bf905-20cf-405c-bc54-7eaf6eed8574"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-16"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f78dfec5-3fdd-4cb9-bdd9-dd83bcaee4d1">
		<rdfs:label>article-f78dfec5-3fdd-4cb9-bdd9-dd83bcaee4d1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention said this week that while she was encouraged by the gains against the pandemic, Americans should remain vigilant to the threat of the virus around the world.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-cc485407-61fb-4f46-96a9-c260884f0314"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-e2ba983e-eb48-483d-afa1-e67b02e88f99"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7957848-aa15-4712-a822-83cd4a8ef5e8">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7957848-aa15-4712-a822-83cd4a8ef5e8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The $1.5 million ad buy focuses on when Mr. Fetterman brandished a shotgun to stop and detain an unarmed Black jogger in 2013.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8eb0923f-854c-4241-9d79-040d1aeeb0c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7974b4b-a61e-4c59-973f-4aad500439ab">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7974b4b-a61e-4c59-973f-4aad500439ab</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The races for governor are likely to be noisy and in some of the most competitive states, the outcome has implications far beyond the governor’s mansion.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a5fb0ba0-4965-4f76-8b52-d16ac9dac194"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f79a8370-d200-4c16-823f-13210b585259">
		<rdfs:label>article-f79a8370-d200-4c16-823f-13210b585259</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden’s remarks reflect the urgent concern in Washington and among Western allies that Russia may be searching for a pretext to unleash a battlefield nuclear weapon.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f79f5519-1c60-4669-aac5-22677475ebfe">
		<rdfs:label>article-f79f5519-1c60-4669-aac5-22677475ebfe</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Primary elections are being pushed back. The Olympics are officially in 2021. The election-year calendar seemed set in stone and now it is up in the air.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f33dc887-a9a6-4b4f-adce-fc81b6f27a0c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7a1c582-fb40-4bdb-b7ad-bef0f27e379b">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7a1c582-fb40-4bdb-b7ad-bef0f27e379b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Defense Secretary Mark T. Esper, who issued the warning after an American contractor was killed by an Iranian-supported militia, said, “The game has changed.”</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3bea54bd-f3ee-4712-b704-2739e55e376e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7a625b9-47f8-4589-baf7-d33b413bb921">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7a625b9-47f8-4589-baf7-d33b413bb921</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>With sheriffs vouching for them and a flood of ads proclaiming their support for the police, Democrats are shoring up their public safety bona fides. Still, some worry it’s too late.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8eb0923f-854c-4241-9d79-040d1aeeb0c0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c2e66850-f7bc-45ca-83ed-c0a1f8490a14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-11-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7a66eab-d77a-4b7c-91ab-7e600acbcef4">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7a66eab-d77a-4b7c-91ab-7e600acbcef4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>“Task forces and vice presidents don’t get to decide things,” said Tim Pawlenty, the former Minnesota governor.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-049fb7b6-9066-46e6-b432-7450b1cd6746"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-922ad7b9-e6de-456a-9bc2-69207748d175"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-05-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7a84754-d15b-4c10-8f7a-ee2546b3bdcf">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7a84754-d15b-4c10-8f7a-ee2546b3bdcf</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The days when presidential candidates would choose running mates who could deliver their home states are now long gone.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0b1c0734-81f6-4bd6-ab6e-2c3d3239bc31"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9c6cc67a-b3c2-45c5-af7a-92a423ab1249"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ebf4f94d-a728-4327-b424-d347782b7b17"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-11"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7a98c2e-6367-4785-92ec-80b6fa470916">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7a98c2e-6367-4785-92ec-80b6fa470916</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In a complaint unsealed on Friday, whistle-blowers working on President Trump’s wall said that contractors were illegally bringing in Mexican guards to protect construction sites.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7aaaf0f-d834-402d-9da6-a71b16cdc7e8">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7aaaf0f-d834-402d-9da6-a71b16cdc7e8</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Attorney General Merrick B. Garland held a virtual meeting with 35 state Supreme Court justices in an effort to encourage them to try to avert or delay evictions.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7479f929-0522-4f1f-a391-dcdb5f4e726c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-12"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7aabfc7-9a3e-4b89-8f6d-1e0072577986">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7aabfc7-9a3e-4b89-8f6d-1e0072577986</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Los Angeles, like other cities across the nation, is facing a rise in gun violence. And the police budget is growing.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-9a5389b6-c0ea-4275-8951-1523cfe86f87"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7ab6d03-1df6-4346-82be-3c7c4a0cde69">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7ab6d03-1df6-4346-82be-3c7c4a0cde69</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>But if you don’t want to flip the channels between Biden and Trump, join our live chat, where we’ll cover both town halls.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5298104c-81c8-4a22-af1d-23823869871b"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7acfc47-b31d-4ca6-8e6d-90e34d56ca34">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7acfc47-b31d-4ca6-8e6d-90e34d56ca34</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The front-runner was Susan Wright, who was endorsed by Donald J. Trump and is the widow of Representative Ron Wright, who died of Covid-19 in February.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ba1def2a-fecf-4911-9182-36727aa8deac"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-fd2d6ec4-4aa3-452f-8e17-99a953af7b67"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7af5c20-52ee-42b2-a9da-27103c5a5530">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7af5c20-52ee-42b2-a9da-27103c5a5530</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Gov. Gavin Newsom pledged that the state was “putting everything we have” on the ravaging wildfires, acknowledging that even that was not enough to blunt their spread.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-21"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7af9589-bee2-4b20-9725-bd79a9a0b1b4">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7af9589-bee2-4b20-9725-bd79a9a0b1b4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The panel demanded information from 14 people who were part of bogus slates of electors for President Donald J. Trump, digging deeper into an aspect of his efforts to overturn the 2020 election.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-90788841-2a13-4598-abd3-3b677caff4d4"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-01-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f7b049fa-e680-4499-a942-d5db28cf521a">
		<rdfs:label>article-f7b049fa-e680-4499-a942-d5db28cf521a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Democrats leading the investigation are seeking to determine whether the federal government has done enough to ensure that the substance is safe to use on humans.</rdfs:comment>
