		<rdfs:label>article-f7cc8726-a156-40bc-a7eb-b51c53fb6c8c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The country’s economy, like the nation’s politics, is queasily suspended between the Trump and Biden administrations — at a moment when the rampaging pandemic has prompted deep concerns over the strength, timing and even likelihood of a possible recovery next year.</rdfs:comment>
