	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9a10a3f-0eaa-4a09-b357-80bf2701761f">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9a10a3f-0eaa-4a09-b357-80bf2701761f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In 2005, Hurricane Rita leveled some coastal communities in southwest Louisiana, forcing changes to building codes and attitudes. As Laura approached, the region was ready.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-781f7c76-864b-4901-8b16-90c83d96e113"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d7a0b17f-e0aa-44c5-a995-e81e028fa879"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9a4338c-dcb1-4c52-8fc0-5b55aa40324c">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9a4338c-dcb1-4c52-8fc0-5b55aa40324c</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The congressman’s involvement underlined how far the former president was willing to go to overturn the election, and Democratic lawmakers have begun calling for investigations into those efforts.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd522e1c-57a0-49bc-9835-fae39d9d58a6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-01-24"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9aa4018-e780-485b-8006-f3387cc707ca">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9aa4018-e780-485b-8006-f3387cc707ca</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>PHOENIX — More than 150 supporters of President Trump, some of them armed, gathered outside the Maricopa County election office on Wednesday and chanted “Count the vote,” as officials did just that under the protection of sheriff’s deputies.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f7d54296-4f6d-4656-bd4e-ce98de1cb5ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9aff8f3-6c7b-423c-bf19-90f5d130438e">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9aff8f3-6c7b-423c-bf19-90f5d130438e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>“He’s being somewhat difficult,” Representative Jerrold Nadler, Democrat of New York and the Judiciary Committee chairman, said during a break midway through the session with Donald F. McGahn II, the former White House counsel.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-06-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9b47e16-fe27-41d4-808f-62b57c9dfa9b">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9b47e16-fe27-41d4-808f-62b57c9dfa9b</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>As he had done countless times in his career in public office, Joe Biden returned to the Wilmington suburbs from Washington on Friday — this time, as the commander in chief.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-7da4dfa6-58ba-4b1b-8d80-6c39df820022"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-02-07"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9bc8b9a-8b1f-40bb-aa23-783bdcbfae47">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9bc8b9a-8b1f-40bb-aa23-783bdcbfae47</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>RAMSTEIN AIR BASE, Germany — Emphasizing that the United States was prepared to support Ukraine “for the long haul,” Defense Secretary Lloyd J. Austin III said Thursday that Washington will send an additional $675 million in military supplies to Ukraine, including air-launched missiles designed to destroy enemy radars.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-524922c4-c335-4218-b145-d4752931be34"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-08"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9bdc19e-da35-487f-a7ea-61f217970861">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9bdc19e-da35-487f-a7ea-61f217970861</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The governor hailed the factory as an economic boon that would put Georgia at the vanguard of the green economy. Not everyone liked the idea.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-80938ccc-3865-4478-bf4f-7759ead7221e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9c0f02f-5e2f-4caa-95e3-0ac68006ed2e">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9c0f02f-5e2f-4caa-95e3-0ac68006ed2e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The Eastern European countries had sought to buy Pegasus, spyware made by an Israeli firm, to carry out intelligence operations against Russia, according to people with knowledge of the discussions.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-43071aec-9461-4281-991c-f7a69b5d74cf"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-92d6a2c3-4676-4b0a-b692-bac80f669045"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-03-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9c16b51-f104-4b9d-be15-a1a7fb655ae7">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9c16b51-f104-4b9d-be15-a1a7fb655ae7</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Some are certain the election was fraudulent. Others aren’t so sure. What becomes of their skepticism has important implications for American democracy.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-81f0af94-b9cf-4dcb-8ae5-91c423d251ff"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-12-14"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9c58c69-1555-4d3d-ac9d-4cd4ffe6cd33">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9c58c69-1555-4d3d-ac9d-4cd4ffe6cd33</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Democrats and Republicans managed to come together to update the archaic Electoral Count Act after they recognized it could again be abused to subvert the presidential vote.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0e84c75e-7bc1-4744-83f1-7496fcf4721d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9c69b48-bd38-4d57-b511-746071927eb3">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9c69b48-bd38-4d57-b511-746071927eb3</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>At a Munich security conference, the president of France urged Europe to create its own policy toward Russia.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-79c2c4e0-5cef-490b-bc75-d2f869534716"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-02-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9c883e0-e62a-4cc2-96b0-9a1ecc6425fe">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9c883e0-e62a-4cc2-96b0-9a1ecc6425fe</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The looming vote on creating a commission to investigate the Jan. 6 Capitol assault could reignite a clash over the Senate blocking tactic. Activists worry that time is short for a bid to eliminate it.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-0e84c75e-7bc1-4744-83f1-7496fcf4721d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-05-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9c8a48c-63ec-42ed-98fe-f61c62c88cac">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9c8a48c-63ec-42ed-98fe-f61c62c88cac</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The conspiracy theorist filed for bankruptcy for Infowars’ parent company, but lawyers for parents of the school shooting victims called it a ploy to shield him from paying damages.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d33d714f-8a3d-4efb-bf05-335e32075194"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-08-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9ca4ece-d83d-4c35-8226-e7973da2bca1">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9ca4ece-d83d-4c35-8226-e7973da2bca1</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Biden said the United States and Britain would help Australia to deploy nuclear-powered submarines, adding to the Western presence in the region.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-558cc815-e7e6-47a5-bd90-ac5a453042ba"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-b6772619-716a-4e22-b807-36e658c83435"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-09-15"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9cf9c91-9b0c-45a5-bac5-b9655d6544bd">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9cf9c91-9b0c-45a5-bac5-b9655d6544bd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The episode highlights how murky the new guidelines are, particularly for a White House that has pledged to embrace progressive positions.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd42dd7e-7a0d-4a74-908e-252de023edfb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-03-19"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9d4fb64-3e97-4ac8-915c-d0cc732992b3">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9d4fb64-3e97-4ac8-915c-d0cc732992b3</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The nominee, Phillip A. Washington, who has yet to receive a confirmation hearing, has drawn scrutiny over his aviation experience and his involvement in a corruption inquiry.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-bdbbb05b-6fa3-49c7-aa85-71057abb04d2"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-12-26"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9d7505a-ca7d-4221-b020-2a986a6e02de">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9d7505a-ca7d-4221-b020-2a986a6e02de</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Weeks before the midterm elections, the House minority leader presented a platform of neutral-sounding ideas that he said would guide a Republican majority. The hard right was there to cheer him on.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-a2860122-d5d8-4996-a4a4-bc29b03dbcd0"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-09-23"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9da0192-3e51-4c2b-8340-3915c2a7bade">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9da0192-3e51-4c2b-8340-3915c2a7bade</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Alex Padilla, California’s secretary of state, has emerged as the front-runner to succeed Kamala Harris. But Gov. Gavin Newsom appears to be in no rush to make his choice.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-204cd1d8-9d72-4785-968e-7d68ce7d17d7"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-3488268a-8b17-411a-8185-6859abbab9a8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-29"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9e04bda-eb2b-4a51-b14d-80ebc7d56ff2">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9e04bda-eb2b-4a51-b14d-80ebc7d56ff2</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>The story of Cassidy Hutchinson, who became the first Trump White House aide to testify publicly in the Jan. 6 inquiry, showed the outsize influence of young aides in the nation’s capital.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c67a9047-7b94-4e45-aaa9-c820c2b967de"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-07-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9e6d748-f1ab-4ecd-953d-986c9613138a">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9e6d748-f1ab-4ecd-953d-986c9613138a</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>An Islamic State affiliate that is a sworn enemy of both the Taliban and the United States threatens a large-scale attack against the mission at the airport.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5a3094b1-6bc7-47d7-8f53-c56fd8ed0c59"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2021-08-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9e776cd-ba73-4811-bc8b-30323df366b4">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9e776cd-ba73-4811-bc8b-30323df366b4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Attorneys general have long sought to stop a proposed expansion of the authority of the department’s independent inspector general.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-010e943a-d70f-4929-8957-2d55ddf6a675"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-559d35dd-0818-4064-bd03-731b6c32d473"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-dd522e1c-57a0-49bc-9835-fae39d9d58a6"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-06-25"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9e7fa60-a6ae-4739-993f-611958dcc998">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9e7fa60-a6ae-4739-993f-611958dcc998</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>After the Democratic primary campaign came to an abrupt halt in late March as the coronavirus swept through the nation, the Democrats and Republicans have looked to the conventions as their candidates’ biggest stage.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-887d1269-7020-4c8e-8dfc-eae7c464f3cb"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-08-22"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9f677cd-1168-4156-a319-e33de7b324f0">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9f677cd-1168-4156-a319-e33de7b324f0</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump’s bombshell announcement early Friday morning that he and the first lady had tested positive for the coronavirus has set off a frenzy in the White House and beyond as politicians and operatives who have interacted with Mr. Trump in recent days have raced to get their own tests and, in some cases, report the results.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-5d63bd62-89ce-492f-b9ae-e5b2f12971c8"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8a614115-3578-4c7f-b70a-6cdd9b0a4f3d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-02"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9f72376-4e8c-4df2-8f0c-bb3a629fd34d">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9f72376-4e8c-4df2-8f0c-bb3a629fd34d</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Countries aren’t doing nearly enough to protect against the disasters to come as the planet keeps heating up, a major new scientific report concludes.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-d8148593-227b-4889-ae70-592b440737ae"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-f47e8c73-b108-4497-8696-b024a69f280e"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-02-28"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9f7d773-d835-412e-9df5-fdb6dd8dcecd">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9f7d773-d835-412e-9df5-fdb6dd8dcecd</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Election officials opened 21 satellite voting sites on Monday in Detroit, where election headquarters and city hall have been open for absentee voting for the past 10 days. The new sites, set up across the city, allow voters to pick up or drop off absentee ballots.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-44926325-5c4f-4e18-89e5-b1470d62842c"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-10-05"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9f8cbfb-0248-447e-b277-978c5652a627">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9f8cbfb-0248-447e-b277-978c5652a627</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>In the absence of federal privacy legislation, the state’s law is considered among the nation’s strongest.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8645bedc-c642-4ef0-8efb-ff731885cf27"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-05-30"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-f9ff262f-bbc2-4aa4-b800-8393dd24f091">
		<rdfs:label>article-f9ff262f-bbc2-4aa4-b800-8393dd24f091</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Sarah McBride won her State Senate race in Delaware on Tuesday, making her the first openly transgender person to be elected to that position nationwide. When she is sworn in, she will become the nation’s highest-ranking transgender elected official.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-8a614115-3578-4c7f-b70a-6cdd9b0a4f3d"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-04"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-fa02cb4c-da77-435e-b4a0-e9a1e433f045">
		<rdfs:label>article-fa02cb4c-da77-435e-b4a0-e9a1e433f045</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>President Trump’s iron grip on his party has inspired love for him among some Republican lawmakers and fear among others. Neither group will tell him it is time to concede his loss —  or at the very least, to stop spreading claims about the integrity of the nation’s elections that are contrary to considerable evidence.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-ce324a4b-e256-4143-b6b8-1dde4bc956af"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-11-10"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-fa04158d-b51f-4a68-a626-c44b9e84d4eb">
		<rdfs:label>article-fa04158d-b51f-4a68-a626-c44b9e84d4eb</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Aerial imagery taken before and after Hurricane Ian made landfall revealed the extent of the damage to parts of Florida’s Gulf Coast.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-c91ef78d-fe3b-4dd3-966c-66ab802c08ca"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2022-10-01"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-fa05a229-5259-424e-8429-78a1ad52975f">
		<rdfs:label>article-fa05a229-5259-424e-8429-78a1ad52975f</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>At stake in the lawsuit is the single biggest effort by the United States to fight the climate crisis.</rdfs:comment>
