	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-fb5c7a9d-6aeb-4837-8b67-8abf03c9a7a4">
		<rdfs:label>article-fb5c7a9d-6aeb-4837-8b67-8abf03c9a7a4</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Are the wealthy a liability in 2020? Or will they help get him elected?</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-730e51bd-9f9d-4526-a335-84c6ed305d85"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-01-03"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublisher rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;NewYorkTimes"/>
	</PoliticalJournalism:Article>
	
	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-fb5ccc16-8fbf-4caf-ad1c-017a19440bb9">
		<rdfs:label>article-fb5ccc16-8fbf-4caf-ad1c-017a19440bb9</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>But you could still face high medical bills. Experts advise consumers to not write a check immediately because more aid may be coming.</rdfs:comment>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasAuthor rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;author-025a9bc6-15b8-40f2-8470-85a30f6b6e94"/>
		<PoliticalJournalism:hasPublishDate rdf:resource="&PoliticalJournalism;date-2020-03-19"/>
