	<PoliticalJournalism:Article rdf:about="&PoliticalJournalism;article-fe226af5-b81b-4431-a8f2-4551d774db6e">
		<rdfs:label>article-fe226af5-b81b-4431-a8f2-4551d774db6e</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:comment>Readers of newspapers like The Miami Herald and The Kansas City Star will probably have to choose a presidential candidate in November without the help of their local editorial boards, according to a memo circulated by the company that owns the newspapers, McClatchy.</rdfs:comment>
